1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,200
Stop thinking for a moment.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:09,920
Whatever your mind is working on, it will
still be there tomorrow, and it will be easier

3
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,860
then.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:18,040
For the next few hours there's nothing to
follow and nothing to remember — just the Psalms

5
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:20,160
and Proverbs, read slowly.

6
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,120
Close your eyes.

7
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:28,340
If your mind is somewhere heavy tonight, put it
in the comments — this is a good place

8
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:29,360
to be prayed for.

9
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,500
Subscribe if you'd like the next reading
to find you.

10
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,400
Lord, my mind is still going, and it has
been going for hours.

11
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:45,440
It keeps turning the same few things over,
as if turning them once more will finally

12
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:46,380
settle them.

13
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:48,020
It won't.

14
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,280
I know that by now, and I still can't
stop.

15
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:54,700
I'm not asking you to answer any of it
tonight.

16
00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:00,160
Most of it isn't a question, it's just
noise wearing the shape of a question.

17
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:07,200
What I'm asking is narrower: let something truer
than my own thinking be the last thing

18
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:08,140
in my ears.

19
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:12,200
Let these psalms and proverbs run past me
slowly.

20
00:01:13,380 --> 00:01:14,720
I don't need to follow them.

21
00:01:15,320 --> 00:01:17,360
I don't need to remember them in the
morning.

22
00:01:18,320 --> 00:01:19,740
You made the night for sleeping.

23
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:24,060
You didn't make me to keep watch over
things you're already watching.

24
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:27,020
So take the shift from me now.

25
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:31,560
Let my thoughts slow to your pace instead
of their own.

26
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:38,100
Give me sleep, and give it to the people
who are lying awake tonight the way I am.

27
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:39,380
Amen.

28
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:41,440
Psalm ninety.

29
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:44,980
Lord, you have been our dwelling place for
all generations.

30
00:01:46,340 --> 00:01:52,340
Before the mountains were born, before you had
formed the earth and the world, even from

31
00:01:52,380 --> 00:01:55,660
everlasting to everlasting, you are God.

32
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:01,780
You turn man to destruction, saying,
“Return, you children of men.”

33
00:02:02,300 --> 00:02:08,040
For a thousand years in your sight are just
like yesterday when it is past, like a watch

34
00:02:08,080 --> 00:02:08,980
in the night.

35
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:11,700
You sweep them away as they sleep.

36
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:14,740
In the morning they sprout like new grass.

37
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:17,920
In the morning it sprouts and springs up.

38
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,880
By evening, it is withered and dry.

39
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:23,800
For we are consumed in your anger.

40
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,900
We are troubled in your wrath.

41
00:02:26,334 --> 00:02:31,933
You have set our iniquities before you, our
secret sins in the light of your presence.

42
00:02:33,134 --> 00:02:36,234
For all our days have passed away in your
wrath.

43
00:02:37,354 --> 00:02:40,033
We bring our years to an end as a sigh.

44
00:02:40,533 --> 00:02:47,114
The days of our years are seventy, or
even by reason of strength eighty years; yet their

45
00:02:47,153 --> 00:02:52,914
pride is but labour and sorrow, for it
passes quickly, and we fly away.

46
00:02:53,794 --> 00:02:59,593
Who knows the power of your anger, your wrath
according to the fear that is due to you?

47
00:02:59,974 --> 00:03:04,153
So teach us to count our days, that we may
gain a heart of wisdom.

48
00:03:05,234 --> 00:03:06,134
Relent, LORD!

49
00:03:06,734 --> 00:03:07,634
How long?

50
00:03:08,054 --> 00:03:09,633
Have compassion on your servants!

51
00:03:10,493 --> 00:03:15,894
Satisfy us in the morning with your loving
kindness, that we may rejoice and be glad

52
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:16,894
all our days.

53
00:03:17,894 --> 00:03:24,093
Make us glad for as many days as you have
afflicted us, for as many years as we have

54
00:03:24,133 --> 00:03:25,033
seen evil.

55
00:03:25,153 --> 00:03:29,394
Let your work appear to your servants,
your glory to their children.

56
00:03:30,093 --> 00:03:32,974
Let the favour of the Lord our God be on
us.

57
00:03:33,854 --> 00:03:36,474
Establish the work of our hands for us.

58
00:03:37,773 --> 00:03:40,514
Yes, establish the work of our hands.

59
00:03:41,873 --> 00:03:44,514
Psalm ninety-one.

60
00:03:44,554 --> 00:03:50,554
He who dwells in the secret place of the
Most High will rest in the shadow of the Almighty.

61
00:03:51,054 --> 00:03:57,593
I will say of the LORD, “He is my refuge
and my fortress; my God, in whom I

62
00:03:57,633 --> 00:03:58,533
trust.”

63
00:03:58,993 --> 00:04:04,633
For he will deliver you from the snare
of the fowler, and from the deadly pestilence.

64
00:04:05,554 --> 00:04:07,394
He will cover you with his feathers.

65
00:04:08,054 --> 00:04:09,813
Under his wings you will take refuge.

66
00:04:11,133 --> 00:04:14,133
His faithfulness is your shield and
rampart.

67
00:04:14,734 --> 00:04:21,833
You shall not be afraid of the terror by
night, nor of the arrow that flies by day, nor

68
00:04:21,873 --> 00:04:28,453
of the pestilence that walks in darkness,
nor of the destruction that wastes at noonday.

69
00:04:28,494 --> 00:04:34,833
A thousand may fall at your side, and ten
thousand at your right hand; but it will not

70
00:04:34,874 --> 00:04:35,793
come near you.

71
00:04:35,833 --> 00:04:40,794
You will only look with your eyes, and see
the recompense of the wicked.

72
00:04:41,953 --> 00:04:48,053
Because you have made the LORD your refuge,
and the Most High your dwelling place, no

73
00:04:48,093 --> 00:04:53,134
evil shall happen to you, neither shall
any plague come near your dwelling.

74
00:04:53,555 --> 00:04:58,595
For he will put his angels in charge of
you, to guard you in all your ways.

75
00:04:59,395 --> 00:05:04,975
They will bear you up in their hands, so
that you won’t dash your foot against a stone.

76
00:05:05,915 --> 00:05:08,335
You will tread on the lion and cobra.

77
00:05:08,855 --> 00:05:12,315
You will trample the young lion and the
serpent underfoot.

78
00:05:12,355 --> 00:05:17,415
“Because he has set his love on me,
therefore I will deliver him.

79
00:05:17,935 --> 00:05:21,955
I will set him on high, because he has
known my name.

80
00:05:22,595 --> 00:05:26,055
He will call on me, and I will answer him.

81
00:05:26,935 --> 00:05:28,455
I will be with him in trouble.

82
00:05:29,235 --> 00:05:31,455
I will deliver him, and honour him.

83
00:05:31,755 --> 00:05:36,115
I will satisfy him with long life, and
show him my salvation.”

84
00:05:36,975 --> 00:05:39,095
Psalm ninety-two.

85
00:05:39,135 --> 00:05:45,015
It is a good thing to give thanks to
the LORD, to sing praises to your name, Most High,

86
00:05:45,675 --> 00:05:51,515
to proclaim your loving kindness in the
morning, and your faithfulness every night, with

87
00:05:51,555 --> 00:05:56,115
the ten-stringed lute, with the harp, and
with the melody of the lyre.

88
00:05:56,675 --> 00:05:59,875
For you, LORD, have made me glad through
your work.

89
00:06:00,595 --> 00:06:03,355
I will triumph in the works of your hands.

90
00:06:04,415 --> 00:06:06,075
How great are your works, LORD!

91
00:06:07,015 --> 00:06:08,455
Your thoughts are very deep.

92
00:06:09,135 --> 00:06:15,395
A senseless man doesn’t know, neither does
a fool understand this: though the wicked

93
00:06:15,435 --> 00:06:21,515
spring up as the grass, and all
the evildoers flourish, they will be destroyed forever.

94
00:06:22,635 --> 00:06:25,575
But you, LORD, are on high forever more.

95
00:06:26,095 --> 00:06:30,955
For behold, your enemies, LORD, for
behold, your enemies shall perish.

96
00:06:31,675 --> 00:06:33,555
All the evildoers will be scattered.

97
00:06:34,255 --> 00:06:38,095
But you have exalted my horn like that of
the wild ox.

98
00:06:39,075 --> 00:06:40,935
I am anointed with fresh oil.

99
00:06:41,935 --> 00:06:44,095
My eye has also seen my enemies.

100
00:06:45,055 --> 00:06:48,955
My ears have heard of the wicked enemies
who rise up against me.

101
00:06:49,855 --> 00:06:52,595
The righteous shall flourish like the palm
tree.

102
00:06:53,235 --> 00:06:55,175
He will grow like a cedar in Lebanon.

103
00:06:56,155 --> 00:06:58,215
They are planted in the LORD’s house.

104
00:06:58,995 --> 00:07:00,855
They will flourish in our God’s courts.

105
00:07:01,595 --> 00:07:04,275
They will still produce fruit in old age.

106
00:07:05,115 --> 00:07:09,435
They will be full of sap and green, to
show that the LORD is upright.

107
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:13,735
He is my rock, and there is no
unrighteousness in him.

108
00:07:14,515 --> 00:07:16,815
Psalm ninety-three.

109
00:07:16,855 --> 00:07:17,975
The LORD reigns!

110
00:07:18,555 --> 00:07:19,955
He is clothed with majesty!

111
00:07:20,695 --> 00:07:22,395
The LORD is armed with strength.

112
00:07:23,455 --> 00:07:25,175
The world also is established.

113
00:07:26,215 --> 00:07:27,235
It can’t be moved.

114
00:07:28,135 --> 00:07:30,535
Your throne is established from long ago.

115
00:07:31,155 --> 00:07:32,495
You are from everlasting.

116
00:07:34,075 --> 00:07:38,495
The floods have lifted up, LORD, the
floods have lifted up their voice.

117
00:07:39,455 --> 00:07:40,935
The floods lift up their waves.

118
00:07:40,975 --> 00:07:47,695
Above the voices of many waters, the
mighty breakers of the sea, The LORD

119
00:07:47,735 --> 00:07:49,015
on high is mighty.

120
00:07:49,815 --> 00:07:51,435
Your statutes stand firm.

121
00:07:52,355 --> 00:07:56,235
Holiness adorns your house, LORD, forever
more.

122
00:07:56,275 --> 00:07:58,295
Psalm ninety-four.

123
00:07:58,335 --> 00:08:04,935
LORD, you God to whom vengeance belongs,
you God to whom vengeance belongs, shine

124
00:08:04,975 --> 00:08:05,875
out.

125
00:08:05,995 --> 00:08:08,055
Rise up, you judge of the earth.

126
00:08:08,835 --> 00:08:10,655
Pay back the proud what they deserve.

127
00:08:10,695 --> 00:08:15,815
LORD, how long will the wicked, how long
will the wicked triumph?

128
00:08:16,795 --> 00:08:18,415
They pour out arrogant words.

129
00:08:19,215 --> 00:08:20,655
All the evildoers boast.

130
00:08:21,655 --> 00:08:25,475
They break your people in pieces, LORD,
and afflict your heritage.

131
00:08:26,275 --> 00:08:29,895
They kill the widow and the alien, and
murder the fatherless.

132
00:08:30,755 --> 00:08:36,055
They say, “The LORD will not see, neither
will Jacob’s God consider.”

133
00:08:37,115 --> 00:08:42,955
Consider, you senseless amongst the
people; you fools, when will you be wise?

134
00:08:43,515 --> 00:08:46,235
He who implanted the ear, won’t he hear?

135
00:08:46,855 --> 00:08:49,735
He who formed the eye, won’t he see?

136
00:08:50,515 --> 00:08:53,255
He who disciplines the nations, won’t he
punish?

137
00:08:54,315 --> 00:08:56,255
He who teaches man knows.

138
00:08:57,095 --> 00:09:00,515
The LORD knows the thoughts of man, that
they are futile.

139
00:09:01,135 --> 00:09:06,535
Blessed is the man whom you discipline, LORD,
and teach out of your law, that you may

140
00:09:06,575 --> 00:09:11,435
give him rest from the days of adversity,
until the pit is dug for the wicked.

141
00:09:12,055 --> 00:09:16,795
For the LORD won’t reject his people,
neither will he forsake his inheritance.

142
00:09:18,095 --> 00:09:20,035
For judgement will return to
righteousness.

143
00:09:21,315 --> 00:09:23,595
All the upright in heart shall follow it.

144
00:09:24,175 --> 00:09:26,795
Who will rise up for me against the
wicked?

145
00:09:27,495 --> 00:09:31,055
Who will stand up for me against the
evildoers?

146
00:09:31,095 --> 00:09:35,855
Unless the LORD had been my help, my soul
would have soon lived in silence.

147
00:09:37,015 --> 00:09:39,055
When I said, “My foot is slipping!”

148
00:09:40,175 --> 00:09:42,375
Your loving kindness, LORD, held me up.

149
00:09:42,415 --> 00:09:47,795
In the multitude of my thoughts within me,
your comforts delight my soul.

150
00:09:48,145 --> 00:09:53,445
Shall the throne of wickedness have
fellowship with you, which brings about mischief

151
00:09:53,485 --> 00:09:54,605
by statute?

152
00:09:55,325 --> 00:10:01,185
They gather themselves together against the soul
of the righteous, and condemn the innocent

153
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:02,125
blood.

154
00:10:02,585 --> 00:10:07,945
But the LORD has been my high tower, my
God, the rock of my refuge.

155
00:10:08,825 --> 00:10:14,505
He has brought on them their own iniquity,
and will cut them off in their own wickedness.

156
00:10:15,145 --> 00:10:18,025
The LORD, our God, will cut them off.

157
00:10:39,145 --> 00:10:40,622
Psalm ninety-five.

158
00:10:40,662 --> 00:10:41,440
Oh come, let’s sing to the LORD.

159
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,493
Let’s shout aloud to the rock of our
salvation!

160
00:10:42,533 --> 00:10:43,311
Let’s come before his presence with
thanksgiving.

161
00:10:43,351 --> 00:10:43,896
Let’s extol him with songs!

162
00:10:43,936 --> 00:10:45,416
For the LORD is a great God, a great King
above all gods.

163
00:10:45,456 --> 00:10:46,585
In his hand are the deep places of the
earth.

164
00:10:46,625 --> 00:10:47,520
The heights of the mountains are also his.

165
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,525
The sea is his, and he made it.

166
00:10:48,825 --> 00:10:50,685
His hands formed the dry land.

167
00:10:50,725 --> 00:10:54,045
Oh come, let’s worship and bow down.

168
00:10:54,665 --> 00:10:58,405
Let’s kneel before the LORD, our Maker,
for he is our God.

169
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:03,085
We are the people of his pasture, and the
sheep in his care.

170
00:11:04,065 --> 00:11:06,985
Today, oh that you would hear his voice!

171
00:11:07,745 --> 00:11:14,225
Don’t harden your heart, as at Meribah, as
in the day of Massah in the wilderness, when

172
00:11:14,265 --> 00:11:18,245
your fathers tempted me, tested me, and
saw my work.

173
00:11:18,285 --> 00:11:24,825
Forty long years I was grieved with that
generation, and said, “They

174
00:11:24,865 --> 00:11:26,825
are a people who err in their heart.

175
00:11:27,625 --> 00:11:29,165
They have not known my ways.”

176
00:11:29,945 --> 00:11:34,045
Therefore I swore in my wrath, “They won’t
enter into my rest.”

177
00:11:35,285 --> 00:11:37,805
Psalm ninety-six.

178
00:11:37,845 --> 00:11:39,325
Sing to the LORD a new song!

179
00:11:39,945 --> 00:11:42,045
Sing to the LORD, all the earth.

180
00:11:42,705 --> 00:11:43,705
Sing to the LORD!

181
00:11:44,205 --> 00:11:45,185
Bless his name!

182
00:11:45,885 --> 00:11:48,285
Proclaim his salvation from day to day!

183
00:11:48,845 --> 00:11:53,945
Declare his glory amongst the nations, his
marvellous works amongst all the peoples.

184
00:11:54,825 --> 00:11:57,645
For the LORD is great, and greatly to be
praised!

185
00:11:58,565 --> 00:12:00,445
He is to be feared above all gods.

186
00:12:01,125 --> 00:12:05,305
For all the gods of the peoples are idols,
but the LORD made the heavens.

187
00:12:05,345 --> 00:12:08,065
Honour and majesty are before him.

188
00:12:08,665 --> 00:12:11,025
Strength and beauty are in his sanctuary.

189
00:12:12,265 --> 00:12:18,105
Ascribe to the LORD, you families of
nations, ascribe to the LORD glory and strength.

190
00:12:18,566 --> 00:12:21,966
Ascribe to the LORD the glory due to his
name.

191
00:12:22,986 --> 00:12:25,686
Bring an offering, and come into his
courts.

192
00:12:26,866 --> 00:12:28,846
Worship the LORD in holy array.

193
00:12:29,946 --> 00:12:32,166
Tremble before him, all the earth.

194
00:12:33,046 --> 00:12:36,586
Say amongst the nations, “The LORD
reigns.”

195
00:12:36,846 --> 00:12:39,046
The world is also established.

196
00:12:39,866 --> 00:12:40,926
It can’t be moved.

197
00:12:41,706 --> 00:12:43,966
He will judge the peoples with equity.

198
00:12:44,726 --> 00:12:47,986
Let the heavens be glad, and let the earth
rejoice.

199
00:12:49,106 --> 00:12:51,626
Let the sea roar, and its fullness!

200
00:12:52,226 --> 00:12:56,266
Let the field and all that is in it exult!

201
00:12:56,306 --> 00:13:02,826
Then all the trees of the woods shall sing
for joy before the LORD; for he comes, for

202
00:13:02,866 --> 00:13:04,506
he comes to judge the earth.

203
00:13:05,086 --> 00:13:09,486
He will judge the world with
righteousness, the peoples with his truth.

204
00:13:10,506 --> 00:13:12,806
Psalm ninety-seven.

205
00:13:12,846 --> 00:13:14,006
The LORD reigns!

206
00:13:14,406 --> 00:13:15,426
Let the earth rejoice!

207
00:13:16,406 --> 00:13:18,566
Let the multitude of islands be glad!

208
00:13:19,106 --> 00:13:21,266
Clouds and darkness are around him.

209
00:13:22,066 --> 00:13:25,366
Righteousness and justice are the
foundation of his throne.

210
00:13:26,166 --> 00:13:31,186
A fire goes before him, and burns up his
adversaries on every side.

211
00:13:32,186 --> 00:13:34,046
His lightning lights up the world.

212
00:13:34,926 --> 00:13:36,886
The earth sees, and trembles.

213
00:13:37,706 --> 00:13:43,246
The mountains melt like wax at the presence
of the LORD, at the presence of the Lord

214
00:13:43,286 --> 00:13:44,266
of the whole earth.

215
00:13:45,106 --> 00:13:47,146
The heavens declare his righteousness.

216
00:13:47,866 --> 00:13:49,766
All the peoples have seen his glory.

217
00:13:50,706 --> 00:13:56,386
Let all them be shamed who serve engraved
images, who boast in their idols.

218
00:13:57,266 --> 00:13:59,086
Worship him, all you gods!

219
00:14:00,126 --> 00:14:02,066
Zion heard and was glad.

220
00:14:02,966 --> 00:14:06,766
The daughters of Judah rejoiced because of
your judgements, LORD.

221
00:14:07,586 --> 00:14:10,806
For you, LORD, are most high above all the
earth.

222
00:14:11,426 --> 00:14:13,926
You are exalted far above all gods.

223
00:14:14,926 --> 00:14:17,566
You who love the LORD, hate evil!

224
00:14:18,466 --> 00:14:20,746
He preserves the souls of his saints.

225
00:14:21,466 --> 00:14:24,046
He delivers them out of the hand of the
wicked.

226
00:14:24,526 --> 00:14:28,926
Light is sown for the righteous, and
gladness for the upright in heart.

227
00:14:29,946 --> 00:14:32,526
Be glad in the LORD, you righteous people!

228
00:14:33,146 --> 00:14:35,026
Give thanks to his holy Name.

229
00:14:36,046 --> 00:14:38,166
Psalm ninety-eight.

230
00:14:38,206 --> 00:14:42,706
Sing to the LORD a new song, for he has
done marvellous things!

231
00:14:43,766 --> 00:14:48,046
His right hand and his holy arm have
worked salvation for him.

232
00:14:48,086 --> 00:14:51,126
The LORD has made known his salvation.

233
00:14:51,665 --> 00:14:55,325
He has openly shown his righteousness in
the sight of the nations.

234
00:14:56,485 --> 00:15:01,145
He has remembered his loving kindness and
his faithfulness towards the house of Israel.

235
00:15:02,385 --> 00:15:05,925
All the ends of the earth have seen the
salvation of our God.

236
00:15:07,005 --> 00:15:10,285
Make a joyful noise to the LORD, all the
earth!

237
00:15:10,965 --> 00:15:14,325
Burst out and sing for joy, yes, sing
praises!

238
00:15:14,365 --> 00:15:19,505
Sing praises to the LORD with the harp,
with the harp and the voice of melody.

239
00:15:19,545 --> 00:15:26,265
With trumpets and sound of the ram’s horn,
make a joyful noise before the King,

240
00:15:26,865 --> 00:15:27,205
the LORD.

241
00:15:27,245 --> 00:15:32,645
Let the sea roar with its fullness; the
world, and those who dwell therein.

242
00:15:32,685 --> 00:15:35,025
Let the rivers clap their hands.

243
00:15:35,885 --> 00:15:38,005
Let the mountains sing for joy together.

244
00:15:38,965 --> 00:15:43,025
Let them sing before the LORD, for he
comes to judge the earth.

245
00:15:43,865 --> 00:15:48,085
He will judge the world with
righteousness, and the peoples with equity.

246
00:15:48,125 --> 00:15:49,280
Psalm ninety-nine.

247
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:51,074
The LORD reigns!

248
00:15:51,114 --> 00:15:53,465
Let the peoples tremble.

249
00:15:53,505 --> 00:15:56,545
He sits enthroned amongst the cherubim.

250
00:15:57,265 --> 00:15:58,865
Let the earth be moved.

251
00:15:59,945 --> 00:16:01,385
The LORD is great in Zion.

252
00:16:02,385 --> 00:16:04,325
He is high above all the peoples.

253
00:16:05,205 --> 00:16:07,885
Let them praise your great and awesome
name.

254
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:09,785
He is Holy!

255
00:16:10,065 --> 00:16:12,485
The King’s strength also loves justice.

256
00:16:13,545 --> 00:16:14,705
You establish equity.

257
00:16:15,665 --> 00:16:18,685
You execute justice and righteousness in
Jacob.

258
00:16:19,365 --> 00:16:21,025
Exalt the LORD our God.

259
00:16:21,765 --> 00:16:23,305
Worship at his footstool.

260
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:25,025
He is Holy!

261
00:16:25,865 --> 00:16:31,985
Moses and Aaron were amongst his priests, Samuel
was amongst those who call on his name.

262
00:16:32,985 --> 00:16:35,425
They called on the LORD, and he answered
them.

263
00:16:35,825 --> 00:16:37,685
He spoke to them in the pillar of cloud.

264
00:16:38,765 --> 00:16:42,285
They kept his testimonies, the statute
that he gave them.

265
00:16:42,865 --> 00:16:44,845
You answered them, LORD our God.

266
00:16:45,785 --> 00:16:50,905
You are a God who forgave them, although
you took vengeance for their doings.

267
00:16:51,145 --> 00:16:53,345
Exalt the LORD, our God.

268
00:16:54,285 --> 00:16:58,505
Worship at his holy hill, for the LORD,
our God, is holy!

269
00:16:59,085 --> 00:17:01,085
Psalm one hundred.

270
00:17:01,125 --> 00:17:04,065
Shout for joy to the LORD, all you lands!

271
00:17:05,025 --> 00:17:06,745
Serve the LORD with gladness.

272
00:17:07,465 --> 00:17:09,445
Come before his presence with singing.

273
00:17:10,465 --> 00:17:12,445
Know that the LORD, he is God.

274
00:17:13,065 --> 00:17:16,425
It is he who has made us, and we are his.

275
00:17:17,045 --> 00:17:20,225
We are his people, and the sheep of his
pasture.

276
00:17:20,585 --> 00:17:25,285
Enter into his gates with thanksgiving,
and into his courts with praise.

277
00:17:26,485 --> 00:17:29,385
Give thanks to him, and bless his name.

278
00:17:30,405 --> 00:17:31,485
For the LORD is good.

279
00:17:32,405 --> 00:17:37,765
His loving kindness endures forever, his
faithfulness to all generations.

280
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:41,285
Psalm one hundred one.

281
00:17:41,325 --> 00:17:43,965
I will sing of loving kindness and
justice.

282
00:17:44,945 --> 00:17:47,385
To you, LORD, I will sing praises.

283
00:17:48,205 --> 00:17:51,285
I will be careful to live a blameless
life.

284
00:17:52,245 --> 00:17:53,565
When will you come to me?

285
00:17:54,585 --> 00:17:57,625
I will walk within my house with a
blameless heart.

286
00:17:58,505 --> 00:18:01,585
I will set no vile thing before my eyes.

287
00:18:02,045 --> 00:18:04,125
I hate the deeds of faithless men.

288
00:18:04,765 --> 00:18:06,185
They will not cling to me.

289
00:18:07,125 --> 00:18:09,305
A perverse heart will be far from me.

290
00:18:09,865 --> 00:18:11,685
I will have nothing to do with evil.

291
00:18:12,385 --> 00:18:16,845
I will silence whoever secretly slanders
his neighbour.

292
00:18:16,885 --> 00:18:20,185
I won’t tolerate one who is arrogant and
conceited.

293
00:18:21,005 --> 00:18:25,525
My eyes will be on the faithful of the
land, that they may dwell with me.

294
00:18:25,925 --> 00:18:29,365
He who walks in a perfect way, he will
serve me.

295
00:18:29,925 --> 00:18:33,625
He who practices deceit won’t dwell within
my house.

296
00:18:34,225 --> 00:18:41,625
He who

297
00:18:41,665 --> 00:18:41,965
speaks falsehood won’t be established
before my eyes.

298
00:18:42,005 --> 00:18:46,325
Morning by morning, I will destroy all the wicked
of the land, to cut off all the workers

299
00:18:46,365 --> 00:18:48,385
of iniquity from the LORD’s city.

300
00:18:48,905 --> 00:18:51,165
Psalm one hundred two.

301
00:18:51,205 --> 00:18:52,265
Hear my prayer, LORD!

302
00:18:52,905 --> 00:18:54,525
Let my cry come to you.

303
00:18:55,385 --> 00:18:58,265
Don’t hide your face from me in the day of
my distress.

304
00:18:59,385 --> 00:19:00,465
Turn your ear to me.

305
00:19:01,265 --> 00:19:03,545
Answer me quickly in the day when I call.

306
00:19:04,465 --> 00:19:06,785
For my days consume away like smoke.

307
00:19:07,265 --> 00:19:09,025
My bones are burnt as a torch.

308
00:19:09,945 --> 00:19:15,325
My heart is blighted like grass, and
withered, for I forget to eat my bread.

309
00:19:15,985 --> 00:19:20,805
By reason of the voice of my groaning, my
bones stick to my skin.

310
00:19:21,665 --> 00:19:23,705
I am like a pelican of the wilderness.

311
00:19:24,545 --> 00:19:27,505
I have become as an owl of the waste
places.

312
00:19:28,205 --> 00:19:33,505
I watch, and have become like a sparrow
that is alone on the housetop.

313
00:19:34,305 --> 00:19:36,445
My enemies reproach me all day.

314
00:19:37,045 --> 00:19:40,005
Those who are mad at me use my name as a
curse.

315
00:19:40,925 --> 00:19:46,885
For I have eaten ashes like bread, and
mixed my drink with tears, because of your indignation

316
00:19:46,925 --> 00:19:51,625
and your wrath; for you have taken me up
and thrown me away.

317
00:19:52,745 --> 00:19:54,625
My days are like a long shadow.

318
00:19:55,076 --> 00:19:56,596
I have withered like grass.

319
00:19:57,256 --> 00:20:03,276
But you, LORD, will remain forever; your
renown endures to all generations.

320
00:20:04,236 --> 00:20:10,435
You will arise and have mercy on Zion, for
it is time to have pity on her.

321
00:20:11,175 --> 00:20:13,996
Yes, the set time has come.

322
00:20:14,476 --> 00:20:19,416
For your servants take pleasure in her
stones, and have pity on her dust.

323
00:20:19,456 --> 00:20:25,236
So the nations will fear the LORD’s name,
all the kings of the earth your glory.

324
00:20:26,256 --> 00:20:28,076
For the LORD has built up Zion.

325
00:20:28,976 --> 00:20:30,375
He has appeared in his glory.

326
00:20:31,296 --> 00:20:36,356
He has responded to the prayer of
the destitute, and has not despised their prayer.

327
00:20:37,415 --> 00:20:39,935
This will be written for the generation to
come.

328
00:20:40,556 --> 00:20:45,956
A people which will be created will praise
the LORD, for he has looked down from the

329
00:20:45,996 --> 00:20:47,116
height of his sanctuary.

330
00:20:47,796 --> 00:20:54,356
From heaven, the LORD saw the earth, to
hear the groans of the prisoner, to free those

331
00:20:54,395 --> 00:21:00,596
who are condemned to death, that men may
declare the LORD’s name in Zion, and his praise

332
00:21:00,635 --> 00:21:06,856
in Jerusalem, when the peoples are gathered
together, the kingdoms, to serve the LORD.

333
00:21:07,516 --> 00:21:09,736
He weakened my strength along the course.

334
00:21:10,456 --> 00:21:11,695
He shortened my days.

335
00:21:12,496 --> 00:21:17,236
I said, “My God, don’t take me away in the
middle of my days.

336
00:21:17,976 --> 00:21:19,935
Your years are throughout all generations.

337
00:21:21,016 --> 00:21:23,756
Of old, you laid the foundation of the
earth.

338
00:21:24,395 --> 00:21:26,155
The heavens are the work of your hands.

339
00:21:26,895 --> 00:21:29,016
They will perish, but you will endure.

340
00:21:29,796 --> 00:21:32,836
Yes, all of them will wear out like a
garment.

341
00:21:33,536 --> 00:21:37,356
You will change them like a cloak, and
they will be changed.

342
00:21:37,935 --> 00:21:39,336
But you are the same.

343
00:21:40,296 --> 00:21:42,116
Your years will have no end.

344
00:21:42,976 --> 00:21:44,956
The children of your servants will
continue.

345
00:21:45,875 --> 00:21:48,536
Their offspring will be established before
you.”

346
00:21:48,976 --> 00:21:51,176
Psalm one hundred three.

347
00:21:51,216 --> 00:21:52,516
Praise the LORD, my soul!

348
00:21:53,415 --> 00:21:56,195
All that is within me, praise his holy
name!

349
00:21:57,195 --> 00:22:03,155
Praise the LORD, my soul, and don’t forget
all his benefits, who forgives all your sins,

350
00:22:03,736 --> 00:22:09,616
who heals all your diseases, who redeems
your life from destruction, who crowns you with

351
00:22:09,655 --> 00:22:16,135
loving kindness and tender mercies, who satisfies
your desire with good things, so that

352
00:22:16,175 --> 00:22:18,456
your youth is renewed like the eagle’s.

353
00:22:19,002 --> 00:22:24,322
The LORD executes righteous acts, and
justice for all who are oppressed.

354
00:22:25,663 --> 00:22:30,442
He made known his ways to Moses, his deeds
to the children of Israel.

355
00:22:31,002 --> 00:22:37,163
The LORD is merciful and gracious, slow to
anger, and abundant in loving kindness.

356
00:22:38,122 --> 00:22:42,742
He will not always accuse; neither will he
stay angry forever.

357
00:22:43,502 --> 00:22:49,542
He has not dealt with us according to our
sins, nor repaid us for our iniquities.

358
00:22:49,582 --> 00:22:55,403
For as the heavens are high above the
earth, so great is his loving kindness towards

359
00:22:55,442 --> 00:22:56,683
those who fear him.

360
00:22:56,722 --> 00:23:03,122
As far as the east is from the west,
so far has he removed our transgressions from us.

361
00:23:03,462 --> 00:23:09,183
Like a father has compassion on his children,
so the LORD has compassion on those who

362
00:23:09,222 --> 00:23:10,123
fear him.

363
00:23:10,702 --> 00:23:12,423
For he knows how we are made.

364
00:23:13,282 --> 00:23:14,822
He remembers that we are dust.

365
00:23:15,842 --> 00:23:18,363
As for man, his days are like grass.

366
00:23:18,403 --> 00:23:21,883
As a flower of the field, so he
flourishes.

367
00:23:22,683 --> 00:23:25,683
For the wind passes over it, and it is
gone.

368
00:23:26,222 --> 00:23:28,403
Its place remembers it no more.

369
00:23:29,383 --> 00:23:34,822
But the LORD’s loving kindness is from
everlasting to everlasting with those who fear

370
00:23:34,862 --> 00:23:41,722
him, his righteousness to children’s children,
to those who keep his covenant, to

371
00:23:41,762 --> 00:23:44,582
those who remember to obey his precepts.

372
00:23:44,782 --> 00:23:47,383
The LORD has established his throne in the
heavens.

373
00:23:47,423 --> 00:23:51,302
His kingdom rules over all.

374
00:23:51,342 --> 00:23:57,202
Praise the LORD, you angels of his, who
are mighty in strength, who fulfil his word,

375
00:23:57,862 --> 00:23:59,582
obeying the voice of his word.

376
00:24:00,062 --> 00:24:05,643
Praise the LORD, all you armies of his,
you servants of his, who do his pleasure.

377
00:24:06,782 --> 00:24:11,242
Praise the LORD, all you works of his, in
all places of his dominion.

378
00:24:11,923 --> 00:24:13,322
Praise the LORD, my soul!

379
00:24:13,883 --> 00:24:15,903
Psalm one hundred four.

380
00:24:15,942 --> 00:24:17,762
Bless the LORD, my soul.

381
00:24:18,802 --> 00:24:21,782
The LORD, my God, you are very great.

382
00:24:22,582 --> 00:24:25,022
You are clothed with honour and majesty.

383
00:24:25,643 --> 00:24:28,242
He covers himself with light as with a
garment.

384
00:24:29,142 --> 00:24:31,502
He stretches out the heavens like a
curtain.

385
00:24:32,522 --> 00:24:35,202
He lays the beams of his rooms in the
waters.

386
00:24:35,962 --> 00:24:37,802
He makes the clouds his chariot.

387
00:24:38,582 --> 00:24:40,502
He walks on the wings of the wind.

388
00:24:41,442 --> 00:24:45,923
He makes his messengers winds, and his
servants flames of fire.

389
00:24:46,279 --> 00:24:51,219
He laid the foundations of the earth, that
it should not be moved forever.

390
00:24:52,399 --> 00:24:55,079
You covered it with the deep as with a
cloak.

391
00:24:56,019 --> 00:24:58,119
The waters stood above the mountains.

392
00:24:58,919 --> 00:25:00,419
At your rebuke they fled.

393
00:25:01,519 --> 00:25:04,019
At the voice of your thunder they hurried
away.

394
00:25:04,559 --> 00:25:11,019
The mountains rose, the valleys sank down, to
the place which you had assigned to them.

395
00:25:11,759 --> 00:25:17,339
You have set a boundary that they may not
pass over, that they don’t turn again to cover

396
00:25:17,379 --> 00:25:18,279
the earth.

397
00:25:19,079 --> 00:25:21,099
He sends springs into the valleys.

398
00:25:21,799 --> 00:25:23,159
They run amongst the mountains.

399
00:25:24,119 --> 00:25:26,539
They give drink to every animal of the
field.

400
00:25:27,639 --> 00:25:29,699
The wild donkeys quench their thirst.

401
00:25:30,719 --> 00:25:32,939
The birds of the sky nest by them.

402
00:25:33,419 --> 00:25:34,919
They sing amongst the branches.

403
00:25:36,019 --> 00:25:38,219
He waters the mountains from his rooms.

404
00:25:38,899 --> 00:25:41,699
The earth is filled with the fruit of your
works.

405
00:25:42,499 --> 00:25:48,579
He causes the grass to grow for the
livestock, and plants for man to cultivate, that

406
00:25:48,619 --> 00:25:55,079
he may produce food out of the earth: wine
that makes the heart of man glad, oil

407
00:25:55,119 --> 00:25:59,879
to make his face to shine, and bread that
strengthens man’s heart.

408
00:26:00,539 --> 00:26:06,539
The LORD’s trees are well watered, the
cedars of Lebanon, which he has planted, where

409
00:26:06,579 --> 00:26:07,919
the birds make their nests.

410
00:26:08,699 --> 00:26:11,539
The stork makes its home in the cypress
trees.

411
00:26:12,519 --> 00:26:14,699
The high mountains are for the wild goats.

412
00:26:15,699 --> 00:26:18,419
The rocks are a refuge for the rock
badgers.

413
00:26:19,199 --> 00:26:21,519
He appointed the moon for seasons.

414
00:26:22,239 --> 00:26:24,059
The sun knows when to set.

415
00:26:24,919 --> 00:26:30,479
You make darkness, and it is night, in
which all the animals of the forest prowl.

416
00:26:31,239 --> 00:26:36,139
The young lions roar after their prey, and
seek their food from God.

417
00:26:36,579 --> 00:26:41,019
The sun rises, and they steal away, and
lie down in their dens.

418
00:26:41,959 --> 00:26:45,719
Man goes out to his work, to his labour
until the evening.

419
00:26:46,739 --> 00:26:49,239
The LORD, how many are your works!

420
00:26:49,759 --> 00:26:51,519
In wisdom, you have made them all.

421
00:26:52,379 --> 00:26:54,259
The earth is full of your riches.

422
00:26:55,059 --> 00:27:01,139
There is the sea, great and wide, in which
are innumerable living things, both small

423
00:27:01,179 --> 00:27:02,299
and large animals.

424
00:27:03,179 --> 00:27:07,959
There the ships go, and leviathan, whom
you formed to play there.

425
00:27:08,939 --> 00:27:13,939
These all wait for you, that you may give
them their food in due season.

426
00:27:14,468 --> 00:27:16,608
You give to them; they gather.

427
00:27:17,828 --> 00:27:21,388
You open your hand; they are satisfied
with good.

428
00:27:22,208 --> 00:27:24,828
You hide your face; they are troubled.

429
00:27:25,628 --> 00:27:29,888
You take away their breath; they die and
return to the dust.

430
00:27:30,868 --> 00:27:33,728
You send out your Spirit and they are
created.

431
00:27:34,908 --> 00:27:36,708
You renew the face of the ground.

432
00:27:37,868 --> 00:27:39,928
Let the LORD’s glory endure forever.

433
00:27:40,668 --> 00:27:42,888
Let the LORD rejoice in his works.

434
00:27:43,588 --> 00:27:46,388
He looks at the earth, and it trembles.

435
00:27:47,148 --> 00:27:49,448
He touches the mountains, and they smoke.

436
00:27:50,588 --> 00:27:53,168
I will sing to the LORD as long as I live.

437
00:27:54,028 --> 00:27:57,768
I will sing praise to my God while I have
any being.

438
00:27:58,648 --> 00:28:01,048
Let my meditation be sweet to him.

439
00:28:01,788 --> 00:28:03,408
I will rejoice in the LORD.

440
00:28:04,228 --> 00:28:06,368
Let sinners be consumed out of the earth.

441
00:28:07,228 --> 00:28:08,528
Let the wicked be no more.

442
00:28:09,298 --> 00:28:10,968
Bless the LORD, my soul.

443
00:28:11,708 --> 00:28:12,648
Praise the LORD!

444
00:28:13,648 --> 00:28:15,988
Psalm one hundred five.

445
00:28:16,028 --> 00:28:17,428
Give thanks to the LORD!

446
00:28:18,028 --> 00:28:19,068
Call on his name!

447
00:28:19,808 --> 00:28:22,108
Make his doings known amongst the peoples.

448
00:28:23,108 --> 00:28:25,448
Sing to him, sing praises to him!

449
00:28:25,948 --> 00:28:27,808
Tell of all his marvellous works.

450
00:28:28,588 --> 00:28:30,228
Glory in his holy name.

451
00:28:31,148 --> 00:28:33,928
Let the heart of those who seek the LORD
rejoice.

452
00:28:34,668 --> 00:28:36,708
Seek the LORD and his strength.

453
00:28:37,388 --> 00:28:39,828
Seek his face forever more.

454
00:28:39,868 --> 00:28:45,808
Remember his marvellous works that he has
done: his wonders, and the judgements of his

455
00:28:45,848 --> 00:28:52,368
mouth, you offspring of Abraham, his
servant, you children of Jacob, his

456
00:28:52,408 --> 00:28:53,308
chosen ones.

457
00:28:54,048 --> 00:28:55,488
He is the LORD, our God.

458
00:28:56,368 --> 00:28:58,208
His judgements are in all the earth.

459
00:29:02,308 --> 00:29:04,968
He has remembered his covenant forever, the
word which he commanded to a thousand generations,

460
00:29:06,148 --> 00:29:12,108
the covenant which he made with Abraham, his
oath to Isaac, and confirmed it to Jacob

461
00:29:12,148 --> 00:29:18,708
for a statute; to Israel for an
everlasting covenant, saying, “To you I

462
00:29:18,748 --> 00:29:24,108
will give the land of Canaan, the lot
of your inheritance,” when they were but a few

463
00:29:24,148 --> 00:29:28,908
men in number, yes, very few, and
foreigners in it.

464
00:29:29,368 --> 00:29:34,348
They went about from nation to nation,
from one kingdom to another people.

465
00:29:34,948 --> 00:29:37,128
He allowed no one to do them wrong.

466
00:29:37,928 --> 00:29:43,508
Yes, he reproved kings for their sakes,
“Don’t touch my anointed ones!

467
00:29:44,228 --> 00:29:45,768
Do my prophets no harm!”

468
00:29:46,748 --> 00:29:48,648
He called for a famine on the land.

469
00:29:49,548 --> 00:29:50,948
He destroyed the food supplies.

470
00:29:51,505 --> 00:29:53,285
He sent a man before them.

471
00:29:54,245 --> 00:29:56,245
Joseph was sold for a slave.

472
00:29:57,485 --> 00:29:59,725
They bruised his feet with shackles.

473
00:30:00,525 --> 00:30:07,145
His neck was locked in irons, until the
time that his word happened, and the LORD’s word

474
00:30:07,185 --> 00:30:08,285
proved him true.

475
00:30:08,825 --> 00:30:14,745
The king sent and freed him, even the
ruler of peoples, and let him go free.

476
00:30:15,485 --> 00:30:21,505
He made him lord of his house, and
ruler of all of his possessions, to discipline his

477
00:30:21,545 --> 00:30:25,345
princes at his pleasure, and to teach his
elders wisdom.

478
00:30:26,765 --> 00:30:28,785
Israel also came into Egypt.

479
00:30:29,325 --> 00:30:31,345
Jacob lived in the land of Ham.

480
00:30:32,225 --> 00:30:36,845
He increased his people greatly, and made
them stronger than their adversaries.

481
00:30:37,805 --> 00:30:42,405
He turned their heart to hate his people,
to conspire against his servants.

482
00:30:43,665 --> 00:30:48,025
He sent Moses, his servant, and Aaron,
whom he had chosen.

483
00:30:48,605 --> 00:30:52,845
They performed miracles amongst them, and
wonders in the land of Ham.

484
00:30:53,705 --> 00:30:56,265
He sent darkness, and made it dark.

485
00:30:57,245 --> 00:30:59,265
They didn’t rebel against his words.

486
00:30:59,925 --> 00:31:03,565
He turned their waters into blood, and
killed their fish.

487
00:31:04,605 --> 00:31:08,945
Their land swarmed with frogs, even in the
rooms of their kings.

488
00:31:10,105 --> 00:31:15,185
He spoke, and swarms of flies came, and
lice in all their borders.

489
00:31:16,065 --> 00:31:19,765
He gave them hail for rain, with lightning
in their land.

490
00:31:20,525 --> 00:31:26,065
He struck their vines and also their fig
trees, and shattered the trees of their country.

491
00:31:27,045 --> 00:31:32,125
He spoke, and the locusts came with the
grasshoppers, without number.

492
00:31:32,965 --> 00:31:37,705
They ate up every plant in their land, and
ate up the fruit of their ground.

493
00:31:38,485 --> 00:31:44,605
He struck also all the firstborn in their
land, the first fruits of all their manhood.

494
00:31:45,405 --> 00:31:47,945
He brought them out with silver and gold.

495
00:31:48,825 --> 00:31:52,005
There was not one feeble person amongst
his tribes.

496
00:31:52,745 --> 00:31:57,505
Egypt was glad when they departed, for the
fear of them had fallen on them.

497
00:31:58,145 --> 00:32:02,565
He spread a cloud for a covering, fire to
give light in the night.

498
00:32:03,525 --> 00:32:09,345
They asked, and he brought quails, and
satisfied them with the bread of the sky.

499
00:32:10,565 --> 00:32:13,565
He opened the rock, and waters gushed out.

500
00:32:14,085 --> 00:32:16,465
They ran as a river in the dry places.

501
00:32:17,585 --> 00:32:21,485
For he remembered his holy word, and
Abraham, his servant.

502
00:32:22,024 --> 00:32:26,464
He brought his people out with joy, his
chosen with singing.

503
00:32:27,384 --> 00:32:29,444
He gave them the lands of the nations.

504
00:32:30,404 --> 00:32:35,524
They took the labour of the peoples
in possession, that they might keep his statutes,

505
00:32:35,564 --> 00:32:37,664
and observe his laws.

506
00:32:38,604 --> 00:32:39,584
Praise the LORD!

507
00:32:39,924 --> 00:32:42,404
Psalm one hundred six.

508
00:32:42,444 --> 00:32:43,464
Praise the LORD!

509
00:32:44,244 --> 00:32:50,204
Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,
for his loving kindness endures forever.

510
00:32:51,364 --> 00:32:56,724
Who can utter the mighty acts of the LORD,
or fully declare all his praise?

511
00:32:57,784 --> 00:32:59,664
Blessed are those who keep justice.

512
00:33:00,324 --> 00:33:03,644
Blessed is one who does what is right at
all times.

513
00:33:04,344 --> 00:33:08,344
Remember me, LORD, with the favour that
you show to your people.

514
00:33:09,064 --> 00:33:15,624
Visit me with your salvation, that I may
see the prosperity of your chosen, that I

515
00:33:15,664 --> 00:33:21,124
may rejoice in the gladness of your
nation, that I may glory with your inheritance.

516
00:33:21,804 --> 00:33:23,244
We have sinned with our fathers.

517
00:33:23,984 --> 00:33:25,444
We have committed iniquity.

518
00:33:25,984 --> 00:33:27,464
We have done wickedly.

519
00:33:28,024 --> 00:33:31,304
Our fathers didn’t understand your wonders
in Egypt.

520
00:33:32,024 --> 00:33:37,124
They didn’t remember the multitude of your
loving kindnesses, but were rebellious at

521
00:33:37,164 --> 00:33:39,564
the sea, even at the Red Sea.

522
00:33:39,884 --> 00:33:45,764
Nevertheless he saved them for his name’s sake,
that he might make his mighty power known.

523
00:33:46,524 --> 00:33:52,904
He rebuked the Red Sea also, and it was
dried up; so he led them through the depths,

524
00:33:53,404 --> 00:33:54,324
as through a desert.

525
00:33:55,244 --> 00:34:00,624
He saved them from the hand of him who
hated them, and redeemed them from the hand of

526
00:34:00,664 --> 00:34:01,564
the enemy.

527
00:34:01,884 --> 00:34:03,984
The waters covered their adversaries.

528
00:34:04,964 --> 00:34:06,584
There was not one of them left.

529
00:34:07,304 --> 00:34:08,744
Then they believed his words.

530
00:34:09,424 --> 00:34:10,664
They sang his praise.

531
00:34:11,584 --> 00:34:13,144
They soon forgot his works.

532
00:34:14,124 --> 00:34:20,144
They didn’t wait for his counsel, but gave
in to craving in the desert, and tested God

533
00:34:20,184 --> 00:34:21,084
in the wasteland.

534
00:34:22,044 --> 00:34:26,324
He gave them their request, but sent
leanness into their soul.

535
00:34:27,064 --> 00:34:31,844
They envied Moses also in the camp, and
Aaron, the LORD’s saint.

536
00:34:32,764 --> 00:34:38,904
The earth opened and swallowed up Dathan,
and covered the company of Abiram.

537
00:34:38,944 --> 00:34:40,824
A fire was kindled in their company.

538
00:34:41,704 --> 00:34:43,224
The flame burnt up the wicked.

539
00:34:44,084 --> 00:34:47,784
They made a calf in Horeb, and worshipped
a molten image.

540
00:34:48,209 --> 00:34:52,749
Thus they exchanged their glory for an
image of a bull that eats grass.

541
00:34:53,989 --> 00:35:00,869
They forgot God, their Saviour, who had
done great things in Egypt, wondrous works in

542
00:35:00,909 --> 00:35:04,809
the land of Ham, and awesome things by the
Red Sea.

543
00:35:05,629 --> 00:35:11,709
Therefore he said that he would destroy
them, had Moses, his chosen, not stood before

544
00:35:11,749 --> 00:35:17,009
him in the breach, to turn away his wrath,
so that he wouldn’t destroy them.

545
00:35:17,849 --> 00:35:20,649
Yes, they despised the pleasant land.

546
00:35:21,289 --> 00:35:26,929
They didn’t believe his word, but murmured in
their tents, and didn’t listen to the LORD’s

547
00:35:26,969 --> 00:35:27,869
voice.

548
00:35:28,149 --> 00:35:33,389
Therefore he swore to them that he would
overthrow them in the wilderness, that he would

549
00:35:33,429 --> 00:35:38,109
overthrow their offspring amongst the
nations, and scatter them in the lands.

550
00:35:39,009 --> 00:35:44,689
They joined themselves also to Baal Peor,
and ate the sacrifices of the dead.

551
00:35:45,689 --> 00:35:48,469
Thus they provoked him to anger with their
deeds.

552
00:35:49,689 --> 00:35:51,289
The plague broke in on them.

553
00:35:52,269 --> 00:35:57,669
Then Phinehas stood up and executed
judgement, so the plague was stopped.

554
00:35:58,489 --> 00:36:03,049
That was credited to him for
righteousness, for all generations to come.

555
00:36:04,069 --> 00:36:10,289
They angered him also at the waters of
Meribah, so that Moses was troubled for their

556
00:36:10,329 --> 00:36:16,489
sakes; because they were rebellious against his
spirit, he spoke rashly with his lips.

557
00:36:17,129 --> 00:36:22,829
They didn’t destroy the peoples, as the
LORD commanded them, but mixed themselves with

558
00:36:22,869 --> 00:36:25,049
the nations, and learnt their works.

559
00:36:26,089 --> 00:36:29,669
They served their idols, which became a
snare to them.

560
00:36:30,369 --> 00:36:34,629
Yes, they sacrificed their sons and their
daughters to demons.

561
00:36:34,669 --> 00:36:41,309
They shed innocent blood, even the blood of
their sons and of their daughters, whom they

562
00:36:41,349 --> 00:36:43,429
sacrificed to the idols of Canaan.

563
00:36:44,569 --> 00:36:46,489
The land was polluted with blood.

564
00:36:47,369 --> 00:36:52,329
Thus they were defiled with their works,
and prostituted themselves in their deeds.

565
00:36:53,049 --> 00:36:56,029
Therefore the LORD burnt with anger
against his people.

566
00:36:56,629 --> 00:36:57,869
He abhorred his inheritance.

567
00:36:59,109 --> 00:37:01,169
He gave them into the hand of the nations.

568
00:37:01,869 --> 00:37:04,769
Those who hated them ruled over them.

569
00:37:05,509 --> 00:37:07,609
Their enemies also oppressed them.

570
00:37:08,389 --> 00:37:11,029
They were brought into subjection under
their hand.

571
00:37:11,332 --> 00:37:17,112
He rescued them many times, but they
were rebellious in their counsel, and were brought

572
00:37:17,152 --> 00:37:18,532
low in their iniquity.

573
00:37:19,492 --> 00:37:23,552
Nevertheless he regarded their distress,
when he heard their cry.

574
00:37:24,572 --> 00:37:30,152
He remembered for them his covenant, and
repented according to the multitude of his loving

575
00:37:30,192 --> 00:37:31,092
kindnesses.

576
00:37:31,632 --> 00:37:35,632
He made them also to be pitied by all
those who carried them captive.

577
00:37:36,792 --> 00:37:43,312
Save us, LORD, our God, gather us from
amongst the nations, to give thanks to

578
00:37:43,352 --> 00:37:46,172
your holy name, to triumph in your praise!

579
00:37:46,732 --> 00:37:51,952
Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel,
from everlasting even to everlasting!

580
00:37:52,932 --> 00:37:55,212
Let all the people say, “Amen.”

581
00:37:56,012 --> 00:37:57,052
Praise the LORD!

582
00:37:58,052 --> 00:38:00,772
Psalm one hundred seven.

583
00:38:00,812 --> 00:38:06,752
Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,
for his loving kindness endures forever.

584
00:38:07,452 --> 00:38:13,452
Let the redeemed by the LORD say so, whom
he has redeemed from the hand of the adversary,

585
00:38:14,412 --> 00:38:20,292
and gathered out of the lands, from the east
and from the west, from the north and from

586
00:38:20,332 --> 00:38:21,232
the south.

587
00:38:21,972 --> 00:38:24,632
They wandered in the wilderness in a
desert way.

588
00:38:25,612 --> 00:38:27,472
They found no city to live in.

589
00:38:28,012 --> 00:38:31,372
Hungry and thirsty, their soul fainted in
them.

590
00:38:32,352 --> 00:38:37,352
Then they cried to the LORD in their
trouble, and he delivered them out of their distresses.

591
00:38:38,172 --> 00:38:43,552
He led them also by a straight way, that
they might go to a city to live in.

592
00:38:44,112 --> 00:38:49,652
Let them praise the LORD for his loving
kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children

593
00:38:49,692 --> 00:38:50,592
of men!

594
00:38:51,312 --> 00:38:53,692
For he satisfies the longing soul.

595
00:38:54,632 --> 00:38:56,892
He fills the hungry soul with good.

596
00:38:56,932 --> 00:39:03,752
Some sat in darkness and in the shadow of
death, being bound in affliction and iron,

597
00:39:04,412 --> 00:39:09,632
because they rebelled against the words of
God, and condemned the counsel of the Most

598
00:39:09,672 --> 00:39:10,572
High.

599
00:39:11,092 --> 00:39:14,452
Therefore he brought down their heart with
labour.

600
00:39:14,492 --> 00:39:17,532
They fell down, and there was no one to
help.

601
00:39:18,292 --> 00:39:22,912
Then they cried to the LORD in their
trouble, and he saved them out of their distresses.

602
00:39:23,832 --> 00:39:29,152
He brought them out of darkness and the
shadow of death, and broke away their chains.

603
00:39:29,721 --> 00:39:35,421
Let them praise the LORD for his loving
kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children

604
00:39:35,461 --> 00:39:36,361
of men!

605
00:39:36,781 --> 00:39:41,601
For he has broken the gates of bronze, and
cut through bars of iron.

606
00:39:42,541 --> 00:39:47,721
Fools are afflicted because of their
disobedience, and because of their iniquities.

607
00:39:48,421 --> 00:39:51,281
Their soul abhors all kinds of food.

608
00:39:52,041 --> 00:39:53,841
They draw near to the gates of death.

609
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:59,721
Then they cry to the LORD in their
trouble, and he saves them out of their distresses.

610
00:40:00,761 --> 00:40:05,421
He sends his word, and heals them, and
delivers them from their graves.

611
00:40:05,981 --> 00:40:11,281
Let them praise the LORD for his loving
kindness, for his wonderful deeds to the children

612
00:40:11,321 --> 00:40:12,221
of men!

613
00:40:12,581 --> 00:40:17,681
Let them offer the sacrifices of
thanksgiving, and declare his deeds with singing.

614
00:40:18,541 --> 00:40:25,061
Those who go down to the sea in ships, who
do business in great waters, these see the

615
00:40:25,101 --> 00:40:27,761
LORD’s deeds, and his wonders in the deep.

616
00:40:28,221 --> 00:40:33,101
For he commands, and raises the stormy
wind, which lifts up its waves.

617
00:40:33,921 --> 00:40:37,861
They mount up to the sky; they go down
again to the depths.

618
00:40:38,801 --> 00:40:41,201
Their soul melts away because of trouble.

619
00:40:42,101 --> 00:40:48,201
They reel back and forth, and stagger like
a drunken man, and are at their wits’ end.

620
00:40:49,221 --> 00:40:54,001
Then they cry to the LORD in their
trouble, and he brings them out of their distress.

621
00:40:54,521 --> 00:40:58,361
He makes the storm a calm, so that its
waves are still.

622
00:40:59,361 --> 00:41:04,461
Then they are glad because it is calm, so
he brings them to their desired haven.

623
00:41:05,381 --> 00:41:11,001
Let them praise the LORD for his loving
kindness, for his wonderful deeds for the children

624
00:41:11,041 --> 00:41:11,941
of men!

625
00:41:12,161 --> 00:41:17,801
Let them exalt him also in the assembly of
the people, and praise him in the seat of

626
00:41:17,841 --> 00:41:18,741
the elders.

627
00:41:19,101 --> 00:41:25,561
He turns rivers into a desert, water
springs into a thirsty ground, and a

628
00:41:25,601 --> 00:41:30,901
fruitful land into a salt waste, for the
wickedness of those who dwell in it.

629
00:41:31,281 --> 00:41:36,941
He turns a desert into a pool of water,
and a dry land into water springs.

630
00:41:37,981 --> 00:41:43,941
There he makes the hungry live, that they
may prepare a city to live in, sow fields,

631
00:41:43,981 --> 00:41:47,421
plant vineyards, and reap the fruits of
increase.

632
00:41:48,181 --> 00:41:51,541
He blesses them also, so that they are
multiplied greatly.

633
00:41:52,056 --> 00:41:54,556
He doesn’t allow their livestock to
decrease.

634
00:41:55,616 --> 00:42:01,996
Again, they are diminished and bowed down
through oppression, trouble, and sorrow.

635
00:42:03,216 --> 00:42:08,576
He pours contempt on princes, and causes
them to wander in a trackless waste.

636
00:42:09,116 --> 00:42:14,456
Yet he lifts the needy out of their
affliction, and increases their families like a flock.

637
00:42:15,316 --> 00:42:17,596
The upright will see it, and be glad.

638
00:42:18,356 --> 00:42:20,456
All the wicked will shut their mouths.

639
00:42:21,156 --> 00:42:24,596
Whoever is wise will pay attention to
these things.

640
00:42:25,516 --> 00:42:28,476
They will consider the loving kindnesses
of the LORD.

641
00:42:28,516 --> 00:42:31,156
Psalm one hundred eight.

642
00:42:31,196 --> 00:42:32,956
My heart is steadfast, God.

643
00:42:33,736 --> 00:42:37,196
I will sing and I will make music with my
soul.

644
00:42:37,916 --> 00:42:39,956
Wake up, harp and lyre!

645
00:42:40,596 --> 00:42:41,956
I will wake up the dawn.

646
00:42:42,916 --> 00:42:45,776
I will give thanks to you, LORD, amongst
the nations.

647
00:42:46,736 --> 00:42:49,456
I will sing praises to you amongst the
peoples.

648
00:42:50,416 --> 00:42:53,256
For your loving kindness is great above
the heavens.

649
00:42:53,576 --> 00:42:55,776
Your faithfulness reaches to the skies.

650
00:42:56,756 --> 00:42:59,256
Be exalted, God, above the heavens!

651
00:42:59,936 --> 00:43:02,076
Let your glory be over all the earth.

652
00:43:02,896 --> 00:43:08,156
That your beloved may be delivered, save
with your right hand, and answer us.

653
00:43:08,636 --> 00:43:15,316
God has spoken from his sanctuary: “In
triumph, I will divide Shechem, and measure out

654
00:43:15,356 --> 00:43:17,616
the valley of Succoth.

655
00:43:17,656 --> 00:43:18,676
Gilead is mine.

656
00:43:19,576 --> 00:43:20,596
Manasseh is mine.

657
00:43:20,636 --> 00:43:23,296
Ephraim also is my helmet.

658
00:43:24,096 --> 00:43:26,236
Judah is my sceptre.

659
00:43:26,276 --> 00:43:28,556
Moab is my wash pot.

660
00:43:28,596 --> 00:43:30,796
I will toss my sandal on Edom.

661
00:43:31,456 --> 00:43:33,556
I will shout over Philistia.”

662
00:43:33,816 --> 00:43:36,096
Who will bring me into the fortified city?

663
00:43:36,936 --> 00:43:38,356
Who will lead me to Edom?

664
00:43:39,276 --> 00:43:41,116
Haven’t you rejected us, God?

665
00:43:41,676 --> 00:43:44,076
You don’t go out, God, with our armies.

666
00:43:44,836 --> 00:43:48,716
Give us help against the enemy, for the
help of man is vain.

667
00:43:49,876 --> 00:43:55,516
Through God, we will do valiantly, for it
is he who will tread down our enemies.

668
00:43:56,916 --> 00:43:59,216
Psalm one hundred nine.

669
00:43:59,256 --> 00:44:05,596
God of my praise, don’t remain silent, for
they have opened the mouth of the wicked and

670
00:44:05,636 --> 00:44:07,456
the mouth of deceit against me.

671
00:44:08,016 --> 00:44:10,296
They have spoken to me with a lying
tongue.

672
00:44:11,196 --> 00:44:16,456
They have also surrounded me with words of
hatred, and fought against me without a cause.

673
00:44:17,736 --> 00:44:22,376
In return for my love, they are my
adversaries; but I am in prayer.

674
00:44:22,890 --> 00:44:27,210
They have rewarded me evil for good, and
hatred for my love.

675
00:44:28,030 --> 00:44:29,810
Set a wicked man over him.

676
00:44:30,790 --> 00:44:33,410
Let an adversary stand at his right hand.

677
00:44:34,330 --> 00:44:36,990
When he is judged, let him come out
guilty.

678
00:44:38,170 --> 00:44:39,970
Let his prayer be turned into sin.

679
00:44:40,930 --> 00:44:42,110
Let his days be few.

680
00:44:43,170 --> 00:44:44,490
Let another take his office.

681
00:44:45,390 --> 00:44:48,870
Let his children be fatherless, and his
wife a widow.

682
00:44:49,530 --> 00:44:52,270
Let his children be wandering beggars.

683
00:44:52,890 --> 00:44:54,670
Let them be sought from their ruins.

684
00:44:55,550 --> 00:44:57,970
Let the creditor seize all that he has.

685
00:44:58,610 --> 00:45:01,710
Let strangers plunder the fruit of his
labour.

686
00:45:01,750 --> 00:45:07,250
Let there be no one to extend kindness to
him, neither let there be anyone to have pity

687
00:45:07,290 --> 00:45:08,670
on his fatherless children.

688
00:45:09,570 --> 00:45:11,450
Let his posterity be cut off.

689
00:45:12,210 --> 00:45:15,550
In the generation following let their name
be blotted out.

690
00:45:16,270 --> 00:45:19,490
Let the iniquity of his fathers be
remembered by the LORD.

691
00:45:20,050 --> 00:45:22,790
Don’t let the sin of his mother be blotted
out.

692
00:45:23,590 --> 00:45:29,230
Let them be before the LORD continually, that
he may cut off their memory from the earth;

693
00:45:30,030 --> 00:45:36,030
because he didn’t remember to show kindness,
but persecuted the poor and needy man, the

694
00:45:36,070 --> 00:45:37,930
broken in heart, to kill them.

695
00:45:38,450 --> 00:45:41,630
Yes, he loved cursing, and it came to him.

696
00:45:42,270 --> 00:45:45,930
He didn’t delight in blessing, and it was
far from him.

697
00:45:45,970 --> 00:45:50,470
He clothed himself also with cursing as
with his garment.

698
00:45:51,450 --> 00:45:56,330
It came into his inward parts like water,
like oil into his bones.

699
00:45:57,190 --> 00:46:02,990
Let it be to him as the clothing with
which he covers himself, for the belt that is always

700
00:46:03,030 --> 00:46:03,930
around him.

701
00:46:04,610 --> 00:46:10,970
This is the reward of my adversaries from
the LORD, of those who speak evil against my

702
00:46:11,010 --> 00:46:11,910
soul.

703
00:46:12,090 --> 00:46:17,890
But deal with me, GOD the Lord, for
your name’s sake, because your loving kindness is

704
00:46:17,930 --> 00:46:21,970
good, deliver me; for I am poor and needy.

705
00:46:22,830 --> 00:46:24,610
My heart is wounded within me.

706
00:46:25,250 --> 00:46:27,410
I fade away like an evening shadow.

707
00:46:27,890 --> 00:46:29,750
I am shaken off like a locust.

708
00:46:30,530 --> 00:46:32,190
My knees are weak through fasting.

709
00:46:33,170 --> 00:46:35,650
My body is thin and lacks fat.

710
00:46:36,230 --> 00:46:38,310
I have also become a reproach to them.

711
00:46:39,170 --> 00:46:41,630
When they see me, they shake their head.

712
00:46:42,510 --> 00:46:44,490
Help me, LORD, my God.

713
00:46:44,851 --> 00:46:50,711
Save me according to your loving kindness;
that they may know that this is your hand;

714
00:46:51,531 --> 00:46:53,451
that you, LORD, have done it.

715
00:46:54,071 --> 00:46:56,211
They may curse, but you bless.

716
00:46:57,171 --> 00:47:01,531
When they arise, they will be shamed, but
your servant shall rejoice.

717
00:47:02,111 --> 00:47:05,511
Let my adversaries be clothed with
dishonour.

718
00:47:05,551 --> 00:47:09,571
Let them cover themselves with their own
shame as with a robe.

719
00:47:10,411 --> 00:47:13,751
I will give great thanks to the LORD with
my mouth.

720
00:47:14,411 --> 00:47:17,511
Yes, I will praise him amongst the
multitude.

721
00:47:18,311 --> 00:47:23,811
For he will stand at the right hand of
the needy, to save him from those who judge his

722
00:47:23,851 --> 00:47:24,751
soul.

723
00:47:25,491 --> 00:47:27,571
Psalm one hundred ten.

724
00:47:27,611 --> 00:47:33,751
The LORD says to my Lord, “Sit at my
right hand, until I make your enemies your footstool

725
00:47:33,791 --> 00:47:34,691
for your feet.”

726
00:47:35,571 --> 00:47:38,891
The LORD will send out the rod of your
strength out of Zion.

727
00:47:39,511 --> 00:47:41,331
Rule amongst your enemies.

728
00:47:41,851 --> 00:47:47,171
Your people offer themselves willingly in
the day of your power, in holy array.

729
00:47:47,711 --> 00:47:51,551
Out of the womb of the morning, you have
the dew of your youth.

730
00:47:52,491 --> 00:47:59,031
The LORD has sworn, and will not change his
mind: “You are a priest forever in the order

731
00:47:59,071 --> 00:48:00,151
of Melchizedek.”

732
00:48:00,871 --> 00:48:02,731
The Lord is at your right hand.

733
00:48:03,531 --> 00:48:05,871
He will crush kings in the day of his
wrath.

734
00:48:05,911 --> 00:48:08,431
He will judge amongst the nations.

735
00:48:09,271 --> 00:48:10,711
He will heap up dead bodies.

736
00:48:11,591 --> 00:48:13,931
He will crush the ruler of the whole
earth.

737
00:48:14,671 --> 00:48:19,091
He will drink of the brook on the way;
therefore he will lift up his head.

738
00:48:19,971 --> 00:48:21,951
Psalm one hundred eleven.

739
00:48:21,991 --> 00:48:23,451
Praise the LORD!

740
00:48:23,891 --> 00:48:29,231
I will give thanks to the LORD with my
whole heart, in the council of the upright, and

741
00:48:29,271 --> 00:48:30,171
in the congregation.

742
00:48:30,971 --> 00:48:35,391
The LORD’s works are great, pondered by
all those who delight in them.

743
00:48:36,171 --> 00:48:38,251
His work is honour and majesty.

744
00:48:39,331 --> 00:48:41,211
His righteousness endures forever.

745
00:48:42,391 --> 00:48:45,331
He has caused his wonderful works to be
remembered.

746
00:48:45,771 --> 00:48:47,731
The LORD is gracious and merciful.

747
00:48:48,511 --> 00:48:50,851
He has given food to those who fear him.

748
00:48:51,391 --> 00:48:53,171
He always remembers his covenant.

749
00:48:54,031 --> 00:48:59,831
He has shown his people the power of his
works, in giving them the heritage of the nations.

750
00:49:00,671 --> 00:49:03,831
The works of his hands are truth and
justice.

751
00:49:04,591 --> 00:49:06,291
All his precepts are sure.

752
00:49:07,131 --> 00:49:09,451
They are established forever and ever.

753
00:49:09,766 --> 00:49:12,286
They are done in truth and uprightness.

754
00:49:13,206 --> 00:49:15,506
He has sent redemption to his people.

755
00:49:16,386 --> 00:49:18,366
He has ordained his covenant forever.

756
00:49:19,506 --> 00:49:21,766
His name is holy and awesome!

757
00:49:23,006 --> 00:49:25,466
The fear of the LORD is the beginning of
wisdom.

758
00:49:26,086 --> 00:49:29,026
All those who do his work have a good
understanding.

759
00:49:30,346 --> 00:49:31,786
His praise endures forever!

760
00:49:32,906 --> 00:49:34,966
Psalm one hundred twelve.

761
00:49:35,006 --> 00:49:36,126
Praise the LORD!

762
00:49:36,926 --> 00:49:42,046
Blessed is the man who fears the LORD, who
delights greatly in his commandments.

763
00:49:43,126 --> 00:49:45,386
His offspring will be mighty in the land.

764
00:49:46,226 --> 00:49:48,566
The generation of the upright will be
blessed.

765
00:49:49,066 --> 00:49:51,066
Wealth and riches are in his house.

766
00:49:52,726 --> 00:49:53,706
His righteousness endures forever.

767
00:49:54,486 --> 00:49:59,966
Light dawns in the darkness for
the upright, gracious, merciful, and righteous.

768
00:50:01,046 --> 00:50:04,206
It is well with the man who deals
graciously and lends.

769
00:50:05,126 --> 00:50:07,866
He will maintain his cause in judgement.

770
00:50:07,906 --> 00:50:09,306
For he will never be shaken.

771
00:50:10,106 --> 00:50:12,006
The righteous will be remembered forever.

772
00:50:13,146 --> 00:50:15,166
He will not be afraid of evil news.

773
00:50:16,086 --> 00:50:18,986
His heart is steadfast, trusting in the
LORD.

774
00:50:19,986 --> 00:50:20,946
His heart is established.

775
00:50:22,026 --> 00:50:25,926
He will not be afraid in the end when he
sees his adversaries.

776
00:50:26,666 --> 00:50:30,006
He has dispersed, he has given to the
poor.

777
00:50:30,526 --> 00:50:32,206
His righteousness endures forever.

778
00:50:33,226 --> 00:50:36,226
His horn will be exalted with honour.

779
00:50:36,266 --> 00:50:38,546
The wicked will see it, and be grieved.

780
00:50:39,226 --> 00:50:42,046
He shall gnash with his teeth, and melt
away.

781
00:50:43,226 --> 00:50:45,126
The desire of the wicked will perish.

782
00:50:45,726 --> 00:50:48,326
Psalm one hundred thirteen.

783
00:50:48,366 --> 00:50:49,266
Praise the LORD!

784
00:50:49,906 --> 00:50:53,566
Praise, you servants of the LORD, praise
the LORD’s name.

785
00:50:54,366 --> 00:50:59,506
Blessed be the LORD’s name, from this time
forward and forever more.

786
00:50:59,546 --> 00:51:04,986
From the rising of the sun to its going
down, The LORD’s name is to be praised.

787
00:51:05,946 --> 00:51:10,486
The LORD is high above all nations, his
glory above the heavens.

788
00:51:11,346 --> 00:51:17,726
Who is like the LORD, our God, who has his
seat on high, who stoops down to see in heaven

789
00:51:17,766 --> 00:51:18,806
and in the earth?

790
00:51:19,346 --> 00:51:25,666
He raises up the poor out of the dust, and
lifts up the needy from the ash heap, that

791
00:51:25,706 --> 00:51:29,866
he may set him with princes, even with the
princes of his people.

792
00:51:30,766 --> 00:51:35,446
He settles the barren woman in her home as
a joyful mother of children.

793
00:51:36,126 --> 00:51:37,026
Praise the LORD!

794
00:51:37,356 --> 00:51:39,636
Psalm one hundred fourteen.

795
00:51:39,676 --> 00:51:45,636
When Israel went out of Egypt, the house
of Jacob from a people of foreign language,

796
00:51:46,636 --> 00:51:50,436
Judah became his sanctuary, Israel his
dominion.

797
00:51:51,676 --> 00:51:53,496
The sea saw it, and fled.

798
00:51:54,616 --> 00:51:56,196
The Jordan was driven back.

799
00:51:56,556 --> 00:52:01,276
The mountains skipped like rams, the
little hills like lambs.

800
00:52:01,616 --> 00:52:03,956
What was it, you sea, that you fled?

801
00:52:03,996 --> 00:52:07,016
You Jordan, that you turned back?

802
00:52:07,856 --> 00:52:10,676
You mountains, that you skipped like rams?

803
00:52:11,556 --> 00:52:13,636
You little hills, like lambs?

804
00:52:13,996 --> 00:52:19,636
Tremble, you earth, at the presence of the
Lord, at the presence of the God of Jacob,

805
00:52:20,476 --> 00:52:25,876
who turned the rock into a pool of water,
the flint into a spring of waters.

806
00:52:26,416 --> 00:52:28,616
Psalm one hundred fifteen.

807
00:52:28,656 --> 00:52:35,136
Not to us, LORD, not to us, but to your
name give glory, for your loving

808
00:52:35,176 --> 00:52:37,776
kindness, and for your truth’s sake.

809
00:52:38,976 --> 00:52:42,916
Why should the nations say, “Where is
their God, now?”

810
00:52:43,436 --> 00:52:45,036
But our God is in the heavens.

811
00:52:45,916 --> 00:52:47,516
He does whatever he pleases.

812
00:52:48,356 --> 00:52:52,376
Their idols are silver and gold, the work
of men’s hands.

813
00:52:53,076 --> 00:52:55,276
They have mouths, but they don’t speak.

814
00:52:55,956 --> 00:52:58,356
They have eyes, but they don’t see.

815
00:52:58,396 --> 00:53:01,536
They have ears, but they don’t hear.

816
00:53:02,336 --> 00:53:04,616
They have noses, but they don’t smell.

817
00:53:05,476 --> 00:53:07,696
They have hands, but they don’t feel.

818
00:53:08,456 --> 00:53:13,296
They have feet, but they don’t walk,
neither do they speak through their throat.

819
00:53:14,036 --> 00:53:19,876
Those who make them will be like them;
yes, everyone who trusts in them.

820
00:53:20,696 --> 00:53:22,756
Israel, trust in the LORD!

821
00:53:22,796 --> 00:53:25,276
He is their help and their shield.

822
00:53:25,896 --> 00:53:28,036
House of Aaron, trust in the LORD!

823
00:53:28,716 --> 00:53:30,336
He is their help and their shield.

824
00:53:30,976 --> 00:53:33,676
You who fear the LORD, trust in the LORD!

825
00:53:34,216 --> 00:53:35,796
He is their help and their shield.

826
00:53:36,676 --> 00:53:37,916
The LORD remembers us.

827
00:53:38,516 --> 00:53:39,416
He will bless us.

828
00:53:40,076 --> 00:53:41,716
He will bless the house of Israel.

829
00:53:42,556 --> 00:53:44,116
He will bless the house of Aaron.

830
00:53:44,876 --> 00:53:48,896
He will bless those who fear the LORD,
both small and great.

831
00:53:49,456 --> 00:53:53,216
May the LORD increase you more and more,
you and your children.

832
00:53:54,056 --> 00:53:57,376
Blessed are you by the LORD, who made
heaven and earth.

833
00:53:58,156 --> 00:54:03,456
The heavens are the LORD’s heavens, but he
has given the earth to the children of men.

834
00:54:03,848 --> 00:54:10,368
The dead don’t praise the LORD, nor any
who go down into silence, but we will

835
00:54:10,408 --> 00:54:15,568
bless the LORD, from this time forward and
forever more.

836
00:54:15,608 --> 00:54:16,708
Praise the LORD!

837
00:54:17,668 --> 00:54:19,828
Psalm one hundred sixteen.

838
00:54:19,868 --> 00:54:25,368
I love the LORD, because he listens to my
voice, and my cries for mercy.

839
00:54:26,068 --> 00:54:32,388
Because he has turned his ear to me, therefore
I will call on him as long as I live.

840
00:54:33,648 --> 00:54:38,808
The cords of death surrounded me, the
pains of Sheol got a hold of me.

841
00:54:39,808 --> 00:54:41,388
I found trouble and sorrow.

842
00:54:41,948 --> 00:54:47,568
Then I called on the LORD’s name: “LORD, I
beg you, deliver my soul.”

843
00:54:48,688 --> 00:54:50,388
The LORD is gracious and righteous.

844
00:54:51,328 --> 00:54:53,588
Yes, our God is merciful.

845
00:54:54,268 --> 00:54:56,168
The LORD preserves the simple.

846
00:54:57,228 --> 00:54:59,668
I was brought low, and he saved me.

847
00:55:00,668 --> 00:55:05,708
Return to your rest, my soul, for the LORD
has dealt bountifully with you.

848
00:55:06,028 --> 00:55:12,148
For you have delivered my soul from death,
my eyes from tears, and my feet from falling.

849
00:55:12,808 --> 00:55:16,068
I will walk before the LORD in the land of
the living.

850
00:55:16,788 --> 00:55:21,448
I believed, therefore I said, “I was
greatly afflicted.”

851
00:55:22,388 --> 00:55:25,688
I said in my haste, “All people are
liars.”

852
00:55:26,528 --> 00:55:30,228
What will I give to the LORD for all his
benefits towards me?

853
00:55:30,728 --> 00:55:34,748
I will take the cup of salvation, and call
on the LORD’s name.

854
00:55:35,388 --> 00:55:40,308
I will pay my vows to the LORD, yes, in
the presence of all his people.

855
00:55:41,388 --> 00:55:44,548
Precious in the LORD’s sight is the death
of his saints.

856
00:55:45,268 --> 00:55:47,968
LORD, truly I am your servant.

857
00:55:48,588 --> 00:55:51,848
I am your servant, the son of your servant
girl.

858
00:55:52,408 --> 00:55:54,048
You have freed me from my chains.

859
00:55:54,808 --> 00:56:00,328
I will offer to you the sacrifice of
thanksgiving, and will call on the LORD’s name.

860
00:56:00,808 --> 00:56:07,288
I will pay my vows to the LORD, yes,
in the presence of all his people, in the courts

861
00:56:07,328 --> 00:56:10,728
of the LORD’s house, in the middle of you,
Jerusalem.

862
00:56:11,688 --> 00:56:12,908
Praise the LORD!

863
00:56:13,248 --> 00:56:15,628
Psalm one hundred seventeen.

864
00:56:15,668 --> 00:56:17,788
Praise the LORD, all you nations!

865
00:56:17,828 --> 00:56:20,328
Extol him, all you peoples!

866
00:56:21,148 --> 00:56:23,848
For his loving kindness is great towards
us.

867
00:56:24,788 --> 00:56:26,868
The LORD’s faithfulness endures forever.

868
00:56:27,968 --> 00:56:28,868
Praise the LORD!

869
00:56:29,748 --> 00:56:31,808
Psalm one hundred eighteen.

870
00:56:31,848 --> 00:56:37,248
Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,
for his loving kindness endures forever.

871
00:56:37,762 --> 00:56:42,202
Let Israel now say that his loving
kindness endures forever.

872
00:56:43,502 --> 00:56:48,502
Let the house of Aaron now say that his
loving kindness endures forever.

873
00:56:49,442 --> 00:56:55,342
Now let those who fear the LORD say that
his loving kindness endures forever.

874
00:56:55,382 --> 00:56:58,882
Out of my distress, I called on the LORD.

875
00:56:59,382 --> 00:57:01,582
The LORD answered me with freedom.

876
00:57:02,342 --> 00:57:03,882
The LORD is on my side.

877
00:57:04,462 --> 00:57:05,782
I will not be afraid.

878
00:57:06,602 --> 00:57:08,522
What can man do to me?

879
00:57:09,562 --> 00:57:12,762
The LORD is on my side amongst those who
help me.

880
00:57:13,522 --> 00:57:16,882
Therefore I will look in triumph at those
who hate me.

881
00:57:17,262 --> 00:57:21,682
It is better to take refuge in the LORD,
than to put confidence in man.

882
00:57:22,502 --> 00:57:26,882
It is better to take refuge in the LORD,
than to put confidence in princes.

883
00:57:28,262 --> 00:57:32,862
All the nations surrounded me, but in the
LORD’s name I cut them off.

884
00:57:33,322 --> 00:57:36,862
They surrounded me, yes, they surrounded
me.

885
00:57:37,642 --> 00:57:40,222
In the LORD’s name I indeed cut them off.

886
00:57:40,962 --> 00:57:42,562
They surrounded me like bees.

887
00:57:43,282 --> 00:57:45,602
They are quenched like the burning thorns.

888
00:57:46,542 --> 00:57:48,582
In the LORD’s name I cut them off.

889
00:57:49,602 --> 00:57:54,302
You pushed me back hard, to make me fall,
but the LORD helped me.

890
00:57:55,002 --> 00:57:57,082
The LORD is my strength and song.

891
00:57:57,882 --> 00:57:59,202
He has become my salvation.

892
00:57:59,242 --> 00:58:04,142
The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in
the tents of the righteous.

893
00:58:04,942 --> 00:58:07,522
“The right hand of the LORD does
valiantly.

894
00:58:08,362 --> 00:58:10,362
The right hand of the LORD is exalted!

895
00:58:11,342 --> 00:58:13,922
The right hand of the LORD does
valiantly!”

896
00:58:14,602 --> 00:58:18,482
I will not die, but live, and declare the
LORD’s works.

897
00:58:19,482 --> 00:58:24,302
The LORD has punished me severely, but he
has not given me over to death.

898
00:58:25,022 --> 00:58:26,842
Open to me the gates of righteousness.

899
00:58:27,542 --> 00:58:29,522
I will enter into them.

900
00:58:30,002 --> 00:58:32,062
I will give thanks to the LORD.

901
00:58:32,942 --> 00:58:37,502
This is the gate of the LORD; the
righteous will enter into it.

902
00:58:38,182 --> 00:58:43,622
I will give thanks to you, for you have
answered me, and have become my salvation.

903
00:58:44,602 --> 00:58:48,422
The stone which the builders rejected has
become the cornerstone.

904
00:58:49,582 --> 00:58:51,102
This is the LORD’s doing.

905
00:58:51,942 --> 00:58:53,782
It is marvellous in our eyes.

906
00:58:53,822 --> 00:58:56,862
This is the day that the LORD has made.

907
00:58:57,722 --> 00:58:59,782
We will rejoice and be glad in it!

908
00:59:00,182 --> 00:59:02,282
Save us now, we beg you, LORD!

909
00:59:03,062 --> 00:59:06,262
LORD, we beg you, send prosperity now.

910
00:59:06,902 --> 00:59:09,462
Blessed is he who comes in the LORD’s
name!

911
00:59:09,788 --> 00:59:12,228
We have blessed you out of the LORD’s
house.

912
00:59:13,388 --> 00:59:16,448
The LORD is God, and he has given us
light.

913
00:59:17,428 --> 00:59:22,168
Bind the sacrifice with cords, even to the
horns of the altar.

914
00:59:23,468 --> 00:59:26,588
You are my God, and I will give thanks to
you.

915
00:59:27,008 --> 00:59:29,448
You are my God, I will exalt you.

916
00:59:29,488 --> 00:59:35,968
Oh give thanks to the LORD, for he
is good, for his loving kindness endures forever.

917
00:59:37,508 --> 00:59:40,468
Psalm one hundred nineteen.

918
00:59:40,508 --> 00:59:45,568
Blessed are those whose ways are blameless,
who walk according to the LORD’s law.

919
00:59:46,068 --> 00:59:50,628
Blessed are those who keep his statutes,
who seek him with their whole heart.

920
00:59:51,268 --> 00:59:52,688
Yes, they do nothing wrong.

921
00:59:53,488 --> 00:59:54,568
They walk in his ways.

922
00:59:55,668 --> 00:59:59,428
You have commanded your precepts, that we
should fully obey them.

923
01:00:00,428 --> 01:00:03,668
Oh that my ways were steadfast to obey
your statutes!

924
01:00:04,308 --> 01:00:08,728
Then I wouldn’t be disappointed, when I
consider all of your commandments.

925
01:00:09,548 --> 01:00:16,268
I will give thanks to you with uprightness
of heart, when I learn your righteous judgements.

926
01:00:16,308 --> 01:00:17,808
I will observe your statutes.

927
01:00:18,868 --> 01:00:20,568
Don’t utterly forsake me.

928
01:00:21,528 --> 01:00:23,888
How can a young man keep his way pure?

929
01:00:24,708 --> 01:00:26,488
By living according to your word.

930
01:00:26,828 --> 01:00:28,848
With my whole heart I have sought you.

931
01:00:28,888 --> 01:00:31,388
Don’t let me wander from your
commandments.

932
01:00:32,548 --> 01:00:36,828
I have hidden your word in my heart, that
I might not sin against you.

933
01:00:37,708 --> 01:00:39,168
Blessed are you, LORD.

934
01:00:40,068 --> 01:00:41,068
Teach me your statutes.

935
01:00:42,108 --> 01:00:46,188
With my lips, I have declared all the
ordinances of your mouth.

936
01:00:46,828 --> 01:00:51,708
I have rejoiced in the way of your
testimonies, as much as in all riches.

937
01:00:52,908 --> 01:00:56,568
I will meditate on your precepts, and
consider your ways.

938
01:00:57,428 --> 01:00:59,708
I will delight myself in your statutes.

939
01:01:00,848 --> 01:01:02,488
I will not forget your word.

940
01:01:02,968 --> 01:01:04,168
Do good to your servant.

941
01:01:04,968 --> 01:01:07,828
I will live and I will obey your word.

942
01:01:08,428 --> 01:01:12,568
Open my eyes, that I may see wondrous
things out of your law.

943
01:01:13,708 --> 01:01:15,328
I am a stranger on the earth.

944
01:01:16,108 --> 01:01:18,208
Don’t hide your commandments from me.

945
01:01:18,988 --> 01:01:23,668
My soul is consumed with longing for your
ordinances at all times.

946
01:01:24,068 --> 01:01:28,328
You have rebuked the proud who are cursed,
who wander from your commandments.

947
01:01:29,188 --> 01:01:34,028
Take reproach and contempt away from me,
for I have kept your statutes.

948
01:01:34,654 --> 01:01:40,194
Though princes sit and slander me, your
servant will meditate on your statutes.

949
01:01:41,234 --> 01:01:46,294
Indeed your statutes are my delight, and
my counsellors.

950
01:01:46,334 --> 01:01:49,034
My soul is laid low in the dust.

951
01:01:50,074 --> 01:01:52,254
Revive me according to your word!

952
01:01:52,674 --> 01:01:55,494
I declared my ways, and you answered me.

953
01:01:56,434 --> 01:01:57,734
Teach me your statutes.

954
01:01:58,754 --> 01:02:01,714
Let me understand the teaching of your
precepts!

955
01:02:02,494 --> 01:02:05,034
Then I will meditate on your wondrous
works.

956
01:02:06,054 --> 01:02:11,094
My soul is weary with sorrow; strengthen
me according to your word.

957
01:02:11,974 --> 01:02:13,554
Keep me from the way of deceit.

958
01:02:14,234 --> 01:02:15,894
Grant me your law graciously!

959
01:02:16,994 --> 01:02:18,734
I have chosen the way of truth.

960
01:02:19,674 --> 01:02:22,014
I have set your ordinances before me.

961
01:02:22,534 --> 01:02:24,374
I cling to your statutes, LORD.

962
01:02:25,214 --> 01:02:26,494
Don’t let me be disappointed.

963
01:02:27,574 --> 01:02:32,254
I run in the path of your commandments,
for you have set my heart free.

964
01:02:32,974 --> 01:02:35,474
Teach me, LORD, the way of your statutes.

965
01:02:36,434 --> 01:02:38,034
I will keep them to the end.

966
01:02:38,454 --> 01:02:41,614
Give me understanding, and I will keep
your law.

967
01:02:42,394 --> 01:02:45,654
Yes, I will obey it with my whole heart.

968
01:02:46,314 --> 01:02:50,534
Direct me in the path of your
commandments, for I delight in them.

969
01:02:51,534 --> 01:02:55,934
Turn my heart towards your statutes, not
towards selfish gain.

970
01:02:56,954 --> 01:03:00,054
Turn my eyes away from looking at
worthless things.

971
01:03:00,974 --> 01:03:02,434
Revive me in your ways.

972
01:03:02,474 --> 01:03:06,734
Fulfil your promise to your servant, that
you may be feared.

973
01:03:07,374 --> 01:03:11,874
Take away my disgrace that I dread, for
your ordinances are good.

974
01:03:12,834 --> 01:03:15,734
Behold, I long for your precepts!

975
01:03:16,314 --> 01:03:17,874
Revive me in your righteousness.

976
01:03:18,934 --> 01:03:25,394
Let your loving kindness also come to
me, LORD, your salvation, according to your word.

977
01:03:25,834 --> 01:03:30,774
So I will have an answer for him who
reproaches me, for I trust in your word.

978
01:03:31,414 --> 01:03:36,954
Don’t snatch the word of truth out of my
mouth, for I put my hope in your ordinances.

979
01:03:37,974 --> 01:03:42,034
So I will obey your law continually,
forever and ever.

980
01:03:42,734 --> 01:03:46,994
I will walk in liberty, for I have sought
your precepts.

981
01:03:47,854 --> 01:03:52,694
I will also speak of your statutes before
kings, and will not be disappointed.

982
01:03:53,574 --> 01:03:57,374
I will delight myself in your
commandments, because I love them.

983
01:03:58,194 --> 01:04:01,934
I reach out my hands for your
commandments, which I love.

984
01:04:02,914 --> 01:04:04,714
I will meditate on your statutes.

985
01:04:05,335 --> 01:04:09,675
Remember your word to your servant,
because you gave me hope.

986
01:04:10,815 --> 01:04:15,555
This is my comfort in my affliction, for
your word has revived me.

987
01:04:16,715 --> 01:04:21,575
The arrogant mock me excessively, but I
don’t swerve from your law.

988
01:04:21,995 --> 01:04:26,075
I remember your ordinances of old, LORD,
and have comforted myself.

989
01:04:27,075 --> 01:04:32,035
Indignation has taken hold on me, because
of the wicked who forsake your law.

990
01:04:32,875 --> 01:04:36,395
Your statutes have been my songs in the
house where I live.

991
01:04:37,635 --> 01:04:41,915
I have remembered your name, LORD, in the
night, and I obey your law.

992
01:04:42,395 --> 01:04:45,375
This is my way, that I keep your precepts.

993
01:04:46,115 --> 01:04:47,235
The LORD is my portion.

994
01:04:47,975 --> 01:04:49,775
I promised to obey your words.

995
01:04:50,695 --> 01:04:52,915
I sought your favour with my whole heart.

996
01:04:53,835 --> 01:04:56,115
Be merciful to me according to your word.

997
01:04:57,055 --> 01:05:00,935
I considered my ways, and turned my steps
to your statutes.

998
01:05:02,035 --> 01:05:05,315
I will hurry, and not delay, to obey your
commandments.

999
01:05:06,575 --> 01:05:10,735
The ropes of the wicked bind me, but I
won’t forget your law.

1000
01:05:11,455 --> 01:05:16,275
At midnight I will rise to give thanks to
you, because of your righteous ordinances.

1001
01:05:17,435 --> 01:05:23,055
I am a friend of all those who fear you,
of those who observe your precepts.

1002
01:05:23,835 --> 01:05:26,475
The earth is full of your loving kindness,
LORD.

1003
01:05:27,415 --> 01:05:28,395
Teach me your statutes.

1004
01:05:29,095 --> 01:05:32,895
You have treated your servant well,
according to your word, LORD.

1005
01:05:33,775 --> 01:05:37,955
Teach me good judgement and knowledge, for
I believe in your commandments.

1006
01:05:39,135 --> 01:05:43,915
Before I was afflicted, I went astray; but
now I observe your word.

1007
01:05:44,855 --> 01:05:46,615
You are good, and do good.

1008
01:05:47,535 --> 01:05:48,615
Teach me your statutes.

1009
01:05:49,655 --> 01:05:51,835
The proud have smeared a lie upon me.

1010
01:05:52,415 --> 01:05:55,555
With my whole heart, I will keep your
precepts.

1011
01:05:56,335 --> 01:06:00,555
Their heart is as callous as the fat, but
I delight in your law.

1012
01:06:01,595 --> 01:06:05,855
It is good for me that I have been
afflicted, that I may learn your statutes.

1013
01:06:06,575 --> 01:06:11,115
The law of your mouth is better to me than
thousands of pieces of gold and silver.

1014
01:06:11,815 --> 01:06:14,175
Your hands have made me and formed me.

1015
01:06:14,995 --> 01:06:18,115
Give me understanding, that I may learn
your commandments.

1016
01:06:19,435 --> 01:06:25,015
Those who fear you will see me and be
glad, because I have put my hope in your word.

1017
01:06:25,324 --> 01:06:31,604
LORD, I know that your judgements are
righteous, that in faithfulness you have afflicted

1018
01:06:31,644 --> 01:06:32,544
me.

1019
01:06:32,984 --> 01:06:38,844
Please let your loving kindness be for my
comfort, according to your word to your servant.

1020
01:06:39,784 --> 01:06:45,404
Let your tender mercies come to me, that I
may live; for your law is my delight.

1021
01:06:46,344 --> 01:06:50,584
Let the proud be disappointed, for they
have overthrown me wrongfully.

1022
01:06:51,424 --> 01:06:53,604
I will meditate on your precepts.

1023
01:06:54,264 --> 01:06:56,444
Let those who fear you turn to me.

1024
01:06:57,124 --> 01:06:58,484
They will know your statutes.

1025
01:06:59,064 --> 01:07:03,964
Let my heart be blameless towards your
decrees, that I may not be disappointed.

1026
01:07:05,144 --> 01:07:07,304
My soul faints for your salvation.

1027
01:07:08,264 --> 01:07:09,384
I hope in your word.

1028
01:07:10,324 --> 01:07:12,064
My eyes fail for your word.

1029
01:07:13,024 --> 01:07:15,444
I say, “When will you comfort me?”

1030
01:07:16,244 --> 01:07:18,924
For I have become like a wineskin in the
smoke.

1031
01:07:19,684 --> 01:07:21,104
I don’t forget your statutes.

1032
01:07:22,104 --> 01:07:24,004
How many are the days of your servant?

1033
01:07:24,784 --> 01:07:28,224
When will you execute judgement on those
who persecute me?

1034
01:07:28,844 --> 01:07:32,464
The proud have dug pits for me, contrary
to your law.

1035
01:07:33,404 --> 01:07:35,344
All of your commandments are faithful.

1036
01:07:36,344 --> 01:07:37,944
They persecute me wrongfully.

1037
01:07:38,724 --> 01:07:39,624
Help me!

1038
01:07:40,044 --> 01:07:45,124
They had almost wiped me from the earth,
but I didn’t forsake your precepts.

1039
01:07:45,164 --> 01:07:50,984
Preserve my life according to your loving kindness,
so I will obey the statutes of your

1040
01:07:51,024 --> 01:07:51,924
mouth.

1041
01:07:52,304 --> 01:07:55,344
LORD, your word is settled in heaven
forever.

1042
01:07:56,284 --> 01:07:58,184
Your faithfulness is to all generations.

1043
01:07:59,484 --> 01:08:01,984
You have established the earth, and it
remains.

1044
01:08:03,184 --> 01:08:07,024
Your laws remain to this day, for all
things serve you.

1045
01:08:07,804 --> 01:08:12,064
Unless your law had been my delight, I
would have perished in my affliction.

1046
01:08:13,024 --> 01:08:17,664
I will never forget your precepts, for
with them, you have revived me.

1047
01:08:18,404 --> 01:08:19,304
I am yours.

1048
01:08:19,764 --> 01:08:22,544
Save me, for I have sought your precepts.

1049
01:08:22,804 --> 01:08:25,604
The wicked have waited for me, to destroy
me.

1050
01:08:26,544 --> 01:08:28,124
I will consider your statutes.

1051
01:08:29,084 --> 01:08:33,604
I have seen a limit to all perfection, but
your commands are boundless.

1052
01:08:34,404 --> 01:08:35,564
How I love your law!

1053
01:08:36,424 --> 01:08:38,124
It is my meditation all day.

1054
01:08:38,844 --> 01:08:44,524
Your commandments make me wiser than my
enemies, for your commandments are always with

1055
01:08:44,564 --> 01:08:45,304
me.

1056
01:08:45,344 --> 01:08:50,344
I have more understanding than all my
teachers, for your testimonies are my meditation.

1057
01:08:51,013 --> 01:08:55,693
I understand more than the aged, because I
have kept your precepts.

1058
01:08:56,093 --> 01:09:01,353
I have kept my feet from every evil way,
that I might observe your word.

1059
01:09:02,213 --> 01:09:06,553
I have not turned away from your
ordinances, for you have taught me.

1060
01:09:06,593 --> 01:09:11,833
How sweet are your promises to my taste,
more than honey to my mouth!

1061
01:09:12,453 --> 01:09:17,853
Through your precepts, I get understanding;
therefore I hate every false way.

1062
01:09:18,553 --> 01:09:22,533
Your word is a lamp to my feet, and a
light for my path.

1063
01:09:23,533 --> 01:09:28,453
I have sworn, and have confirmed it, that
I will obey your righteous ordinances.

1064
01:09:29,353 --> 01:09:30,773
I am afflicted very much.

1065
01:09:31,653 --> 01:09:34,413
Revive me, LORD, according to your word.

1066
01:09:35,073 --> 01:09:38,613
Accept, I beg you, the willing offerings
of my mouth.

1067
01:09:39,653 --> 01:09:41,493
LORD, teach me your ordinances.

1068
01:09:42,593 --> 01:09:46,993
My soul is continually in my hand, yet I
won’t forget your law.

1069
01:09:47,853 --> 01:09:53,313
The wicked have laid a snare for me, yet I
haven’t gone astray from your precepts.

1070
01:09:53,693 --> 01:09:59,673
I have taken your testimonies as a heritage
forever, for they are the joy of my heart.

1071
01:10:00,453 --> 01:10:05,573
I have set my heart to perform your
statutes forever, even to the end.

1072
01:10:06,633 --> 01:10:10,133
I hate double-minded men, but I love your
law.

1073
01:10:10,573 --> 01:10:12,673
You are my hiding place and my shield.

1074
01:10:13,653 --> 01:10:14,793
I hope in your word.

1075
01:10:14,833 --> 01:10:20,313
Depart from me, you evildoers, that I may
keep the commandments of my God.

1076
01:10:21,173 --> 01:10:24,413
Uphold me according to your word, that I
may live.

1077
01:10:25,433 --> 01:10:27,553
Let me not be ashamed of my hope.

1078
01:10:28,333 --> 01:10:33,713
Hold me up, and I will be safe,
and will have respect for your statutes continually.

1079
01:10:34,613 --> 01:10:39,813
You reject all those who stray from your
statutes, for their deceit is in vain.

1080
01:10:40,533 --> 01:10:44,113
You put away all the wicked of the earth
like dross.

1081
01:10:44,953 --> 01:10:46,973
Therefore I love your testimonies.

1082
01:10:48,053 --> 01:10:50,113
My flesh trembles for fear of you.

1083
01:10:50,853 --> 01:10:53,213
I am afraid of your judgements.

1084
01:10:53,253 --> 01:10:55,153
I have done what is just and righteous.

1085
01:10:56,113 --> 01:10:57,973
Don’t leave me to my oppressors.

1086
01:10:58,613 --> 01:11:01,253
Ensure your servant’s well-being.

1087
01:11:01,293 --> 01:11:03,193
Don’t let the proud oppress me.

1088
01:11:03,913 --> 01:11:08,133
My eyes fail looking for your salvation,
for your righteous word.

1089
01:11:09,043 --> 01:11:12,093
Deal with your servant according to your
loving kindness.

1090
01:11:12,553 --> 01:11:13,593
Teach me your statutes.

1091
01:11:14,493 --> 01:11:15,513
I am your servant.

1092
01:11:15,855 --> 01:11:19,755
Give me understanding, that I may know
your testimonies.

1093
01:11:21,135 --> 01:11:24,495
It is time to act, LORD, for they break
your law.

1094
01:11:25,515 --> 01:11:31,055
Therefore I love your commandments more
than gold, yes, more than pure gold.

1095
01:11:32,155 --> 01:11:35,155
Therefore I consider all of your precepts
to be right.

1096
01:11:36,135 --> 01:11:37,655
I hate every false way.

1097
01:11:38,455 --> 01:11:42,495
Your testimonies are wonderful, therefore
my soul keeps them.

1098
01:11:43,175 --> 01:11:45,535
The entrance of your words gives light.

1099
01:11:46,415 --> 01:11:48,315
It gives understanding to the simple.

1100
01:11:49,355 --> 01:11:54,055
I opened my mouth wide and panted, for I
longed for your commandments.

1101
01:11:54,095 --> 01:12:00,435
Turn to me, and have mercy on me, as you
always do to those who love your name.

1102
01:12:01,015 --> 01:12:03,315
Establish my footsteps in your word.

1103
01:12:04,195 --> 01:12:06,935
Don’t let any iniquity have dominion over
me.

1104
01:12:06,975 --> 01:12:12,455
Redeem me from the oppression of man, so I
will observe your precepts.

1105
01:12:12,975 --> 01:12:15,075
Make your face shine on your servant.

1106
01:12:15,875 --> 01:12:16,975
Teach me your statutes.

1107
01:12:17,695 --> 01:12:22,235
Streams of tears run down my eyes, because
they don’t observe your law.

1108
01:12:22,955 --> 01:12:24,115
You are righteous, LORD.

1109
01:12:24,815 --> 01:12:26,115
Your judgements are upright.

1110
01:12:27,135 --> 01:12:29,315
You have commanded your statutes in
righteousness.

1111
01:12:30,435 --> 01:12:31,575
They are fully trustworthy.

1112
01:12:32,595 --> 01:12:37,495
My zeal wears me out, because my enemies
ignore your words.

1113
01:12:38,575 --> 01:12:42,755
Your promises have been thoroughly tested,
and your servant loves them.

1114
01:12:43,595 --> 01:12:45,235
I am small and despised.

1115
01:12:46,255 --> 01:12:47,735
I don’t forget your precepts.

1116
01:12:48,695 --> 01:12:51,115
Your righteousness is an everlasting
righteousness.

1117
01:12:52,275 --> 01:12:53,255
Your law is truth.

1118
01:12:54,655 --> 01:12:56,715
Trouble and anguish have taken hold of me.

1119
01:12:57,655 --> 01:12:59,135
Your commandments are my delight.

1120
01:12:59,175 --> 01:13:02,095
Your testimonies are righteous forever.

1121
01:13:02,755 --> 01:13:05,395
Give me understanding, that I may live.

1122
01:13:06,355 --> 01:13:08,215
I have called with my whole heart.

1123
01:13:08,875 --> 01:13:09,815
Answer me, LORD!

1124
01:13:10,595 --> 01:13:11,795
I will keep your statutes.

1125
01:13:12,815 --> 01:13:13,935
I have called to you.

1126
01:13:14,655 --> 01:13:15,555
Save me!

1127
01:13:16,255 --> 01:13:17,755
I will obey your statutes.

1128
01:13:18,795 --> 01:13:21,175
I rise before dawn and cry for help.

1129
01:13:21,995 --> 01:13:23,575
I put my hope in your words.

1130
01:13:24,475 --> 01:13:29,775
My eyes stay open through the night
watches, that I might meditate on your word.

1131
01:13:30,775 --> 01:13:33,295
Hear my voice according to your loving
kindness.

1132
01:13:34,115 --> 01:13:36,875
Revive me, LORD, according to your
ordinances.

1133
01:13:37,975 --> 01:13:40,495
They draw near who follow after
wickedness.

1134
01:13:41,195 --> 01:13:42,555
They are far from your law.

1135
01:13:43,415 --> 01:13:44,315
You are near, LORD.

1136
01:13:45,035 --> 01:13:46,635
All your commandments are truth.

1137
01:13:47,085 --> 01:13:52,345
Of old I have known from your testimonies,
that you have founded them forever.

1138
01:13:53,705 --> 01:13:59,065
Consider my affliction, and deliver me,
for I don’t forget your law.

1139
01:14:00,205 --> 01:14:02,485
Plead my cause, and redeem me!

1140
01:14:02,525 --> 01:14:04,945
Revive me according to your promise.

1141
01:14:06,305 --> 01:14:10,705
Salvation is far from the wicked, for they
don’t seek your statutes.

1142
01:14:11,465 --> 01:14:13,565
Great are your tender mercies, LORD.

1143
01:14:14,465 --> 01:14:16,625
Revive me according to your ordinances.

1144
01:14:17,845 --> 01:14:20,285
Many are my persecutors and my
adversaries.

1145
01:14:21,525 --> 01:14:23,565
I haven’t swerved from your testimonies.

1146
01:14:24,325 --> 01:14:28,685
I look at the faithless with loathing,
because they don’t observe your word.

1147
01:14:29,925 --> 01:14:32,305
Consider how I love your precepts.

1148
01:14:32,865 --> 01:14:36,005
Revive me, LORD, according to your loving
kindness.

1149
01:14:36,945 --> 01:14:38,905
All of your words are truth.

1150
01:14:38,945 --> 01:14:42,625
Every one of your righteous ordinances
endures forever.

1151
01:14:44,005 --> 01:14:50,185
Princes have persecuted me without a cause, but
my heart stands in awe of your words.

1152
01:14:51,365 --> 01:14:55,225
I rejoice at your word, as one who finds
great plunder.

1153
01:14:56,045 --> 01:14:57,765
I hate and abhor falsehood.

1154
01:14:58,825 --> 01:14:59,745
I love your law.

1155
01:15:00,685 --> 01:15:05,445
Seven times a day, I praise you, because
of your righteous ordinances.

1156
01:15:06,425 --> 01:15:09,345
Those who love your law have great peace.

1157
01:15:10,185 --> 01:15:11,985
Nothing causes them to stumble.

1158
01:15:12,465 --> 01:15:14,425
I have hoped for your salvation, LORD.

1159
01:15:15,125 --> 01:15:16,505
I have done your commandments.

1160
01:15:17,605 --> 01:15:19,425
My soul has observed your testimonies.

1161
01:15:20,505 --> 01:15:21,405
I love them exceedingly.

1162
01:15:22,765 --> 01:15:28,165
I have obeyed your precepts and your
testimonies, for all my ways are before you.

1163
01:15:29,025 --> 01:15:31,165
Let my cry come before you, LORD.

1164
01:15:32,005 --> 01:15:34,685
Give me understanding according to your
word.

1165
01:15:35,445 --> 01:15:37,785
Let my supplication come before you.

1166
01:15:38,605 --> 01:15:40,565
Deliver me according to your word.

1167
01:15:41,205 --> 01:15:45,205
Let my lips utter praise, for you teach me
your statutes.

1168
01:15:46,425 --> 01:15:51,245
Let my tongue sing of your word, for all
your commandments are righteousness.

1169
01:15:52,305 --> 01:15:57,565
Let your hand be ready to help me, for I
have chosen your precepts.

1170
01:15:57,885 --> 01:16:00,005
I have longed for your salvation, LORD.

1171
01:16:00,945 --> 01:16:02,445
Your law is my delight.

1172
01:16:03,205 --> 01:16:06,105
Let my soul live, that I may praise you.

1173
01:16:07,165 --> 01:16:08,945
Let your ordinances help me.

1174
01:16:09,785 --> 01:16:12,185
I have gone astray like a lost sheep.

1175
01:16:13,285 --> 01:16:16,565
Seek your servant, for I don’t forget your
commandments.

1176
01:16:17,325 --> 01:16:19,765
Psalm one hundred twenty.

1177
01:16:19,805 --> 01:16:22,445
In my distress, I cried to the LORD.

1178
01:16:22,847 --> 01:16:23,747
He answered me.

1179
01:16:24,887 --> 01:16:29,687
Deliver my soul, LORD, from lying lips,
from a deceitful tongue.

1180
01:16:30,767 --> 01:16:36,447
What will be given to you, and what will
be done more to you, you deceitful tongue?

1181
01:16:37,047 --> 01:16:40,287
Sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals of
juniper.

1182
01:16:41,507 --> 01:16:47,127
Woe is me, that I live in Meshech, that I
dwell amongst the tents of Kedar!

1183
01:16:47,607 --> 01:16:52,047
My soul has had her dwelling too long with
him who hates peace.

1184
01:16:53,287 --> 01:16:57,407
I am for peace, but when I speak, they are
for war.

1185
01:16:58,647 --> 01:17:01,547
Psalm one hundred twenty-one.

1186
01:17:01,587 --> 01:17:03,527
I will lift up my eyes to the hills.

1187
01:17:04,127 --> 01:17:05,547
Where does my help come from?

1188
01:17:06,287 --> 01:17:09,947
My help comes from the LORD, who made
heaven and earth.

1189
01:17:10,567 --> 01:17:12,627
He will not allow your foot to be moved.

1190
01:17:13,507 --> 01:17:15,867
He who keeps you will not slumber.

1191
01:17:16,667 --> 01:17:21,267
Behold, he who keeps Israel will neither
slumber nor sleep.

1192
01:17:21,787 --> 01:17:22,687
The LORD is your keeper.

1193
01:17:23,687 --> 01:17:25,907
The LORD is your shade on your right hand.

1194
01:17:26,807 --> 01:17:30,567
The sun will not harm you by day, nor the
moon by night.

1195
01:17:31,567 --> 01:17:33,607
The LORD will keep you from all evil.

1196
01:17:34,367 --> 01:17:35,487
He will keep your soul.

1197
01:17:36,527 --> 01:17:43,187
The LORD will keep your going out and
your coming in, from this time forward, and forever

1198
01:17:43,227 --> 01:17:44,247
more.

1199
01:17:44,287 --> 01:17:46,467
Psalm one hundred twenty-two.

1200
01:17:46,507 --> 01:17:50,807
I was glad when they said to me, “Let’s go
to the LORD’s house!”

1201
01:17:51,807 --> 01:17:54,667
Our feet are standing within your gates,
Jerusalem!

1202
01:17:55,567 --> 01:18:02,047
Jerusalem is built as a city that is
compact together, where the tribes go up, even

1203
01:18:02,087 --> 01:18:07,767
the LORD’s tribes, according to an ordinance
for Israel, to give thanks to the LORD’s

1204
01:18:07,807 --> 01:18:08,327
name.

1205
01:18:08,367 --> 01:18:12,787
For there are set thrones for judgement,
the thrones of David’s house.

1206
01:18:13,907 --> 01:18:15,427
Pray for the peace of Jerusalem.

1207
01:18:16,187 --> 01:18:17,967
Those who love you will prosper.

1208
01:18:18,947 --> 01:18:23,147
Peace be within your walls, and prosperity
within your palaces.

1209
01:18:24,127 --> 01:18:29,987
For my brothers’ and companions’ sakes, I
will now say, “Peace be within you.”

1210
01:18:30,287 --> 01:18:34,587
For the sake of the house of the LORD our
God, I will seek your good.

1211
01:18:35,587 --> 01:18:38,067
Psalm one hundred twenty-three.

1212
01:18:38,107 --> 01:18:41,967
I lift up my eyes to you, you who sit in
the heavens.

1213
01:18:42,397 --> 01:18:49,057
Behold, as the eyes of servants look to the
hand of their master, as the eyes of a maid

1214
01:18:49,097 --> 01:18:55,877
to the hand of her mistress, so our eyes
look to the LORD, our God, until

1215
01:18:55,917 --> 01:18:57,357
he has mercy on us.

1216
01:18:57,677 --> 01:19:03,777
Have mercy on us, LORD, have mercy on us,
for we have endured much contempt.

1217
01:19:04,717 --> 01:19:10,657
Our soul is exceedingly filled with the scoffing
of those who are at ease, with the contempt

1218
01:19:10,697 --> 01:19:11,597
of the proud.

1219
01:19:12,817 --> 01:19:14,977
Psalm one hundred twenty-four.

1220
01:19:15,017 --> 01:19:21,517
If it had not been the LORD who was on our
side, let Israel now say, if it had not

1221
01:19:21,557 --> 01:19:27,097
been the LORD who was on our side, when
men rose up against us, then they would have

1222
01:19:27,137 --> 01:19:33,397
swallowed us up alive, when their wrath
was kindled against us, then the waters would

1223
01:19:33,437 --> 01:19:37,657
have overwhelmed us, the stream would have
gone over our soul.

1224
01:19:38,837 --> 01:19:41,517
Then the proud waters would have gone over
our soul.

1225
01:19:42,537 --> 01:19:46,877
Blessed be the LORD, who has not given us
as a prey to their teeth.

1226
01:19:47,637 --> 01:19:51,457
Our soul has escaped like a bird out of
the fowler’s snare.

1227
01:19:52,157 --> 01:19:54,837
The snare is broken, and we have escaped.

1228
01:19:55,637 --> 01:19:59,737
Our help is in the LORD’s name, who made
heaven and earth.

1229
01:19:59,777 --> 01:20:02,977
Psalm one hundred twenty-five.

1230
01:20:03,017 --> 01:20:09,797
Those who trust in the LORD are as
Mount Zion, which can’t be moved, but remains forever.

1231
01:20:10,557 --> 01:20:16,097
As the mountains surround Jerusalem, so the
LORD surrounds his people from this time

1232
01:20:16,137 --> 01:20:18,957
forward and forever more.

1233
01:20:18,997 --> 01:20:24,737
For the sceptre of wickedness won’t remain
over the allotment of the righteous, so that

1234
01:20:24,777 --> 01:20:27,537
the righteous won’t use their hands to do
evil.

1235
01:20:28,017 --> 01:20:33,097
Do good, LORD, to those who are good, to
those who are upright in their hearts.

1236
01:20:34,217 --> 01:20:39,377
But as for those who turn away to their
crooked ways, The LORD will lead them away with

1237
01:20:39,417 --> 01:20:40,717
the workers of iniquity.

1238
01:20:41,617 --> 01:20:42,957
Peace be on Israel.

1239
01:20:44,517 --> 01:20:46,677
Psalm one hundred twenty-six.

1240
01:20:46,717 --> 01:20:51,937
When the LORD brought back those who returned
to Zion, we were like those who dream.

1241
01:20:52,637 --> 01:20:56,997
Then our mouth was filled with laughter,
and our tongue with singing.

1242
01:20:57,997 --> 01:21:02,897
Then they said amongst the nations, “The
LORD has done great things for them.”

1243
01:21:03,257 --> 01:21:06,757
The LORD has done great things for us, and
we are glad.

1244
01:21:07,209 --> 01:21:11,989
Restore our fortunes again, LORD, like the
streams in the Negev.

1245
01:21:12,649 --> 01:21:15,749
Those who sow in tears will reap in joy.

1246
01:21:17,109 --> 01:21:23,649
He who goes out weeping, carrying seed
for sowing, will certainly come again with joy,

1247
01:21:24,509 --> 01:21:25,829
carrying his sheaves.

1248
01:21:26,189 --> 01:21:28,589
Psalm one hundred twenty-seven.

1249
01:21:28,629 --> 01:21:33,529
Unless the LORD builds the house, they who
build it labour in vain.

1250
01:21:34,769 --> 01:21:39,489
Unless the LORD watches over the city, the
watchman guards it in vain.

1251
01:21:40,149 --> 01:21:46,769
It is vain for you to rise up early, to
stay up late, eating the bread of toil, for he

1252
01:21:46,809 --> 01:21:48,629
gives sleep to his loved ones.

1253
01:21:49,429 --> 01:21:52,309
Behold, children are a heritage of the
LORD.

1254
01:21:53,229 --> 01:21:55,209
The fruit of the womb is his reward.

1255
01:21:56,289 --> 01:22:00,909
As arrows in the hand of a mighty man, so
are the children of youth.

1256
01:22:01,769 --> 01:22:04,809
Happy is the man who has his quiver full
of them.

1257
01:22:05,129 --> 01:22:08,789
They won’t be disappointed when they speak
with their enemies in the gate.

1258
01:22:09,409 --> 01:22:12,329
Psalm one hundred twenty-eight.

1259
01:22:12,369 --> 01:22:16,889
Blessed is everyone who fears the LORD,
who walks in his ways.

1260
01:22:18,049 --> 01:22:20,129
For you will eat the labour of your hands.

1261
01:22:20,729 --> 01:22:23,949
You will be happy, and it will be well
with you.

1262
01:22:24,469 --> 01:22:30,349
Your wife will be as a fruitful vine
in the innermost parts of your house, your children

1263
01:22:30,489 --> 01:22:32,569
like olive shoots around your table.

1264
01:22:33,529 --> 01:22:37,489
Behold, this is how the man who fears the
LORD is blessed.

1265
01:22:38,109 --> 01:22:43,789
May the LORD bless you out of Zion, and
may you see the good of Jerusalem all the days

1266
01:22:43,829 --> 01:22:44,729
of your life.

1267
01:22:45,149 --> 01:22:48,089
Yes, may you see your children’s children.

1268
01:22:49,129 --> 01:22:50,449
Peace be upon Israel.

1269
01:22:51,609 --> 01:22:54,149
Psalm one hundred twenty-nine.

1270
01:22:54,189 --> 01:22:57,749
Many times they have afflicted me from my
youth up.

1271
01:22:58,589 --> 01:23:05,089
Let Israel now say: many times they have
afflicted me from my youth up, yet they

1272
01:23:05,129 --> 01:23:06,929
have not prevailed against me.

1273
01:23:07,909 --> 01:23:09,989
The ploughers ploughed on my back.

1274
01:23:10,589 --> 01:23:12,149
They made their furrows long.

1275
01:23:13,229 --> 01:23:14,329
The LORD is righteous.

1276
01:23:15,249 --> 01:23:17,409
He has cut apart the cords of the wicked.

1277
01:23:18,309 --> 01:23:23,109
Let them be disappointed and turned
backward, all those who hate Zion.

1278
01:23:23,829 --> 01:23:30,109
Let them be as the grass on the
housetops, which withers before it grows up, with which

1279
01:23:30,149 --> 01:23:35,689
the reaper doesn’t fill his hand, nor he
who binds sheaves, his bosom.

1280
01:23:35,955 --> 01:23:40,875
Neither do those who go by say, “The
blessing of the LORD be on you.

1281
01:23:41,655 --> 01:23:43,775
We bless you in the LORD’s name.”

1282
01:23:45,095 --> 01:23:48,015
Psalm one hundred thirty.

1283
01:23:48,055 --> 01:23:50,495
Out of the depths I have cried to you,
LORD.

1284
01:23:51,555 --> 01:23:52,955
Lord, hear my voice.

1285
01:23:54,095 --> 01:23:57,235
Let your ears be attentive to the voice of
my petitions.

1286
01:23:58,155 --> 01:24:02,795
If you, LORD, kept a record of sins, Lord,
who could stand?

1287
01:24:03,515 --> 01:24:07,515
But there is forgiveness with you,
therefore you are feared.

1288
01:24:08,635 --> 01:24:09,815
I wait for the LORD.

1289
01:24:10,495 --> 01:24:11,455
My soul waits.

1290
01:24:12,235 --> 01:24:13,495
I hope in his word.

1291
01:24:13,995 --> 01:24:20,135
My soul longs for the Lord more than
watchmen long for the morning, more than watchmen

1292
01:24:20,175 --> 01:24:21,075
for the morning.

1293
01:24:21,555 --> 01:24:26,195
Israel, hope in the LORD, for there is
loving kindness with the LORD.

1294
01:24:27,055 --> 01:24:28,915
Abundant redemption is with him.

1295
01:24:28,955 --> 01:24:32,335
He will redeem Israel from all their sins.

1296
01:24:33,315 --> 01:24:35,695
Psalm one hundred thirty-one.

1297
01:24:35,735 --> 01:24:42,655
LORD, my heart isn’t arrogant, nor my eyes
lofty; nor do I concern myself with

1298
01:24:42,695 --> 01:24:46,035
great matters, or things too wonderful for
me.

1299
01:24:47,055 --> 01:24:53,915
Surely I have stilled and quieted my soul,
like a weaned child with his mother, like

1300
01:24:53,955 --> 01:24:56,495
a weaned child is my soul within me.

1301
01:24:56,835 --> 01:25:02,995
Israel, hope in the LORD, from this time
forward and forever more.

1302
01:25:03,035 --> 01:25:05,535
Psalm one hundred thirty-two.

1303
01:25:05,575 --> 01:25:12,235
LORD, remember David and all his affliction,
how he swore to the LORD, and vowed

1304
01:25:12,275 --> 01:25:19,135
to the Mighty One of Jacob: “Surely I will
not come into the structure of my house, nor

1305
01:25:19,175 --> 01:25:26,375
go up into my bed; I will not give
sleep to my eyes, or slumber to my eyelids, until

1306
01:25:26,415 --> 01:25:31,195
I find out a place for the LORD, a
dwelling for the Mighty One of Jacob.”

1307
01:25:32,335 --> 01:25:35,635
Behold, we heard of it in Ephrathah.

1308
01:25:35,675 --> 01:25:38,515
We found it in the field of Jaar.

1309
01:25:38,555 --> 01:25:40,435
“We will go into his dwelling place.

1310
01:25:41,135 --> 01:25:42,935
We will worship at his footstool.”

1311
01:25:43,615 --> 01:25:48,735
Arise, LORD, into your resting place, you,
and the ark of your strength.

1312
01:25:49,595 --> 01:25:51,815
Let your priests be clothed with
righteousness.

1313
01:25:52,695 --> 01:25:55,015
Let your saints shout for joy!

1314
01:25:55,635 --> 01:26:00,535
For your servant David’s sake, don’t turn
away the face of your anointed one.

1315
01:26:01,295 --> 01:26:03,415
The LORD has sworn to David in truth.

1316
01:26:04,075 --> 01:26:09,195
He will not turn from it: “I will set the
fruit of your body on your throne.

1317
01:26:09,596 --> 01:26:16,136
If your children will keep my covenant, my
testimony that I will teach them, their children

1318
01:26:16,176 --> 01:26:20,176
also will sit on your throne forever
more.”

1319
01:26:20,216 --> 01:26:22,296
For the LORD has chosen Zion.

1320
01:26:23,356 --> 01:26:25,676
He has desired it for his habitation.

1321
01:26:26,116 --> 01:26:27,896
“This is my resting place forever.

1322
01:26:29,116 --> 01:26:32,036
I will live here, for I have desired it.

1323
01:26:32,616 --> 01:26:34,596
I will abundantly bless her provision.

1324
01:26:35,696 --> 01:26:38,016
I will satisfy her poor with bread.

1325
01:26:38,956 --> 01:26:41,796
I will also clothe her priests with
salvation.

1326
01:26:43,136 --> 01:26:45,396
Her saints will shout aloud for joy.

1327
01:26:46,636 --> 01:26:49,156
I will make the horn of David to bud
there.

1328
01:26:50,076 --> 01:26:52,376
I have ordained a lamp for my anointed.

1329
01:26:53,116 --> 01:26:58,996
I will clothe his enemies with shame, but
on himself, his crown will shine.”

1330
01:27:00,636 --> 01:27:03,516
Psalm one hundred thirty-three.

1331
01:27:03,556 --> 01:27:08,176
See how good and how pleasant it is for
brothers to live together in unity!

1332
01:27:08,756 --> 01:27:15,296
It is like the precious oil on the head,
that ran down on the beard, even Aaron’s

1333
01:27:15,336 --> 01:27:22,176
beard, that came down on the edge of his
robes, like the dew of Hermon, that comes down

1334
01:27:22,216 --> 01:27:28,796
on the hills of Zion; for there the LORD
gives the blessing, even life forever

1335
01:27:28,836 --> 01:27:29,616
more.

1336
01:27:29,656 --> 01:27:31,956
Psalm one hundred thirty-four.

1337
01:27:31,996 --> 01:27:32,896
Look!

1338
01:27:33,216 --> 01:27:38,896
Praise the LORD, all you servants of the
LORD, who stand by night in the LORD’s house!

1339
01:27:39,816 --> 01:27:41,676
Lift up your hands in the sanctuary.

1340
01:27:42,896 --> 01:27:43,816
Praise the LORD!

1341
01:27:44,276 --> 01:27:48,816
May the LORD bless you from Zion, even he
who made heaven and earth.

1342
01:27:49,876 --> 01:27:52,776
Psalm one hundred thirty-five.

1343
01:27:52,816 --> 01:27:53,716
Praise the LORD!

1344
01:27:54,136 --> 01:27:55,256
Praise the LORD’s name!

1345
01:27:55,996 --> 01:28:02,076
Praise him, you servants of the LORD, you
who stand in the LORD’s house, in the courts

1346
01:28:02,116 --> 01:28:03,256
of our God’s house.

1347
01:28:04,436 --> 01:28:07,156
Praise the LORD, for the LORD is good.

1348
01:28:08,116 --> 01:28:11,116
Sing praises to his name, for that is
pleasant.

1349
01:28:11,716 --> 01:28:16,776
For the LORD has chosen Jacob for himself,
Israel for his own possession.

1350
01:28:17,716 --> 01:28:21,916
For I know that the LORD is great, that
our Lord is above all gods.

1351
01:28:23,056 --> 01:28:29,416
Whatever the LORD pleased, that he has done,
in heaven and in earth, in the seas and

1352
01:28:29,456 --> 01:28:30,376
in all deeps.

1353
01:28:31,276 --> 01:28:34,596
He causes the clouds to rise from the ends
of the earth.

1354
01:28:35,396 --> 01:28:36,936
He makes lightnings with the rain.

1355
01:28:37,716 --> 01:28:40,116
He brings the wind out of his treasuries.

1356
01:28:40,499 --> 01:28:44,799
He struck the firstborn of Egypt, both of
man and animal.

1357
01:28:45,899 --> 01:28:52,659
He sent signs and wonders into the middle
of you, Egypt, on Pharaoh, and on all

1358
01:28:52,699 --> 01:28:53,599
his servants.

1359
01:28:54,019 --> 01:29:01,819
He struck many nations, and killed mighty
kings— Sihon king of the Amorites, Og

1360
01:29:01,859 --> 01:29:08,759
king of Bashan, and all the kingdoms of
Canaan— and gave their land for a heritage, a

1361
01:29:08,799 --> 01:29:11,039
heritage to Israel, his people.

1362
01:29:11,459 --> 01:29:17,599
Your name, LORD, endures forever; your
renown, LORD, throughout all generations.

1363
01:29:18,599 --> 01:29:22,539
For the LORD will judge his people and
have compassion on his servants.

1364
01:29:23,719 --> 01:29:28,659
The idols of the nations are silver and
gold, the work of men’s hands.

1365
01:29:29,359 --> 01:29:31,779
They have mouths, but they can’t speak.

1366
01:29:32,559 --> 01:29:34,719
They have eyes, but they can’t see.

1367
01:29:35,239 --> 01:29:40,439
They have ears, but they can’t hear,
neither is there any breath in their mouths.

1368
01:29:41,439 --> 01:29:46,879
Those who make them will be like them,
yes, everyone who trusts in them.

1369
01:29:47,819 --> 01:29:50,159
House of Israel, praise the LORD!

1370
01:29:50,839 --> 01:29:52,679
House of Aaron, praise the LORD!

1371
01:29:53,219 --> 01:29:55,219
House of Levi, praise the LORD!

1372
01:29:56,099 --> 01:29:58,539
You who fear the LORD, praise the LORD!

1373
01:29:59,079 --> 01:30:02,539
Blessed be the LORD from Zion, who dwells
in Jerusalem.

1374
01:30:03,439 --> 01:30:04,339
Praise the LORD!

1375
01:30:05,299 --> 01:30:07,499
Psalm one hundred thirty-six.

1376
01:30:07,539 --> 01:30:13,019
Give thanks to the LORD, for he is good,
for his loving kindness endures forever.

1377
01:30:13,979 --> 01:30:18,979
Give thanks to the God of gods, for his
loving kindness endures forever.

1378
01:30:19,498 --> 01:30:26,038
Give thanks to the Lord of lords, for
his loving kindness endures forever; to him who

1379
01:30:26,078 --> 01:30:33,118
alone does great wonders, for his loving
kindness endures forever; to him who by understanding

1380
01:30:33,158 --> 01:30:39,318
made the heavens, for his loving kindness
endures forever; to him who spread out the

1381
01:30:39,358 --> 01:30:45,898
earth above the waters, for his loving
kindness endures forever; to him who made the

1382
01:30:45,938 --> 01:30:53,158
great lights, for his loving kindness endures
forever; the sun to rule by day, for

1383
01:30:53,198 --> 01:30:59,338
his loving kindness endures forever; the moon and
stars to rule by night, for his loving

1384
01:30:59,378 --> 01:31:05,878
kindness endures forever; to him who
struck down the Egyptian firstborn, for his

1385
01:31:05,918 --> 01:31:11,478
loving kindness endures forever; and brought out
Israel from amongst them, for his loving

1386
01:31:11,518 --> 01:31:18,218
kindness endures forever; with a strong hand,
and with an outstretched arm, for his loving

1387
01:31:18,258 --> 01:31:25,318
kindness endures forever; to him who divided
the Red Sea apart, for his loving kindness

1388
01:31:25,358 --> 01:31:31,058
endures forever; and made Israel to pass through
the middle of it, for his loving kindness

1389
01:31:31,098 --> 01:31:37,818
endures forever; but overthrew Pharaoh and his army
in the Red Sea, for his loving kindness

1390
01:31:37,858 --> 01:31:44,218
endures forever; to him who led his
people through the wilderness, for his loving kindness

1391
01:31:44,258 --> 01:31:50,578
endures forever; to him who struck great
kings, for his loving kindness endures forever;

1392
01:31:50,618 --> 01:31:57,458
and killed mighty kings, for his loving
kindness endures forever; Sihon

1393
01:31:57,498 --> 01:32:04,158
king of the Amorites, for his loving
kindness endures forever; Og king of Bashan,

1394
01:32:04,198 --> 01:32:10,418
for his loving kindness endures forever; and
gave their land as an inheritance, for his

1395
01:32:10,458 --> 01:32:16,398
loving kindness endures forever; even a heritage
to Israel his servant, for his loving

1396
01:32:16,438 --> 01:32:22,698
kindness endures forever; who remembered us in
our low estate, for his loving kindness

1397
01:32:22,738 --> 01:32:28,678
endures forever; and has delivered us from
our adversaries, for his loving kindness endures

1398
01:32:28,718 --> 01:32:34,578
forever; who gives food to every creature,
for his loving kindness endures forever.

1399
01:32:35,358 --> 01:32:40,778
Oh give thanks to the God of heaven, for
his loving kindness endures forever.

1400
01:32:42,238 --> 01:32:44,938
Psalm one hundred thirty-seven.

1401
01:32:44,978 --> 01:32:48,798
By the rivers of Babylon, there we sat
down.

1402
01:32:49,538 --> 01:32:53,318
Yes, we wept, when we remembered Zion.

1403
01:32:53,358 --> 01:32:57,598
On the willows in that land, we hung up
our harps.

1404
01:32:57,958 --> 01:33:02,838
For there, those who led us captive asked
us for songs.

1405
01:33:02,878 --> 01:33:09,538
Those who tormented us demanded songs of
joy: “Sing us one of the songs

1406
01:33:09,578 --> 01:33:10,478
of Zion!”

1407
01:33:11,518 --> 01:33:14,458
How can we sing the LORD’s song in a
foreign land?

1408
01:33:15,598 --> 01:33:20,758
If I forget you, Jerusalem, let my right
hand forget its skill.

1409
01:33:21,438 --> 01:33:27,718
Let my tongue stick to the roof of my
mouth if I don’t remember you, if I don’t prefer

1410
01:33:27,758 --> 01:33:29,898
Jerusalem above my chief joy.

1411
01:33:31,038 --> 01:33:37,218
Remember, LORD, against the children of Edom
in the day of Jerusalem, who said, “Raze

1412
01:33:37,258 --> 01:33:37,558
it!

1413
01:33:37,598 --> 01:33:39,938
Raze it even to its foundation!”

1414
01:33:40,978 --> 01:33:47,658
Daughter of Babylon, doomed to destruction, he
will be happy who repays you, as

1415
01:33:47,698 --> 01:33:48,818
you have done to us.

1416
01:33:49,698 --> 01:33:54,918
Happy shall he be, who takes and dashes
your little ones against the rock.

1417
01:33:55,478 --> 01:33:56,538
Psalm one hundred thirty-eight.

1418
01:33:56,578 --> 01:34:00,738
I will give you thanks with my whole
heart.

1419
01:34:01,638 --> 01:34:04,918
Before the gods, I will sing praises to
you.

1420
01:34:05,398 --> 01:34:11,058
I will bow down towards your holy temple,
and give thanks to your Name for your loving

1421
01:34:11,098 --> 01:34:17,758
kindness and for your truth; for you have
exalted your Name and your Word above all.

1422
01:34:18,558 --> 01:34:21,498
In the day that I called, you answered me.

1423
01:34:21,878 --> 01:34:24,678
You encouraged me with strength in my
soul.

1424
01:34:25,218 --> 01:34:30,318
All the kings of the earth will give
you thanks, LORD, for they have heard the words

1425
01:34:30,358 --> 01:34:31,258
of your mouth.

1426
01:34:32,338 --> 01:34:37,898
Yes, they will sing of the ways of the
LORD, for the LORD’s glory is great!

1427
01:34:38,918 --> 01:34:44,998
For though the LORD is high, yet he looks
after the lowly; but he knows the proud from

1428
01:34:45,038 --> 01:34:45,938
afar.

1429
01:34:46,118 --> 01:34:49,638
Though I walk in the middle of trouble,
you will revive me.

1430
01:34:50,198 --> 01:34:53,878
You will stretch out your hand against the
wrath of my enemies.

1431
01:34:54,838 --> 01:34:56,458
Your right hand will save me.

1432
01:34:57,318 --> 01:35:00,098
The LORD will fulfil that which concerns
me.

1433
01:35:00,438 --> 01:35:03,298
Your loving kindness, LORD, endures
forever.

1434
01:35:04,438 --> 01:35:06,778
Don’t forsake the works of your own hands.

1435
01:35:07,638 --> 01:35:08,538
Psalm one hundred thirty-nine.

1436
01:35:09,487 --> 01:35:12,827
LORD, you have searched me, and you know
me.

1437
01:35:13,487 --> 01:35:16,467
You know my sitting down and my rising up.

1438
01:35:17,007 --> 01:35:19,207
You perceive my thoughts from afar.

1439
01:35:20,247 --> 01:35:25,947
You search out my path and my lying down,
and are acquainted with all my ways.

1440
01:35:26,227 --> 01:35:31,807
For there is not a word on my tongue, but
behold, LORD, you know it altogether.

1441
01:35:32,727 --> 01:35:34,907
You hem me in behind and before.

1442
01:35:35,707 --> 01:35:37,247
You laid your hand on me.

1443
01:35:37,877 --> 01:35:39,587
This knowledge is beyond me.

1444
01:35:40,207 --> 01:35:41,107
It’s lofty.

1445
01:35:41,487 --> 01:35:42,527
I can’t attain it.

1446
01:35:43,187 --> 01:35:44,907
Where could I go from your Spirit?

1447
01:35:45,687 --> 01:35:47,707
Or where could I flee from your presence?

1448
01:35:47,747 --> 01:35:50,887
If I ascend up into heaven, you are there.

1449
01:35:51,727 --> 01:35:55,887
If I make my bed in Sheol, behold, you are
there!

1450
01:35:56,667 --> 01:36:02,767
If I take the wings of the dawn, and
settle in the uttermost parts of the sea, even there

1451
01:36:02,807 --> 01:36:06,547
your hand will lead me, and your right
hand will hold me.

1452
01:36:07,247 --> 01:36:10,847
If I say, “Surely the darkness will
overwhelm me.

1453
01:36:11,367 --> 01:36:17,027
The light around me will be night,” even
the darkness doesn’t hide from you, but the

1454
01:36:17,067 --> 01:36:18,787
night shines as the day.

1455
01:36:19,767 --> 01:36:21,707
The darkness is like light to you.

1456
01:36:22,567 --> 01:36:24,507
For you formed my inmost being.

1457
01:36:25,467 --> 01:36:27,527
You knit me together in my mother’s womb.

1458
01:36:28,127 --> 01:36:32,607
I will give thanks to you, for I am
fearfully and wonderfully made.

1459
01:36:33,247 --> 01:36:34,387
Your works are wonderful.

1460
01:36:35,387 --> 01:36:37,447
My soul knows that very well.

1461
01:36:38,227 --> 01:36:44,547
My frame wasn’t hidden from you, when I
was made in secret, woven together in the depths

1462
01:36:44,587 --> 01:36:45,487
of the earth.

1463
01:36:46,267 --> 01:36:47,847
Your eyes saw my body.

1464
01:36:48,247 --> 01:36:54,027
In your book they were all written, the days
that were ordained for me, when as yet there

1465
01:36:54,067 --> 01:36:54,967
were none of them.

1466
01:36:55,227 --> 01:36:57,627
How precious to me are your thoughts, God!

1467
01:36:58,297 --> 01:37:00,787
How vast is their sum!

1468
01:37:00,827 --> 01:37:04,247
If I would count them, they are more in
number than the sand.

1469
01:37:05,087 --> 01:37:07,727
When I wake up, I am still with you.

1470
01:37:08,367 --> 01:37:11,207
If only you, God, would kill the wicked.

1471
01:37:12,027 --> 01:37:14,307
Get away from me, you bloodthirsty men!

1472
01:37:15,147 --> 01:37:17,107
For they speak against you wickedly.

1473
01:37:17,707 --> 01:37:19,587
Your enemies take your name in vain.

1474
01:37:20,667 --> 01:37:23,227
LORD, don’t I hate those who hate you?

1475
01:37:23,987 --> 01:37:27,067
Am I not grieved with those who rise up
against you?

1476
01:37:27,907 --> 01:37:29,507
I hate them with perfect hatred.

1477
01:37:30,347 --> 01:37:31,627
They have become my enemies.

1478
01:37:32,927 --> 01:37:34,947
Search me, God, and know my heart.

1479
01:37:35,747 --> 01:37:37,507
Try me, and know my thoughts.

1480
01:37:37,972 --> 01:37:43,412
See if there is any wicked way in me, and
lead me in the everlasting way.

1481
01:37:44,592 --> 01:37:47,052
Psalm one hundred forty.

1482
01:37:47,092 --> 01:37:49,832
Deliver me, LORD, from evil men.

1483
01:37:50,672 --> 01:37:55,532
Preserve me from violent men: those who
devise mischief in their hearts.

1484
01:37:56,672 --> 01:37:59,712
They continually gather themselves
together for war.

1485
01:38:00,532 --> 01:38:02,592
They have sharpened their tongues like a
serpent.

1486
01:38:03,832 --> 01:38:05,752
Viper’s poison is under their lips.

1487
01:38:05,792 --> 01:38:07,892
Selah.

1488
01:38:07,932 --> 01:38:10,952
LORD, keep me from the hands of the
wicked.

1489
01:38:11,412 --> 01:38:15,712
Preserve me from the violent men who have
determined to trip my feet.

1490
01:38:16,752 --> 01:38:22,232
The proud have hidden a snare for me, they
have spread the cords of a net by the path.

1491
01:38:22,912 --> 01:38:24,372
They have set traps for me.

1492
01:38:24,412 --> 01:38:26,312
Selah.

1493
01:38:26,352 --> 01:38:29,172
I said to the LORD, “You are my God.”

1494
01:38:30,072 --> 01:38:32,492
Listen to the cry of my petitions, LORD.

1495
01:38:32,532 --> 01:38:39,172
LORD, the Lord, the strength of my salvation,
you have covered my head in the day

1496
01:38:39,212 --> 01:38:40,112
of battle.

1497
01:38:40,632 --> 01:38:43,332
LORD, don’t grant the desires of the
wicked.

1498
01:38:44,072 --> 01:38:48,272
Don’t let their evil plans succeed, or
they will become proud.

1499
01:38:48,312 --> 01:38:50,672
Selah.

1500
01:38:50,712 --> 01:38:57,092
As for the head of those who surround me,
let the mischief of their own lips cover them.

1501
01:38:57,892 --> 01:39:00,152
Let burning coals fall on them.

1502
01:39:00,192 --> 01:39:06,272
Let them be thrown into the fire, into
miry pits, from where they never rise.

1503
01:39:06,952 --> 01:39:09,952
An evil speaker won’t be established in
the earth.

1504
01:39:10,892 --> 01:39:14,152
Evil will hunt the violent man to
overthrow him.

1505
01:39:15,292 --> 01:39:20,752
I know that the LORD will maintain the
cause of the afflicted, and justice for the needy.

1506
01:39:21,692 --> 01:39:24,472
Surely the righteous will give thanks to
your name.

1507
01:39:25,272 --> 01:39:27,512
The upright will dwell in your presence.

1508
01:39:28,332 --> 01:39:31,012
Psalm one hundred forty-one.

1509
01:39:31,052 --> 01:39:33,712
LORD, I have called on you.

1510
01:39:34,372 --> 01:39:35,332
Come to me quickly!

1511
01:39:36,412 --> 01:39:38,672
Listen to my voice when I call to you.

1512
01:39:39,552 --> 01:39:45,872
Let my prayer be set before you like incense;
the lifting up of my hands like the evening

1513
01:39:45,912 --> 01:39:46,812
sacrifice.

1514
01:39:47,292 --> 01:39:49,732
Set a watch, LORD, before my mouth.

1515
01:39:50,392 --> 01:39:51,952
Keep the door of my lips.

1516
01:39:52,832 --> 01:39:58,952
Don’t incline my heart to any evil thing,
to practise deeds of wickedness with men who

1517
01:39:58,992 --> 01:39:59,952
work iniquity.

1518
01:40:00,612 --> 01:40:02,812
Don’t let me eat of their delicacies.

1519
01:40:03,302 --> 01:40:10,022
Let the righteous strike me, it is kindness;
let him reprove me, it is like oil

1520
01:40:10,062 --> 01:40:16,702
on the head; don’t let my head refuse it;
Yet my prayer is always against evil

1521
01:40:16,742 --> 01:40:17,642
deeds.

1522
01:40:18,402 --> 01:40:21,542
Their judges are thrown down by the sides
of the rock.

1523
01:40:22,422 --> 01:40:25,742
They will hear my words, for they are well
spoken.

1524
01:40:26,382 --> 01:40:32,002
“As when one ploughs and breaks up the
earth, our bones are scattered at the mouth of

1525
01:40:32,042 --> 01:40:32,942
Sheol.”

1526
01:40:33,522 --> 01:40:36,482
For my eyes are on you, LORD, the Lord.

1527
01:40:37,322 --> 01:40:38,782
I take refuge in you.

1528
01:40:39,522 --> 01:40:41,562
Don’t leave my soul destitute.

1529
01:40:41,862 --> 01:40:47,182
Keep me from the snare which they have laid
for me, from the traps of the workers of

1530
01:40:47,222 --> 01:40:48,122
iniquity.

1531
01:40:48,262 --> 01:40:52,922
Let the wicked fall together into their
own nets while I pass by.

1532
01:40:54,202 --> 01:40:56,802
Psalm one hundred forty-two.

1533
01:40:56,842 --> 01:40:59,362
I cry with my voice to the LORD.

1534
01:41:00,182 --> 01:41:02,942
With my voice, I ask the LORD for mercy.

1535
01:41:03,422 --> 01:41:05,462
I pour out my complaint before him.

1536
01:41:06,162 --> 01:41:07,462
I tell him my troubles.

1537
01:41:08,422 --> 01:41:12,422
When my spirit was overwhelmed within me,
you knew my route.

1538
01:41:13,162 --> 01:41:17,122
On the path in which I walk, they have
hidden a snare for me.

1539
01:41:17,902 --> 01:41:23,302
Look on my right, and see; for there is no
one who is concerned for me.

1540
01:41:24,222 --> 01:41:25,922
Refuge has fled from me.

1541
01:41:26,682 --> 01:41:28,282
No one cares for my soul.

1542
01:41:29,422 --> 01:41:30,562
I cried to you, LORD.

1543
01:41:31,322 --> 01:41:35,802
I said, “You are my refuge, my portion in
the land of the living.”

1544
01:41:36,362 --> 01:41:39,562
Listen to my cry, for I am in desperate
need.

1545
01:41:40,542 --> 01:41:44,582
Deliver me from my persecutors, for they
are too strong for me.

1546
01:41:45,382 --> 01:41:49,502
Bring my soul out of prison, that I may
give thanks to your name.

1547
01:41:50,562 --> 01:41:54,002
The righteous will surround me, for you
will be good to me.

1548
01:41:54,962 --> 01:41:57,922
Psalm one hundred forty-three.

1549
01:41:57,962 --> 01:41:58,882
Hear my prayer, LORD.

1550
01:41:59,582 --> 01:42:00,602
Listen to my petitions.

1551
01:42:01,882 --> 01:42:04,982
In your faithfulness and righteousness,
relieve me.

1552
01:42:06,002 --> 01:42:11,662
Don’t enter into judgement with your servant, for
in your sight no man living is righteous.

1553
01:42:12,502 --> 01:42:14,602
For the enemy pursues my soul.

1554
01:42:15,422 --> 01:42:17,702
He has struck my life down to the ground.

1555
01:42:18,422 --> 01:42:23,162
He has made me live in dark places, as
those who have been long dead.

1556
01:42:24,022 --> 01:42:26,882
Therefore my spirit is overwhelmed within
me.

1557
01:42:27,502 --> 01:42:29,162
My heart within me is desolate.

1558
01:42:30,242 --> 01:42:31,842
I remember the days of old.

1559
01:42:32,522 --> 01:42:34,462
I meditate on all your doings.

1560
01:42:35,082 --> 01:42:37,022
I contemplate the work of your hands.

1561
01:42:37,470 --> 01:42:39,310
I spread out my hands to you.

1562
01:42:40,210 --> 01:42:43,710
My soul thirsts for you, like a parched
land.

1563
01:42:43,750 --> 01:42:46,210
Selah.

1564
01:42:46,250 --> 01:42:47,910
Hurry to answer me, LORD.

1565
01:42:48,890 --> 01:42:49,830
My spirit fails.

1566
01:42:50,950 --> 01:42:56,150
Don’t hide your face from me, so that I
don’t become like those who go down into the

1567
01:42:56,190 --> 01:42:57,090
pit.

1568
01:42:57,430 --> 01:43:02,610
Cause me to hear your loving kindness in
the morning, for I trust in you.

1569
01:43:02,650 --> 01:43:08,530
Cause me to know the way in which I should
walk, for I lift up my soul to you.

1570
01:43:09,530 --> 01:43:12,050
Deliver me, LORD, from my enemies.

1571
01:43:13,210 --> 01:43:14,850
I flee to you to hide me.

1572
01:43:15,750 --> 01:43:18,910
Teach me to do your will, for you are my
God.

1573
01:43:19,390 --> 01:43:20,450
Your Spirit is good.

1574
01:43:21,430 --> 01:43:23,410
Lead me in the land of uprightness.

1575
01:43:24,270 --> 01:43:26,910
Revive me, LORD, for your name’s sake.

1576
01:43:26,950 --> 01:43:30,770
In your righteousness, bring my soul out
of trouble.

1577
01:43:31,730 --> 01:43:37,930
In your loving kindness, cut off my enemies,
and destroy all those who afflict my soul,

1578
01:43:38,610 --> 01:43:39,850
For I am your servant.

1579
01:43:41,250 --> 01:43:43,550
Psalm one hundred forty-four.

1580
01:43:43,590 --> 01:43:50,990
Blessed be the LORD, my rock, who trains my
hands to war, and my fingers to battle— my

1581
01:43:51,030 --> 01:43:58,090
loving kindness, my fortress, my high
tower, my deliverer, my shield, and

1582
01:43:58,130 --> 01:44:02,370
he in whom I take refuge, who subdues my
people under me.

1583
01:44:03,190 --> 01:44:06,650
LORD, what is man, that you care for him?

1584
01:44:07,210 --> 01:44:09,790
Or the son of man, that you think of him?

1585
01:44:10,730 --> 01:44:11,970
Man is like a breath.

1586
01:44:12,850 --> 01:44:15,390
His days are like a shadow that passes
away.

1587
01:44:16,450 --> 01:44:18,970
Part your heavens, LORD, and come down.

1588
01:44:19,850 --> 01:44:21,990
Touch the mountains, and they will smoke.

1589
01:44:22,850 --> 01:44:25,110
Throw out lightning, and scatter them.

1590
01:44:25,950 --> 01:44:28,030
Send out your arrows, and rout them.

1591
01:44:28,710 --> 01:44:35,710
Stretch out your hand from above, rescue me,
and deliver me out of great waters, out

1592
01:44:35,750 --> 01:44:42,050
of the hands of foreigners, whose mouths speak
deceit, whose right hand is a right hand

1593
01:44:42,090 --> 01:44:42,990
of falsehood.

1594
01:44:43,550 --> 01:44:45,990
I will sing a new song to you, God.

1595
01:44:46,410 --> 01:44:50,250
On a ten-stringed lyre, I will sing
praises to you.

1596
01:44:50,790 --> 01:44:57,150
You are he who gives salvation to kings,
who rescues David, his servant, from the deadly

1597
01:44:57,190 --> 01:44:58,090
sword.

1598
01:44:58,730 --> 01:45:04,290
Rescue me, and deliver me out of the hands
of foreigners, whose mouths speak deceit,

1599
01:45:05,130 --> 01:45:07,370
whose right hand is a right hand of
falsehood.

1600
01:45:08,350 --> 01:45:14,110
Then our sons will be like well-nurtured
plants, our daughters like pillars carved to

1601
01:45:14,150 --> 01:45:15,050
adorn a palace.

1602
01:45:15,548 --> 01:45:19,328
Our barns are full, filled with all kinds
of provision.

1603
01:45:20,808 --> 01:45:24,748
Our sheep produce thousands and ten
thousands in our fields.

1604
01:45:25,868 --> 01:45:27,988
Our oxen will pull heavy loads.

1605
01:45:29,208 --> 01:45:34,768
There is no breaking in, and no going
away, and no outcry in our streets.

1606
01:45:35,448 --> 01:45:38,048
Happy are the people who are in such a
situation.

1607
01:45:39,028 --> 01:45:41,568
Happy are the people whose God is the
LORD.

1608
01:45:42,908 --> 01:45:45,608
Psalm one hundred forty-five.

1609
01:45:45,648 --> 01:45:48,448
I will exalt you, my God, the King.

1610
01:45:49,528 --> 01:45:52,068
I will praise your name forever and ever.

1611
01:45:52,768 --> 01:45:54,428
Every day I will praise you.

1612
01:45:55,248 --> 01:45:57,888
I will extol your name forever and ever.

1613
01:45:58,708 --> 01:46:01,828
Great is the LORD, and greatly to be
praised!

1614
01:46:02,948 --> 01:46:04,628
His greatness is unsearchable.

1615
01:46:05,348 --> 01:46:10,748
One generation will commend your works to
another, and will declare your mighty acts.

1616
01:46:11,628 --> 01:46:16,808
I will meditate on the glorious majesty of
your honour, on your wondrous works.

1617
01:46:17,868 --> 01:46:20,888
Men will speak of the might of your
awesome acts.

1618
01:46:21,728 --> 01:46:23,128
I will declare your greatness.

1619
01:46:23,888 --> 01:46:28,608
They will utter the memory of your
great goodness, and will sing of your righteousness.

1620
01:46:29,868 --> 01:46:35,948
The LORD is gracious, merciful, slow to
anger, and of great loving kindness.

1621
01:46:36,948 --> 01:46:38,928
The LORD is good to all.

1622
01:46:39,548 --> 01:46:42,348
His tender mercies are over all his works.

1623
01:46:42,888 --> 01:46:45,408
All your works will give thanks to you,
LORD.

1624
01:46:46,008 --> 01:46:47,708
Your saints will extol you.

1625
01:46:48,428 --> 01:46:54,308
They will speak of the glory of your
kingdom, and talk about your power, to make known

1626
01:46:54,348 --> 01:46:59,768
to the sons of men his mighty acts, the
glory of the majesty of his kingdom.

1627
01:47:00,248 --> 01:47:02,428
Your kingdom is an everlasting kingdom.

1628
01:47:03,138 --> 01:47:05,948
Your dominion endures throughout all
generations.

1629
01:47:06,928 --> 01:47:11,608
The LORD is faithful in all his words, and
loving in all his deeds.

1630
01:47:12,988 --> 01:47:18,428
The LORD upholds all who fall, and raises
up all those who are bowed down.

1631
01:47:19,368 --> 01:47:21,308
The eyes of all wait for you.

1632
01:47:22,028 --> 01:47:24,248
You give them their food in due season.

1633
01:47:24,828 --> 01:47:29,368
You open your hand, and satisfy the desire
of every living thing.

1634
01:47:29,968 --> 01:47:34,748
The LORD is righteous in all his ways, and
gracious in all his works.

1635
01:47:35,548 --> 01:47:41,608
The LORD is near to all those who call on
him, to all who call on him in truth.

1636
01:47:42,648 --> 01:47:45,748
He will fulfil the desire of those who
fear him.

1637
01:47:45,971 --> 01:47:49,451
He also will hear their cry, and will save
them.

1638
01:47:50,711 --> 01:47:56,051
The LORD preserves all those who love him,
but he will destroy all the wicked.

1639
01:47:57,111 --> 01:47:59,851
My mouth will speak the praise of the
LORD.

1640
01:48:00,291 --> 01:48:04,171
Let all flesh bless his holy name forever
and ever.

1641
01:48:04,631 --> 01:48:07,431
Psalm one hundred forty-six.

1642
01:48:07,471 --> 01:48:08,531
Praise the LORD!

1643
01:48:08,911 --> 01:48:10,511
Praise the LORD, my soul.

1644
01:48:11,131 --> 01:48:13,791
While I live, I will praise the LORD.

1645
01:48:14,651 --> 01:48:18,431
I will sing praises to my God as long as I
exist.

1646
01:48:19,691 --> 01:48:25,151
Don’t put your trust in princes, in a son
of man in whom there is no help.

1647
01:48:26,211 --> 01:48:29,371
His spirit departs, and he returns to the
earth.

1648
01:48:30,291 --> 01:48:32,891
In that very day, his thoughts perish.

1649
01:48:33,631 --> 01:48:40,211
Happy is he who has the God of Jacob for
his help, whose hope is in the LORD, his God,

1650
01:48:41,051 --> 01:48:47,211
who made heaven and earth, the sea, and
all that is in them; who keeps truth forever;

1651
01:48:48,271 --> 01:48:52,911
who executes justice for the oppressed;
who gives food to the hungry.

1652
01:48:54,011 --> 01:48:55,331
The LORD frees the prisoners.

1653
01:48:56,191 --> 01:48:58,331
The LORD opens the eyes of the blind.

1654
01:48:59,271 --> 01:49:02,071
The LORD raises up those who are bowed
down.

1655
01:49:03,031 --> 01:49:04,551
The LORD loves the righteous.

1656
01:49:05,551 --> 01:49:07,251
The LORD preserves the foreigners.

1657
01:49:07,951 --> 01:49:14,031
He upholds the fatherless and widow, but he
turns the way of the wicked upside down.

1658
01:49:15,091 --> 01:49:20,411
The LORD will reign forever; your God, O
Zion, to all generations.

1659
01:49:21,411 --> 01:49:22,311
Praise the LORD!

1660
01:49:22,771 --> 01:49:25,951
Psalm one hundred forty-seven.

1661
01:49:25,991 --> 01:49:32,671
Praise the LORD, for it is good to sing
praises to our God; for it is pleasant and fitting

1662
01:49:32,711 --> 01:49:33,731
to praise him.

1663
01:49:34,791 --> 01:49:36,351
The LORD builds up Jerusalem.

1664
01:49:37,451 --> 01:49:40,291
He gathers together the outcasts of
Israel.

1665
01:49:40,831 --> 01:49:44,391
He heals the broken in heart, and binds up
their wounds.

1666
01:49:45,231 --> 01:49:46,831
He counts the number of the stars.

1667
01:49:47,811 --> 01:49:49,711
He calls them all by their names.

1668
01:49:50,511 --> 01:49:53,231
Great is our Lord, and mighty in power.

1669
01:49:54,231 --> 01:49:55,871
His understanding is infinite.

1670
01:49:56,891 --> 01:49:58,451
The LORD upholds the humble.

1671
01:49:59,351 --> 01:50:01,491
He brings the wicked down to the ground.

1672
01:50:02,491 --> 01:50:04,291
Sing to the LORD with thanksgiving.

1673
01:50:04,971 --> 01:50:11,771
Sing praises on the harp to our God,
who covers the sky with clouds, who prepares rain

1674
01:50:11,811 --> 01:50:15,531
for the earth, who makes grass grow on the
mountains.

1675
01:50:16,691 --> 01:50:21,091
He provides food for the livestock, and
for the young ravens when they call.

1676
01:50:21,486 --> 01:50:23,966
He doesn’t delight in the strength of the
horse.

1677
01:50:24,866 --> 01:50:27,386
He takes no pleasure in the legs of a man.

1678
01:50:28,526 --> 01:50:34,386
The LORD takes pleasure in those who fear
him, in those who hope in his loving kindness.

1679
01:50:35,466 --> 01:50:36,886
Praise the LORD, Jerusalem!

1680
01:50:38,006 --> 01:50:39,166
Praise your God, Zion!

1681
01:50:40,226 --> 01:50:42,466
For he has strengthened the bars of your
gates.

1682
01:50:43,306 --> 01:50:45,366
He has blessed your children within you.

1683
01:50:46,106 --> 01:50:47,706
He makes peace in your borders.

1684
01:50:48,626 --> 01:50:51,426
He fills you with the finest of the wheat.

1685
01:50:51,466 --> 01:50:53,886
He sends out his commandment to the earth.

1686
01:50:54,826 --> 01:50:56,546
His word runs very swiftly.

1687
01:50:57,186 --> 01:51:01,106
He gives snow like wool, and scatters
frost like ashes.

1688
01:51:02,006 --> 01:51:04,306
He hurls down his hail like pebbles.

1689
01:51:05,006 --> 01:51:06,586
Who can stand before his cold?

1690
01:51:07,366 --> 01:51:09,986
He sends out his word, and melts them.

1691
01:51:10,886 --> 01:51:14,066
He causes his wind to blow, and the waters
flow.

1692
01:51:14,966 --> 01:51:19,766
He shows his word to Jacob, his statutes
and his ordinances to Israel.

1693
01:51:20,286 --> 01:51:22,586
He has not done this for just any nation.

1694
01:51:23,326 --> 01:51:24,766
They don’t know his ordinances.

1695
01:51:25,726 --> 01:51:26,626
Praise the LORD!

1696
01:51:27,266 --> 01:51:29,786
Psalm one hundred forty-eight.

1697
01:51:29,826 --> 01:51:30,726
Praise the LORD!

1698
01:51:31,346 --> 01:51:32,866
Praise the LORD from the heavens!

1699
01:51:33,626 --> 01:51:34,606
Praise him in the heights!

1700
01:51:35,306 --> 01:51:36,746
Praise him, all his angels!

1701
01:51:37,506 --> 01:51:38,806
Praise him, all his army!

1702
01:51:39,626 --> 01:51:40,826
Praise him, sun and moon!

1703
01:51:41,546 --> 01:51:43,406
Praise him, all you shining stars!

1704
01:51:44,126 --> 01:51:48,326
Praise him, you heavens of heavens, you
waters that are above the heavens.

1705
01:51:48,886 --> 01:51:53,546
Let them praise the LORD’s name, for he
commanded, and they were created.

1706
01:51:54,646 --> 01:51:57,446
He has also established them forever and
ever.

1707
01:51:58,166 --> 01:52:00,986
He has made a decree which will not pass
away.

1708
01:52:01,786 --> 01:52:07,526
Praise the LORD from the earth, you
great sea creatures, and all depths, lightning and

1709
01:52:07,566 --> 01:52:14,246
hail, snow and clouds, stormy wind,
fulfilling his word, mountains and all hills,

1710
01:52:15,086 --> 01:52:21,586
fruit trees and all cedars, wild animals
and all livestock, small creatures and flying

1711
01:52:21,626 --> 01:52:28,406
birds, kings of the earth and all peoples,
princes and all judges of the earth, both

1712
01:52:28,446 --> 01:52:31,406
young men and maidens, old men and
children.

1713
01:52:32,056 --> 01:52:36,206
Let them praise the LORD’s name, for his
name alone is exalted.

1714
01:52:37,206 --> 01:52:39,546
His glory is above the earth and the
heavens.

1715
01:52:39,953 --> 01:52:46,473
He has lifted up the horn of his people,
the praise of all his saints, even of the

1716
01:52:46,513 --> 01:52:49,533
children of Israel, a people near to him.

1717
01:52:50,693 --> 01:52:51,593
Praise the LORD!

1718
01:52:52,453 --> 01:52:55,213
Psalm one hundred forty-nine.

1719
01:52:55,253 --> 01:52:56,193
Praise the LORD!

1720
01:52:56,653 --> 01:53:01,333
Sing to the LORD a new song, his praise in
the assembly of the saints.

1721
01:53:02,553 --> 01:53:05,233
Let Israel rejoice in him who made them.

1722
01:53:05,273 --> 01:53:08,713
Let the children of Zion be joyful in
their King.

1723
01:53:09,813 --> 01:53:11,873
Let them praise his name in the dance!

1724
01:53:12,733 --> 01:53:16,433
Let them sing praises to him with
tambourine and harp!

1725
01:53:16,973 --> 01:53:19,393
For the LORD takes pleasure in his people.

1726
01:53:20,073 --> 01:53:21,753
He crowns the humble with salvation.

1727
01:53:23,093 --> 01:53:25,853
Let the saints rejoice in honour.

1728
01:53:25,893 --> 01:53:28,173
Let them sing for joy on their beds.

1729
01:53:28,513 --> 01:53:34,113
May the high praises of God be in
their mouths, and a two-edged sword in their hand,

1730
01:53:34,153 --> 01:53:40,493
to execute vengeance on the nations, and
punishments on the peoples; to bind their kings

1731
01:53:40,533 --> 01:53:47,693
with chains, and their nobles with fetters of
iron; to execute on them the written judgement.

1732
01:53:47,733 --> 01:53:50,213
All his saints have this honour.

1733
01:53:50,253 --> 01:53:51,153
Praise the LORD!

1734
01:53:51,873 --> 01:53:53,993
Psalm one hundred fifty.

1735
01:53:54,033 --> 01:53:54,933
Praise the LORD!

1736
01:53:55,313 --> 01:53:56,893
Praise God in his sanctuary!

1737
01:53:57,873 --> 01:54:01,153
Praise him in his heavens for his acts of
power!

1738
01:54:01,933 --> 01:54:03,833
Praise him for his mighty acts!

1739
01:54:04,673 --> 01:54:07,033
Praise him according to his excellent
greatness!

1740
01:54:08,033 --> 01:54:09,973
Praise him with the sounding of the
trumpet!

1741
01:54:10,773 --> 01:54:12,593
Praise him with harp and lyre!

1742
01:54:13,273 --> 01:54:15,393
Praise him with tambourine and dancing!

1743
01:54:16,253 --> 01:54:18,733
Praise him with stringed instruments and
flute!

1744
01:54:19,373 --> 01:54:21,553
Praise him with loud cymbals!

1745
01:54:21,593 --> 01:54:24,373
Praise him with resounding cymbals!

1746
01:54:24,413 --> 01:54:27,253
Let everything that has breath praise the
LORD!

1747
01:54:27,913 --> 01:54:28,813
Praise the LORD!

1748
01:54:29,513 --> 01:54:30,513
Proverbs, chapter one.

1749
01:54:31,387 --> 01:54:37,947
The proverbs of Solomon, the son of David,
king of Israel: to know wisdom

1750
01:54:37,987 --> 01:54:44,487
and instruction; to discern the words
of understanding; to receive instruction in wise

1751
01:54:44,527 --> 01:54:52,107
dealing, in righteousness, justice, and equity;
to give prudence to the simple, knowledge

1752
01:54:52,287 --> 01:54:58,187
and discretion to the young man— that the
wise man may hear, and increase in learning;

1753
01:54:58,847 --> 01:55:04,607
that the man of understanding may attain
to sound counsel; to understand a proverb and

1754
01:55:04,647 --> 01:55:07,727
parables, the words and riddles of the
wise.

1755
01:55:08,407 --> 01:55:13,887
The fear of the LORD is the beginning
of knowledge, but the foolish despise wisdom and

1756
01:55:13,927 --> 01:55:14,827
instruction.

1757
01:55:15,367 --> 01:55:21,427
My son, listen to your father’s
instruction, and don’t forsake your mother’s teaching;

1758
01:55:22,467 --> 01:55:26,887
for they will be a garland to grace your
head, and chains around your neck.

1759
01:55:27,527 --> 01:55:31,227
My son, if sinners entice you, don’t
consent.

1760
01:55:32,507 --> 01:55:34,167
If they say, “Come with us.

1761
01:55:34,667 --> 01:55:36,487
Let’s lie in wait for blood.

1762
01:55:37,027 --> 01:55:40,427
Let’s lurk secretly for the innocent
without cause.

1763
01:55:41,547 --> 01:55:47,987
Let’s swallow them up alive like Sheol, and
whole, like those who go down into the pit.

1764
01:55:48,627 --> 01:55:50,927
We’ll find all valuable wealth.

1765
01:55:51,647 --> 01:55:53,307
We’ll fill our houses with plunder.

1766
01:55:54,407 --> 01:55:56,387
You shall cast your lot amongst us.

1767
01:55:57,067 --> 01:56:02,727
We’ll all have one purse”— my son, don’t
walk on the path with them.

1768
01:56:03,347 --> 01:56:07,067
Keep your foot from their path, for their
feet run to evil.

1769
01:56:07,887 --> 01:56:09,347
They hurry to shed blood.

1770
01:56:10,107 --> 01:56:15,667
For the net is spread in vain in the sight
of any bird; but these lay in wait for their

1771
01:56:15,707 --> 01:56:16,607
own blood.

1772
01:56:17,187 --> 01:56:19,467
They lurk secretly for their own lives.

1773
01:56:20,127 --> 01:56:23,647
So are the ways of everyone who is greedy
for gain.

1774
01:56:24,727 --> 01:56:26,767
It takes away the life of its owners.

1775
01:56:27,307 --> 01:56:29,327
Wisdom calls aloud in the street.

1776
01:56:30,107 --> 01:56:32,507
She utters her voice in the public
squares.

1777
01:56:33,467 --> 01:56:35,787
She calls at the head of noisy places.

1778
01:56:36,327 --> 01:56:42,487
At the entrance of the city gates, she
utters her words: “How long, you simple ones,

1779
01:56:43,007 --> 01:56:44,187
will you love simplicity?

1780
01:56:45,547 --> 01:56:50,627
How long will mockers delight themselves
in mockery, and fools hate knowledge?

1781
01:56:51,047 --> 01:56:53,247
Turn at my reproof.

1782
01:56:53,867 --> 01:56:56,627
Behold, I will pour out my spirit on you.

1783
01:56:57,347 --> 01:56:59,467
I will make known my words to you.

1784
01:56:59,703 --> 01:57:06,303
Because I have called, and you have refused;
I have stretched out my hand, and no one

1785
01:57:06,343 --> 01:57:13,283
has paid attention; but you have ignored all
my counsel, and wanted none of my reproof;

1786
01:57:13,703 --> 01:57:16,483
I also will laugh at your disaster.

1787
01:57:17,323 --> 01:57:24,563
I will mock when calamity overtakes you,
when calamity overtakes you like a storm, when

1788
01:57:24,603 --> 01:57:30,423
your disaster comes on like a whirlwind,
when distress and anguish come on you.

1789
01:57:31,303 --> 01:57:34,783
Then they will call on me, but I will not
answer.

1790
01:57:35,303 --> 01:57:40,923
They will seek me diligently, but they
will not find me, because they hated knowledge,

1791
01:57:40,963 --> 01:57:43,683
and didn’t choose the fear of the LORD.

1792
01:57:44,423 --> 01:57:46,183
They wanted none of my counsel.

1793
01:57:47,043 --> 01:57:49,323
They despised all my reproof.

1794
01:57:49,523 --> 01:57:54,823
Therefore they will eat of the fruit of their
own way, and be filled with their own schemes.

1795
01:57:55,603 --> 01:57:58,363
For the backsliding of the simple will
kill them.

1796
01:57:59,223 --> 01:58:02,223
The careless ease of fools will destroy
them.

1797
01:58:03,203 --> 01:58:09,963
But whoever listens to me will dwell securely,
and will be at ease, without fear of harm.”

1798
01:58:10,463 --> 01:58:12,543
Proverbs, chapter two.

1799
01:58:12,583 --> 01:58:19,143
My son, if you will receive my words, and
store up my commandments within you, so

1800
01:58:19,183 --> 01:58:25,683
as to turn your ear to wisdom, and apply
your heart to understanding; yes, if

1801
01:58:25,723 --> 01:58:31,443
you call out for discernment, and lift up
your voice for understanding; if you seek her

1802
01:58:31,483 --> 01:58:37,603
as silver, and search for her as for
hidden treasures; then you will understand the fear

1803
01:58:37,643 --> 01:58:40,643
of the LORD, and find the knowledge of
God.

1804
01:58:41,663 --> 01:58:43,283
For the LORD gives wisdom.

1805
01:58:43,973 --> 01:58:46,863
Out of his mouth comes knowledge and
understanding.

1806
01:58:47,923 --> 01:58:50,283
He lays up sound wisdom for the upright.

1807
01:58:51,143 --> 01:58:56,783
He is a shield to those who walk in
integrity, that he may guard the paths of justice,

1808
01:58:56,823 --> 01:58:59,383
and preserve the way of his saints.

1809
01:59:00,523 --> 01:59:05,963
Then you will understand righteousness and
justice, equity and every good path.

1810
01:59:06,883 --> 01:59:08,963
For wisdom will enter into your heart.

1811
01:59:09,503 --> 01:59:11,423
Knowledge will be pleasant to your soul.

1812
01:59:12,143 --> 01:59:13,903
Discretion will watch over you.

1813
01:59:14,204 --> 01:59:20,624
Understanding will keep you, to deliver you from
the way of evil, from the men who speak

1814
01:59:20,664 --> 01:59:27,084
perverse things, who forsake the paths of
uprightness, to walk in the ways of darkness,

1815
01:59:28,064 --> 01:59:34,404
who rejoice to do evil, and delight in
the perverseness of evil, who are crooked in their

1816
01:59:34,444 --> 01:59:41,004
ways, and wayward in their paths, to deliver
you from the strange woman, even from the

1817
01:59:41,044 --> 01:59:46,984
foreigner who flatters with her words, who
forsakes the friend of her youth, and forgets

1818
01:59:47,024 --> 01:59:53,064
the covenant of her God; for her house
leads down to death, her paths to the departed

1819
01:59:53,104 --> 01:59:54,004
spirits.

1820
01:59:54,204 --> 01:59:59,504
None who go to her return again, neither
do they attain to the paths of life.

1821
02:00:00,464 --> 02:00:04,824
Therefore walk in the way of good men, and
keep the paths of the righteous.

1822
02:00:05,724 --> 02:00:07,804
For the upright will dwell in the land.

1823
02:00:08,564 --> 02:00:10,164
The perfect will remain in it.

1824
02:00:10,204 --> 02:00:12,984
But the wicked will be cut off from the
land.

1825
02:00:13,624 --> 02:00:15,724
The treacherous will be rooted out of it.

1826
02:00:16,544 --> 02:00:19,044
Proverbs, chapter three.

1827
02:00:19,084 --> 02:00:26,104
My son, don’t forget my teaching, but let
your heart keep my commandments, for

1828
02:00:26,144 --> 02:00:30,284
they will add to you length of days, years
of life, and peace.

1829
02:00:31,304 --> 02:00:34,024
Don’t let kindness and truth forsake you.

1830
02:00:34,904 --> 02:00:36,184
Bind them around your neck.

1831
02:00:36,724 --> 02:00:38,664
Write them on the tablet of your heart.

1832
02:00:39,664 --> 02:00:44,364
So you will find favour, and good
understanding in the sight of God and man.

1833
02:00:45,284 --> 02:00:50,224
Trust in the LORD with all your heart, and
don’t lean on your own understanding.

1834
02:00:51,364 --> 02:00:55,784
In all your ways acknowledge him, and he
will make your paths straight.

1835
02:00:56,524 --> 02:00:58,384
Don’t be wise in your own eyes.

1836
02:00:59,264 --> 02:01:01,464
Fear the LORD, and depart from evil.

1837
02:01:02,304 --> 02:01:06,104
It will be health to your body, and
nourishment to your bones.

1838
02:01:06,144 --> 02:01:12,884
Honour the LORD with your substance, with
the first fruits of all your increase; so

1839
02:01:12,924 --> 02:01:18,284
your barns will be filled with plenty, and
your vats will overflow with new wine.

1840
02:01:18,944 --> 02:01:25,844
My son, don’t despise the LORD’s discipline,
neither be weary of his correction; for

1841
02:01:25,884 --> 02:01:32,264
whom the LORD loves, he corrects, even as
a father reproves the son in whom he delights.

1842
02:01:33,124 --> 02:01:37,544
Happy is the man who finds wisdom, the man
who gets understanding.

1843
02:01:37,996 --> 02:01:43,496
For her good profit is better than getting
silver, and her return is better than fine

1844
02:01:43,536 --> 02:01:44,436
gold.

1845
02:01:44,836 --> 02:01:47,056
She is more precious than rubies.

1846
02:01:48,056 --> 02:01:51,576
None of the things you can desire are to
be compared to her.

1847
02:01:52,796 --> 02:01:55,076
Length of days is in her right hand.

1848
02:01:56,176 --> 02:01:58,756
In her left hand are riches and honour.

1849
02:01:58,796 --> 02:02:00,696
Her ways are ways of pleasantness.

1850
02:02:01,416 --> 02:02:02,636
All her paths are peace.

1851
02:02:03,556 --> 02:02:06,936
She is a tree of life to those who lay
hold of her.

1852
02:02:07,896 --> 02:02:10,216
Happy is everyone who retains her.

1853
02:02:11,176 --> 02:02:13,456
By wisdom the LORD founded the earth.

1854
02:02:14,216 --> 02:02:17,076
By understanding, he established the
heavens.

1855
02:02:17,676 --> 02:02:23,116
By his knowledge, the depths were broken
up, and the skies drop down the dew.

1856
02:02:23,636 --> 02:02:26,616
My son, let them not depart from your
eyes.

1857
02:02:27,636 --> 02:02:33,896
Keep sound wisdom and discretion, so they will
be life to your soul, and grace for your

1858
02:02:33,936 --> 02:02:34,836
neck.

1859
02:02:35,276 --> 02:02:37,276
Then you shall walk in your way securely.

1860
02:02:38,016 --> 02:02:39,156
Your foot won’t stumble.

1861
02:02:40,136 --> 02:02:42,496
When you lie down, you will not be afraid.

1862
02:02:43,196 --> 02:02:47,276
Yes, you will lie down, and your sleep
will be sweet.

1863
02:02:48,316 --> 02:02:53,756
Don’t be afraid of sudden fear, neither of
the desolation of the wicked, when it comes;

1864
02:02:54,336 --> 02:02:59,216
for the LORD will be your confidence, and
will keep your foot from being taken.

1865
02:02:59,816 --> 02:03:05,076
Don’t withhold good from those to whom it is
due, when it is in the power of your hand

1866
02:03:05,116 --> 02:03:06,016
to do it.

1867
02:03:06,536 --> 02:03:12,836
Don’t say to your neighbour, “Go, and come
again; tomorrow I will give it to you,” when

1868
02:03:12,876 --> 02:03:13,956
you have it by you.

1869
02:03:14,856 --> 02:03:19,576
Don’t devise evil against your neighbour,
since he dwells securely by you.

1870
02:03:20,076 --> 02:03:24,656
Don’t strive with a man without cause, if
he has done you no harm.

1871
02:03:25,716 --> 02:03:27,476
Don’t envy the man of violence.

1872
02:03:28,336 --> 02:03:29,736
Choose none of his ways.

1873
02:03:30,376 --> 02:03:36,116
For the perverse is an abomination to the
LORD, but his friendship is with the upright.

1874
02:03:36,896 --> 02:03:42,116
The LORD’s curse is in the house of
the wicked, but he blesses the habitation of the

1875
02:03:42,156 --> 02:03:43,056
righteous.

1876
02:03:43,496 --> 02:03:47,796
Surely he mocks the mockers, but he gives
grace to the humble.

1877
02:03:48,696 --> 02:03:53,376
The wise will inherit glory, but shame
will be the promotion of fools.

1878
02:03:53,976 --> 02:03:54,376
Proverbs, chapter four.

1879
02:03:54,416 --> 02:03:54,716
Listen, sons, to a father’s instruction.

1880
02:03:54,756 --> 02:03:55,656
Pay attention and know understanding; for
I give you sound learning.

1881
02:04:05,001 --> 02:04:06,501
Don’t forsake my law.

1882
02:04:07,421 --> 02:04:13,601
For I was a son to my father, tender and
an only child in the sight of my mother.

1883
02:04:14,181 --> 02:04:19,761
He taught me, and said to me: “Let your
heart retain my words.

1884
02:04:20,501 --> 02:04:22,661
Keep my commandments, and live.

1885
02:04:23,581 --> 02:04:24,481
Get wisdom.

1886
02:04:24,661 --> 02:04:25,561
Get understanding.

1887
02:04:26,641 --> 02:04:30,601
Don’t forget, and don’t deviate from the
words of my mouth.

1888
02:04:30,641 --> 02:04:33,901
Don’t forsake her, and she will preserve
you.

1889
02:04:34,641 --> 02:04:36,641
Love her, and she will keep you.

1890
02:04:37,541 --> 02:04:38,681
Wisdom is supreme.

1891
02:04:39,701 --> 02:04:40,601
Get wisdom.

1892
02:04:41,101 --> 02:04:45,601
Yes, though it costs all your possessions,
get understanding.

1893
02:04:45,641 --> 02:04:49,241
Esteem her, and she will exalt you.

1894
02:04:49,901 --> 02:04:52,621
She will bring you to honour when you
embrace her.

1895
02:04:53,161 --> 02:04:55,541
She will give to your head a garland of
grace.

1896
02:04:56,421 --> 02:04:59,261
She will deliver a crown of splendour to
you.”

1897
02:05:00,121 --> 02:05:03,221
Listen, my son, and receive my sayings.

1898
02:05:03,961 --> 02:05:05,881
The years of your life will be many.

1899
02:05:06,781 --> 02:05:08,641
I have taught you in the way of wisdom.

1900
02:05:09,341 --> 02:05:11,161
I have led you in straight paths.

1901
02:05:12,101 --> 02:05:14,961
When you go, your steps will not be
hampered.

1902
02:05:15,721 --> 02:05:17,881
When you run, you will not stumble.

1903
02:05:18,841 --> 02:05:20,341
Take firm hold of instruction.

1904
02:05:21,161 --> 02:05:22,401
Don’t let her go.

1905
02:05:23,161 --> 02:05:25,301
Keep her, for she is your life.

1906
02:05:26,421 --> 02:05:28,481
Don’t enter into the path of the wicked.

1907
02:05:29,301 --> 02:05:31,521
Don’t walk in the way of evil men.

1908
02:05:32,181 --> 02:05:34,581
Avoid it, and don’t pass by it.

1909
02:05:35,241 --> 02:05:36,981
Turn from it, and pass on.

1910
02:05:37,501 --> 02:05:39,861
For they don’t sleep unless they do evil.

1911
02:05:40,801 --> 02:05:44,601
Their sleep is taken away, unless they
make someone fall.

1912
02:05:44,641 --> 02:05:49,461
For they eat the bread of wickedness and
drink the wine of violence.

1913
02:05:50,381 --> 02:05:56,181
But the path of the righteous is like
the dawning light that shines more and more until

1914
02:05:56,221 --> 02:05:57,201
the perfect day.

1915
02:05:57,801 --> 02:05:59,581
The way of the wicked is like darkness.

1916
02:06:00,561 --> 02:06:02,601
They don’t know what they stumble over.

1917
02:06:03,361 --> 02:06:05,801
My son, attend to my words.

1918
02:06:06,701 --> 02:06:08,501
Turn your ear to my sayings.

1919
02:06:09,221 --> 02:06:11,041
Let them not depart from your eyes.

1920
02:06:11,501 --> 02:06:13,201
Keep them in the centre of your heart.

1921
02:06:13,801 --> 02:06:18,261
For they are life to those who find them,
and health to their whole body.

1922
02:06:18,781 --> 02:06:23,301
Keep your heart with all diligence, for
out of it is the wellspring of life.

1923
02:06:24,261 --> 02:06:26,721
Put away from yourself a perverse mouth.

1924
02:06:27,701 --> 02:06:29,561
Put corrupt lips far from you.

1925
02:06:30,441 --> 02:06:32,181
Let your eyes look straight ahead.

1926
02:06:33,001 --> 02:06:35,221
Fix your gaze directly before you.

1927
02:06:35,539 --> 02:06:37,279
Make the path of your feet level.

1928
02:06:38,579 --> 02:06:40,599
Let all of your ways be established.

1929
02:06:41,779 --> 02:06:44,419
Don’t turn to the right hand nor to the
left.

1930
02:06:45,659 --> 02:06:46,859
Remove your foot from evil.

1931
02:06:47,759 --> 02:06:50,779
Proverbs, chapter five.

1932
02:06:50,819 --> 02:06:53,459
My son, pay attention to my wisdom.

1933
02:06:54,179 --> 02:07:00,519
Turn your ear to my understanding, that
you may maintain discretion, that your lips may

1934
02:07:00,559 --> 02:07:01,539
preserve knowledge.

1935
02:07:02,259 --> 02:07:04,739
For the lips of an adulteress drip honey.

1936
02:07:05,639 --> 02:07:11,919
Her mouth is smoother than oil, but in the
end she is as bitter as wormwood, and as sharp

1937
02:07:11,959 --> 02:07:13,439
as a two-edged sword.

1938
02:07:14,319 --> 02:07:15,819
Her feet go down to death.

1939
02:07:16,499 --> 02:07:19,239
Her steps lead straight to Sheol.

1940
02:07:19,279 --> 02:07:21,439
She gives no thought to the way of life.

1941
02:07:22,259 --> 02:07:24,979
Her ways are crooked, and she doesn’t know
it.

1942
02:07:25,719 --> 02:07:28,499
Now therefore, my sons, listen to me.

1943
02:07:29,219 --> 02:07:31,579
Don’t depart from the words of my mouth.

1944
02:07:32,179 --> 02:07:33,939
Remove your way far from her.

1945
02:07:34,499 --> 02:07:40,019
Don’t come near the door of her house,
lest you give your honour to others, and your

1946
02:07:40,059 --> 02:07:46,239
years to the cruel one; lest strangers
feast on your wealth, and your labours enrich

1947
02:07:46,279 --> 02:07:47,699
another man’s house.

1948
02:07:48,419 --> 02:07:54,259
You will groan at your latter end, when
your flesh and your body are consumed, and say,

1949
02:07:55,039 --> 02:07:59,579
“How I have hated instruction, and my
heart despised reproof.

1950
02:08:00,299 --> 02:08:05,299
I haven’t obeyed the voice of my teachers,
nor turned my ear to those who instructed

1951
02:08:05,339 --> 02:08:06,239
me!

1952
02:08:06,299 --> 02:08:10,639
I have come to the brink of utter ruin,
amongst the gathered assembly.”

1953
02:08:11,719 --> 02:08:16,639
Drink water out of your own cistern,
running water out of your own well.

1954
02:08:17,359 --> 02:08:22,899
Should your springs overflow in the streets,
streams of water in the public squares?

1955
02:08:23,359 --> 02:08:27,579
Let them be for yourself alone, not for
strangers with you.

1956
02:08:28,039 --> 02:08:29,499
Let your spring be blessed.

1957
02:08:30,339 --> 02:08:32,279
Rejoice in the wife of your youth.

1958
02:08:32,979 --> 02:08:38,879
A loving doe and a graceful deer— let her
breasts satisfy you at all times.

1959
02:08:39,759 --> 02:08:41,999
Be captivated always with her love.

1960
02:08:42,419 --> 02:08:47,179
For why should you, my son, be captivated
with an adulteress?

1961
02:08:47,219 --> 02:08:49,319
Why embrace the bosom of another?

1962
02:08:50,039 --> 02:08:52,899
For the ways of man are before the LORD’s
eyes.

1963
02:08:53,859 --> 02:08:55,539
He examines all his paths.

1964
02:08:56,659 --> 02:08:59,179
The evil deeds of the wicked ensnare him.

1965
02:09:00,099 --> 02:09:02,199
The cords of his sin hold him firmly.

1966
02:09:02,706 --> 02:09:04,686
He will die for lack of instruction.

1967
02:09:06,026 --> 02:09:09,086
In the greatness of his folly, he will go
astray.

1968
02:09:10,626 --> 02:09:13,246
Proverbs, chapter six.

1969
02:09:13,286 --> 02:09:19,846
My son, if you have become collateral for
your neighbour, if you have struck your hands

1970
02:09:19,886 --> 02:09:26,106
in pledge for a stranger, you are trapped
by the words of your mouth; you are ensnared

1971
02:09:26,146 --> 02:09:27,546
with the words of your mouth.

1972
02:09:28,286 --> 02:09:34,626
Do this now, my son, and deliver yourself,
since you have come into the hand of your

1973
02:09:34,666 --> 02:09:35,606
neighbour.

1974
02:09:35,646 --> 02:09:37,626
Go, humble yourself.

1975
02:09:38,186 --> 02:09:40,666
Press your plea with your neighbour.

1976
02:09:40,706 --> 02:09:44,986
Give no sleep to your eyes, nor slumber to
your eyelids.

1977
02:09:45,486 --> 02:09:51,586
Free yourself, like a gazelle from the hand
of the hunter, like a bird from the snare

1978
02:09:51,626 --> 02:09:52,526
of the fowler.

1979
02:09:53,426 --> 02:09:55,926
Go to the ant, you sluggard.

1980
02:09:55,966 --> 02:10:03,046
Consider her ways, and be wise; which
having no chief, overseer, or ruler, provides

1981
02:10:03,086 --> 02:10:06,906
her bread in the summer, and gathers her
food in the harvest.

1982
02:10:07,686 --> 02:10:10,346
How long will you sleep, sluggard?

1983
02:10:10,386 --> 02:10:12,406
When will you arise out of your sleep?

1984
02:10:13,026 --> 02:10:19,866
A little sleep, a little slumber, a little
folding of the hands to sleep— so

1985
02:10:19,906 --> 02:10:24,746
your poverty will come as a robber, and
your scarcity as an armed man.

1986
02:10:24,786 --> 02:10:32,226
A worthless person, a man of iniquity, is
he who walks with a perverse mouth, who

1987
02:10:32,266 --> 02:10:38,666
winks with his eyes, who signals with his
feet, who motions with his fingers, in whose

1988
02:10:38,706 --> 02:10:45,186
heart is perverseness, who devises evil
continually, who always sows discord.

1989
02:10:45,726 --> 02:10:47,986
Therefore his calamity will come suddenly.

1990
02:10:48,766 --> 02:10:52,226
He will be broken suddenly, and that
without remedy.

1991
02:10:53,046 --> 02:10:59,706
There are six things which the LORD hates;
yes, seven which are an abomination to

1992
02:10:59,746 --> 02:11:06,846
him: arrogant eyes, a lying tongue, hands
that shed innocent blood, a

1993
02:11:06,886 --> 02:11:13,166
heart that devises wicked schemes, feet that
are swift in running to mischief, a false

1994
02:11:13,206 --> 02:11:22,166
witness who utters lies, and he who

1995
02:11:22,206 --> 02:11:22,506
sows discord amongst brothers.

1996
02:11:22,546 --> 02:11:23,826
My son, keep your father’s commandment,
and don’t forsake your mother’s teaching.

1997
02:11:25,146 --> 02:11:27,106
Bind them continually on your heart.

1998
02:11:28,346 --> 02:11:29,426
Tie them around your neck.

1999
02:11:30,346 --> 02:11:32,146
When you walk, it will lead you.

2000
02:11:32,926 --> 02:11:35,386
When you sleep, it will watch over you.

2001
02:11:35,640 --> 02:11:38,020
When you awake, it will talk with you.

2002
02:11:39,040 --> 02:11:42,600
For the commandment is a lamp, and the law
is light.

2003
02:11:43,880 --> 02:11:49,720
Reproofs of instruction are the way of life,
to keep you from the immoral woman, from

2004
02:11:49,760 --> 02:11:52,040
the flattery of the wayward wife’s tongue.

2005
02:11:52,740 --> 02:11:58,620
Don’t lust after her beauty in your heart,
neither let her captivate you with her eyelids.

2006
02:11:59,280 --> 02:12:02,380
For a prostitute reduces you to a piece of
bread.

2007
02:12:03,100 --> 02:12:06,040
The adulteress hunts for your precious
life.

2008
02:12:07,240 --> 02:12:11,680
Can a man scoop fire into his lap, and his
clothes not be burnt?

2009
02:12:12,280 --> 02:12:16,580
Or can one walk on hot coals, and his feet
not be scorched?

2010
02:12:17,620 --> 02:12:20,680
So is he who goes in to his neighbour’s
wife.

2011
02:12:21,580 --> 02:12:24,200
Whoever touches her will not be
unpunished.

2012
02:12:25,240 --> 02:12:32,320
Men don’t despise a thief if he

2013
02:12:32,360 --> 02:12:34,240
steals to satisfy himself when he is hungry,
but if he is found, he shall restore seven

2014
02:12:34,280 --> 02:12:35,180
times.

2015
02:12:35,400 --> 02:12:37,520
He shall give all the wealth of his house.

2016
02:12:38,640 --> 02:12:42,280
He who commits adultery with a woman is
void of understanding.

2017
02:12:43,380 --> 02:12:45,960
He who does it destroys his own soul.

2018
02:12:47,080 --> 02:12:49,600
He will get wounds and dishonour.

2019
02:12:49,640 --> 02:12:51,660
His reproach will not be wiped away.

2020
02:12:52,120 --> 02:12:54,760
For jealousy arouses the fury of the
husband.

2021
02:12:55,560 --> 02:12:57,420
He won’t spare in the day of vengeance.

2022
02:12:58,310 --> 02:13:04,600
He won’t regard any ransom, neither will
he rest content, though you give many gifts.

2023
02:13:05,880 --> 02:13:07,860
Proverbs, chapter seven.

2024
02:13:07,900 --> 02:13:10,100
My son, keep my words.

2025
02:13:11,060 --> 02:13:12,920
Lay up my commandments within you.

2026
02:13:13,760 --> 02:13:15,700
Keep my commandments and live!

2027
02:13:16,480 --> 02:13:19,000
Guard my teaching as the apple of your
eye.

2028
02:13:19,560 --> 02:13:20,880
Bind them on your fingers.

2029
02:13:21,920 --> 02:13:23,620
Write them on the tablet of your heart.

2030
02:13:24,340 --> 02:13:27,180
Tell wisdom, “You are my sister.”

2031
02:13:28,200 --> 02:13:33,720
Call understanding your relative, that they may
keep you from the strange woman, from

2032
02:13:33,760 --> 02:13:36,040
the foreigner who flatters with her words.

2033
02:13:36,500 --> 02:13:40,440
For at the window of my house, I looked
out through my lattice.

2034
02:13:40,900 --> 02:13:42,720
I saw amongst the simple ones.

2035
02:13:43,620 --> 02:13:49,540
I discerned amongst the youths a young man
void of understanding, passing through the

2036
02:13:49,580 --> 02:13:55,780
street near her corner, he went the way to
her house, in the twilight, in the evening

2037
02:13:55,820 --> 02:13:59,200
of the day, in the middle of the night and
in the darkness.

2038
02:13:59,644 --> 02:14:06,244
Behold, there a woman met him with the
attire of a prostitute, and with crafty

2039
02:14:06,284 --> 02:14:07,184
intent.

2040
02:14:07,644 --> 02:14:09,144
She is loud and defiant.

2041
02:14:10,264 --> 02:14:12,064
Her feet don’t stay in her house.

2042
02:14:12,964 --> 02:14:18,784
Now she is in the streets, now in the
squares, and lurking at every corner.

2043
02:14:19,664 --> 02:14:22,044
So she caught him, and kissed him.

2044
02:14:22,424 --> 02:14:28,844
With an impudent face she said to
him: “Sacrifices of peace offerings are with me.

2045
02:14:29,744 --> 02:14:31,804
Today I have paid my vows.

2046
02:14:32,704 --> 02:14:38,744
Therefore I came out to meet you, to
diligently seek your face, and I have found you.

2047
02:14:39,204 --> 02:14:45,024
I have spread my couch with carpets of
tapestry, with striped cloths of the yarn of Egypt.

2048
02:14:45,824 --> 02:14:49,804
I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, aloes,
and cinnamon.

2049
02:14:51,084 --> 02:14:55,084
Come, let’s take our fill of loving until
the morning.

2050
02:14:55,924 --> 02:14:58,284
Let’s solace ourselves with loving.

2051
02:14:58,664 --> 02:15:00,324
For my husband isn’t at home.

2052
02:15:01,204 --> 02:15:02,864
He has gone on a long journey.

2053
02:15:03,744 --> 02:15:05,804
He has taken a bag of money with him.

2054
02:15:06,604 --> 02:15:08,364
He will come home at the full moon.”

2055
02:15:09,204 --> 02:15:11,744
With persuasive words, she led him astray.

2056
02:15:12,704 --> 02:15:15,644
With the flattering of her lips, she
seduced him.

2057
02:15:16,804 --> 02:15:23,104
He followed her immediately, as an ox goes
to the slaughter, as a fool stepping into

2058
02:15:23,144 --> 02:15:24,044
a noose.

2059
02:15:24,324 --> 02:15:30,444
Until an arrow strikes through his liver, as
a bird hurries to the snare, and doesn’t

2060
02:15:30,484 --> 02:15:32,264
know that it will cost his life.

2061
02:15:33,104 --> 02:15:36,164
Now therefore, sons, listen to me.

2062
02:15:36,984 --> 02:15:39,224
Pay attention to the words of my mouth.

2063
02:15:39,964 --> 02:15:41,924
Don’t let your heart turn to her ways.

2064
02:15:42,684 --> 02:15:47,204
Don’t go astray in her paths, for she has
thrown down many wounded.

2065
02:15:48,024 --> 02:15:51,264
Yes, all her slain are a mighty army.

2066
02:15:52,184 --> 02:15:56,524
Her house is the way to Sheol, going down
to the rooms of death.

2067
02:15:56,564 --> 02:15:59,284
Proverbs, chapter eight.

2068
02:15:59,324 --> 02:16:01,424
Doesn’t wisdom cry out?

2069
02:16:01,464 --> 02:16:04,524
Doesn’t understanding raise her voice?

2070
02:16:05,244 --> 02:16:10,164
On the top of high places by the way,
where the paths meet, she stands.

2071
02:16:11,164 --> 02:16:18,284
Beside the gates, at the entry of the
city, at the entry doors, she cries aloud: “I

2072
02:16:18,324 --> 02:16:19,284
call to you men!

2073
02:16:19,664 --> 02:16:21,944
I send my voice to the sons of mankind.

2074
02:16:22,664 --> 02:16:25,584
You simple, understand prudence!

2075
02:16:26,404 --> 02:16:29,044
You fools, be of an understanding heart!

2076
02:16:29,084 --> 02:16:32,704
Hear, for I will speak excellent things.

2077
02:16:33,604 --> 02:16:36,204
The opening of my lips is for right
things.

2078
02:16:36,670 --> 02:16:38,250
For my mouth speaks truth.

2079
02:16:39,370 --> 02:16:41,770
Wickedness is an abomination to my lips.

2080
02:16:42,870 --> 02:16:45,050
All the words of my mouth are in
righteousness.

2081
02:16:45,990 --> 02:16:48,810
There is nothing crooked or perverse in
them.

2082
02:16:49,470 --> 02:16:54,810
They are all plain to him who understands,
right to those who find knowledge.

2083
02:16:55,630 --> 02:17:00,770
Receive my instruction rather than silver,
knowledge rather than choice gold.

2084
02:17:01,730 --> 02:17:04,250
For wisdom is better than rubies.

2085
02:17:05,010 --> 02:17:08,890
All the things that may be desired can’t
be compared to it.

2086
02:17:09,230 --> 02:17:12,750
“I, wisdom, have made prudence my
dwelling.

2087
02:17:13,770 --> 02:17:15,590
Find out knowledge and discretion.

2088
02:17:16,830 --> 02:17:18,870
The fear of the LORD is to hate evil.

2089
02:17:19,550 --> 02:17:24,530
I hate pride, arrogance, the evil way, and
the perverse mouth.

2090
02:17:25,610 --> 02:17:27,950
Counsel and sound knowledge are mine.

2091
02:17:28,740 --> 02:17:30,670
I have understanding and power.

2092
02:17:30,710 --> 02:17:34,750
By me kings reign, and princes decree
justice.

2093
02:17:35,610 --> 02:17:40,950
By me princes rule, nobles, and all the
righteous rulers of the earth.

2094
02:17:41,950 --> 02:17:43,570
I love those who love me.

2095
02:17:44,210 --> 02:17:46,790
Those who seek me diligently will find me.

2096
02:17:47,690 --> 02:17:51,790
With me are riches, honour, enduring
wealth, and prosperity.

2097
02:17:53,090 --> 02:18:00,110
My fruit is better than gold, yes, than
fine gold, my yield than choice silver.

2098
02:18:00,770 --> 02:18:06,490
I walk in the way of righteousness, in the
middle of the paths of justice, that I may

2099
02:18:06,530 --> 02:18:08,410
give wealth to those who love me.

2100
02:18:09,330 --> 02:18:10,650
I fill their treasuries.

2101
02:18:11,530 --> 02:18:15,990
“The LORD possessed me in the beginning of
his work, before his deeds of old.

2102
02:18:16,590 --> 02:18:21,810
I was set up from everlasting, from the
beginning, before the earth existed.

2103
02:18:23,050 --> 02:18:28,630
When there were no depths, I was born,
when there were no springs abounding with water.

2104
02:18:29,690 --> 02:18:35,950
Before the mountains were settled in place, before
the hills, I was born; while as yet

2105
02:18:35,990 --> 02:18:41,490
he had not made the earth, nor the fields,
nor the beginning of the dust of the world.

2106
02:18:42,550 --> 02:18:45,590
When he established the heavens, I was
there.

2107
02:18:45,937 --> 02:18:51,317
When he set a circle on the surface
of the deep, when he established the clouds above,

2108
02:18:52,017 --> 02:18:58,857
when the springs of the deep became strong,
when he gave to the sea its boundary, that

2109
02:18:58,897 --> 02:19:04,517
the waters should not violate his commandment,
when he marked out the foundations of

2110
02:19:04,557 --> 02:19:07,437
the earth, then I was the craftsman by his
side.

2111
02:19:08,177 --> 02:19:14,677
I was a delight day by day,
always rejoicing before him, rejoicing in his whole

2112
02:19:14,717 --> 02:19:15,617
world.

2113
02:19:16,277 --> 02:19:18,437
My delight was with the sons of men.

2114
02:19:19,457 --> 02:19:25,617
“Now therefore, my sons, listen to me, for
blessed are those who keep my ways.

2115
02:19:26,577 --> 02:19:28,437
Hear instruction, and be wise.

2116
02:19:29,177 --> 02:19:30,237
Don’t refuse it.

2117
02:19:30,917 --> 02:19:37,857
Blessed is the man who hears me, watching
daily at my gates, waiting at my door posts.

2118
02:19:37,897 --> 02:19:42,917
For whoever finds me finds life, and will
obtain favour from the LORD.

2119
02:19:43,757 --> 02:19:46,777
But he who sins against me wrongs his own
soul.

2120
02:19:47,277 --> 02:19:49,297
All those who hate me love death.”

2121
02:19:50,357 --> 02:19:53,037
Proverbs, chapter nine.

2122
02:19:53,077 --> 02:19:55,137
Wisdom has built her house.

2123
02:19:55,877 --> 02:19:57,777
She has carved out her seven pillars.

2124
02:19:58,837 --> 02:20:00,017
She has prepared her meat.

2125
02:20:00,837 --> 02:20:01,957
She has mixed her wine.

2126
02:20:02,817 --> 02:20:04,297
She has also set her table.

2127
02:20:05,137 --> 02:20:06,917
She has sent out her maidens.

2128
02:20:07,437 --> 02:20:13,937
She cries from the highest places of the
city: “Whoever is simple, let him turn in here!”

2129
02:20:14,637 --> 02:20:21,317
As for him who is void of understanding, she
says to him, “Come, eat some of my bread,

2130
02:20:21,897 --> 02:20:24,137
Drink some of the wine which I have mixed!

2131
02:20:25,017 --> 02:20:27,377
Leave your simple ways, and live.

2132
02:20:28,237 --> 02:20:29,797
Walk in the way of understanding.”

2133
02:20:30,357 --> 02:20:33,397
One who corrects a mocker invites insult.

2134
02:20:34,097 --> 02:20:37,317
One who reproves a wicked man invites
abuse.

2135
02:20:37,837 --> 02:20:40,857
Don’t reprove a scoffer, lest he hate you.

2136
02:20:41,717 --> 02:20:44,977
Reprove a wise person, and he will love
you.

2137
02:20:45,957 --> 02:20:49,597
Instruct a wise person, and he will be
still wiser.

2138
02:20:50,797 --> 02:20:54,117
Teach a righteous person, and he will
increase in learning.

2139
02:20:54,737 --> 02:20:57,037
The fear of the LORD is the beginning of
wisdom.

2140
02:20:57,917 --> 02:21:00,517
The knowledge of the Holy One is
understanding.

2141
02:21:01,397 --> 02:21:03,597
For by me your days will be multiplied.

2142
02:21:04,697 --> 02:21:06,717
The years of your life will be increased.

2143
02:21:08,057 --> 02:21:10,637
If you are wise, you are wise for
yourself.

2144
02:21:11,857 --> 02:21:14,177
If you mock, you alone will bear it.

2145
02:21:15,277 --> 02:21:19,537
The foolish woman is loud, undisciplined,
and knows nothing.

2146
02:21:19,880 --> 02:21:26,240
She sits at the door of her house, on a
seat in the high places of the city, to call

2147
02:21:26,280 --> 02:21:32,820
to those who pass by, who go straight on
their ways, “Whoever is simple, let him

2148
02:21:32,860 --> 02:21:33,760
turn in here.”

2149
02:21:33,960 --> 02:21:40,240
As for him who is void of understanding,
she says to him, “Stolen water is sweet.

2150
02:21:40,860 --> 02:21:42,760
Food eaten in secret is pleasant.”

2151
02:21:43,680 --> 02:21:49,460
But he doesn’t know that the departed spirits
are there, that her guests are in the depths

2152
02:21:49,500 --> 02:21:50,400
of Sheol.

2153
02:21:51,480 --> 02:21:53,480
Proverbs, chapter ten.

2154
02:21:53,520 --> 02:21:54,720
The proverbs of Solomon.

2155
02:21:55,320 --> 02:22:01,180
A wise son makes a glad father; but a
foolish son brings grief to his mother.

2156
02:22:01,860 --> 02:22:07,080
Treasures of wickedness profit nothing,
but righteousness delivers from death.

2157
02:22:08,160 --> 02:22:14,020
The LORD will not allow the soul of the
righteous to go hungry, but he thrusts away the

2158
02:22:14,060 --> 02:22:15,220
desire of the wicked.

2159
02:22:15,640 --> 02:22:21,860
He becomes poor who works with a lazy
hand, but the hand of the diligent brings wealth.

2160
02:22:22,500 --> 02:22:29,060
He who gathers in summer is a wise son,
but he who sleeps during the harvest is a

2161
02:22:29,100 --> 02:22:30,460
son who causes shame.

2162
02:22:31,720 --> 02:22:36,980
Blessings are on the head of the righteous,
but violence covers the mouth of the wicked.

2163
02:22:37,640 --> 02:22:42,520
The memory of the righteous is blessed,
but the name of the wicked will rot.

2164
02:22:43,260 --> 02:22:47,960
The wise in heart accept commandments, but
a chattering fool will fall.

2165
02:22:49,100 --> 02:22:55,480
He who walks blamelessly walks surely, but he
who perverts his ways will be found out.

2166
02:22:56,480 --> 02:23:01,760
One who winks with the eye causes sorrow,
but a chattering fool will fall.

2167
02:23:02,460 --> 02:23:07,780
The mouth of the righteous is a spring of
life, but violence covers the mouth of the

2168
02:23:07,820 --> 02:23:08,720
wicked.

2169
02:23:09,180 --> 02:23:13,340
Hatred stirs up strife, but love covers
all wrongs.

2170
02:23:14,160 --> 02:23:19,940
Wisdom is found on the lips of him who has
discernment, but a rod is for the back of

2171
02:23:19,980 --> 02:23:21,740
him who is void of understanding.

2172
02:23:22,500 --> 02:23:27,060
Wise men lay up knowledge, but the mouth
of the foolish is near ruin.

2173
02:23:28,000 --> 02:23:30,500
The rich man’s wealth is his strong city.

2174
02:23:31,540 --> 02:23:33,680
The destruction of the poor is their
poverty.

2175
02:23:34,940 --> 02:23:37,040
The labour of the righteous leads to life.

2176
02:23:37,080 --> 02:23:40,380
The increase of the wicked leads to sin.

2177
02:23:40,828 --> 02:23:47,588
He is in the way of life who
heeds correction, but he who forsakes reproof leads

2178
02:23:47,628 --> 02:23:48,588
others astray.

2179
02:23:49,568 --> 02:23:52,428
He who hides hatred has lying lips.

2180
02:23:53,368 --> 02:23:55,968
He who utters a slander is a fool.

2181
02:23:56,008 --> 02:24:02,548
In the multitude of words there is no lack
of disobedience, but he who restrains

2182
02:24:02,588 --> 02:24:04,048
his lips does wisely.

2183
02:24:04,908 --> 02:24:07,528
The tongue of the righteous is like choice
silver.

2184
02:24:08,648 --> 02:24:11,028
The heart of the wicked is of little
worth.

2185
02:24:12,148 --> 02:24:17,488
The lips of the righteous feed many, but
the foolish die for lack of understanding.

2186
02:24:18,588 --> 02:24:23,088
The LORD’s blessing brings wealth, and he
adds no trouble to it.

2187
02:24:23,588 --> 02:24:29,408
It is a fool’s pleasure to do wickedness,
but wisdom is a man of understanding’s pleasure.

2188
02:24:30,308 --> 02:24:35,968
What the wicked fear will overtake them, but
the desire of the righteous will be granted.

2189
02:24:37,048 --> 02:24:43,148
When the whirlwind passes, the wicked is
no more; but the righteous stand firm forever.

2190
02:24:43,948 --> 02:24:50,368
As vinegar to the teeth, and as smoke to
the eyes, so is the sluggard to those who send

2191
02:24:50,408 --> 02:24:51,308
him.

2192
02:24:51,448 --> 02:24:56,788
The fear of the LORD prolongs days, but
the years of the wicked shall be shortened.

2193
02:24:57,508 --> 02:25:02,788
The prospect of the righteous is joy, but
the hope of the wicked will perish.

2194
02:25:03,448 --> 02:25:08,908
The way of the LORD is a stronghold to
the upright, but it is a destruction to the workers

2195
02:25:08,948 --> 02:25:09,868
of iniquity.

2196
02:25:10,728 --> 02:25:15,588
The righteous will never be removed, but
the wicked will not dwell in the land.

2197
02:25:16,728 --> 02:25:21,948
The mouth of the righteous produces wisdom,
but the perverse tongue will be cut off.

2198
02:25:22,628 --> 02:25:28,368
The lips of the righteous know what is
acceptable, but the mouth of the wicked is perverse.

2199
02:25:29,668 --> 02:25:32,408
Proverbs, chapter eleven.

2200
02:25:32,448 --> 02:25:38,968
A false balance is an abomination to
the LORD, but accurate weights are his delight.

2201
02:25:39,008 --> 02:25:44,588
When pride comes, then comes shame, but
with humility comes wisdom.

2202
02:25:45,528 --> 02:25:50,528
The integrity of the upright shall guide
them, but the perverseness of the treacherous

2203
02:25:50,568 --> 02:25:52,148
shall destroy them.

2204
02:25:52,968 --> 02:25:58,288
Riches don’t profit in the day of wrath,
but righteousness delivers from death.

2205
02:25:58,688 --> 02:26:04,108
The righteousness of the blameless will direct
his way, but the wicked shall fall by

2206
02:26:04,148 --> 02:26:05,168
his own wickedness.

2207
02:26:05,504 --> 02:26:10,984
The righteousness of the upright shall deliver
them, but the unfaithful will be trapped

2208
02:26:11,024 --> 02:26:12,184
by evil desires.

2209
02:26:13,264 --> 02:26:19,724
When a wicked man dies, hope perishes, and
expectation of power comes to

2210
02:26:19,764 --> 02:26:20,664
nothing.

2211
02:26:21,244 --> 02:26:25,804
A righteous person is delivered out of
trouble, and the wicked takes his place.

2212
02:26:26,584 --> 02:26:32,384
With his mouth the godless man destroys
his neighbour, but the righteous will be delivered

2213
02:26:32,424 --> 02:26:33,324
through knowledge.

2214
02:26:34,304 --> 02:26:38,324
When it goes well with the righteous, the
city rejoices.

2215
02:26:39,164 --> 02:26:41,424
When the wicked perish, there is shouting.

2216
02:26:42,024 --> 02:26:48,064
By the blessing of the upright, the city
is exalted, but it is overthrown by the mouth

2217
02:26:48,104 --> 02:26:49,004
of the wicked.

2218
02:26:49,864 --> 02:26:55,844
One who despises his neighbour is void of
wisdom, but a man of understanding holds his

2219
02:26:55,884 --> 02:26:56,784
peace.

2220
02:26:56,864 --> 02:27:03,504
One who brings gossip betrays a confidence, but
one who is of a trustworthy spirit is

2221
02:27:03,544 --> 02:27:04,764
one who keeps a secret.

2222
02:27:06,124 --> 02:27:11,864
Where there is no wise guidance, the
nation falls, but in the multitude of counsellors

2223
02:27:11,904 --> 02:27:12,924
there is victory.

2224
02:27:13,784 --> 02:27:19,784
He who is collateral for a stranger will
suffer for it, but he who refuses pledges of

2225
02:27:19,824 --> 02:27:21,124
collateral is secure.

2226
02:27:22,284 --> 02:27:26,704
A gracious woman obtains honour, but
violent men obtain riches.

2227
02:27:27,764 --> 02:27:33,584
The merciful man does good to his own soul,
but he who is cruel troubles his own flesh.

2228
02:27:34,444 --> 02:27:40,964
Wicked people earn deceitful wages, but
one who sows righteousness reaps a sure

2229
02:27:41,004 --> 02:27:41,904
reward.

2230
02:27:42,764 --> 02:27:45,184
He who is truly righteous gets life.

2231
02:27:46,224 --> 02:27:48,244
He who pursues evil gets death.

2232
02:27:49,304 --> 02:27:54,964
Those who are perverse in heart are an
abomination to the LORD, but those whose ways

2233
02:27:55,004 --> 02:27:56,764
are blameless are his delight.

2234
02:27:57,484 --> 02:28:03,464
Most certainly, the evil man will not
be unpunished, but the offspring of the righteous

2235
02:28:03,504 --> 02:28:04,404
will be delivered.

2236
02:28:05,464 --> 02:28:10,604
Like a gold ring in a pig’s snout, is a
beautiful woman who lacks discretion.

2237
02:28:11,784 --> 02:28:14,284
The desire of the righteous is only good.

2238
02:28:15,184 --> 02:28:17,304
The expectation of the wicked is wrath.

2239
02:28:18,004 --> 02:28:21,324
There is one who scatters, and increases
yet more.

2240
02:28:21,984 --> 02:28:26,804
There is one who withholds more than is
appropriate, but gains poverty.

2241
02:28:28,064 --> 02:28:30,264
The liberal soul shall be made fat.

2242
02:28:31,164 --> 02:28:33,764
He who waters shall be watered also
himself.

2243
02:28:34,336 --> 02:28:40,456
People curse someone who withholds grain, but blessing
will be on the head of him who

2244
02:28:40,496 --> 02:28:41,396
sells it.

2245
02:28:42,456 --> 02:28:49,456
He who diligently seeks good seeks favour,
but he who searches after evil, it

2246
02:28:49,496 --> 02:28:50,396
shall come to him.

2247
02:28:50,776 --> 02:28:56,936
He who trusts in his riches will fall, but
the righteous shall flourish as the green

2248
02:28:56,976 --> 02:28:57,276
leaf.

2249
02:28:57,316 --> 02:29:01,436
He who troubles his own house shall
inherit the wind.

2250
02:29:02,616 --> 02:29:05,516
The foolish shall be servant to the wise
of heart.

2251
02:29:06,616 --> 02:29:09,236
The fruit of the righteous is a tree of
life.

2252
02:29:09,776 --> 02:29:11,956
He who is wise wins souls.

2253
02:29:12,976 --> 02:29:19,316
Behold, the righteous shall be repaid in the
earth, how much more the wicked and the

2254
02:29:19,356 --> 02:29:20,256
sinner!

2255
02:29:20,876 --> 02:29:23,176
Proverbs, chapter twelve.

2256
02:29:23,216 --> 02:29:29,356
Whoever loves correction loves knowledge,
but he who hates reproof is stupid.

2257
02:29:30,656 --> 02:29:36,496
A good man shall obtain favour from the LORD,
but he will condemn a man of wicked plans.

2258
02:29:37,736 --> 02:29:43,156
A man shall not be established by wickedness,
but the root of the righteous shall not

2259
02:29:43,196 --> 02:29:44,096
be moved.

2260
02:29:44,556 --> 02:29:50,656
A worthy woman is the crown of her
husband, but a disgraceful wife is as rottenness in

2261
02:29:50,696 --> 02:29:51,596
his bones.

2262
02:29:52,376 --> 02:29:57,616
The thoughts of the righteous are just,
but the advice of the wicked is deceitful.

2263
02:29:58,436 --> 02:30:04,236
The words of the wicked are about lying in
wait for blood, but the speech of the upright

2264
02:30:04,276 --> 02:30:05,196
rescues them.

2265
02:30:05,676 --> 02:30:11,796
The wicked are overthrown, and are no more,
but the house of the righteous shall stand.

2266
02:30:12,756 --> 02:30:18,996
A man shall be commended according to his
wisdom, but he who has a warped mind shall

2267
02:30:19,036 --> 02:30:19,936
be despised.

2268
02:30:20,256 --> 02:30:26,576
Better is he who is little known, and has
a servant, than he who honours himself and

2269
02:30:26,616 --> 02:30:27,516
lacks bread.

2270
02:30:28,076 --> 02:30:33,736
A righteous man respects the life of his
animal, but the tender mercies of the wicked

2271
02:30:33,776 --> 02:30:34,676
are cruel.

2272
02:30:35,476 --> 02:30:42,116
He who tills his land shall have plenty of
bread, but he who chases fantasies is

2273
02:30:42,156 --> 02:30:43,256
void of understanding.

2274
02:30:44,016 --> 02:30:49,456
The wicked desires the plunder of evil
men, but the root of the righteous flourishes.

2275
02:30:49,496 --> 02:30:56,196
An evil man is trapped by sinfulness of
lips, but the righteous shall come out of trouble.

2276
02:30:57,356 --> 02:31:01,156
A man shall be satisfied with good by the
fruit of his mouth.

2277
02:31:01,591 --> 02:31:04,871
The work of a man’s hands shall be
rewarded to him.

2278
02:31:06,011 --> 02:31:12,311
The way of a fool is right in his
own eyes, but he who is wise listens to counsel.

2279
02:31:13,651 --> 02:31:19,971
A fool shows his annoyance the same day,
but one who overlooks an insult is prudent.

2280
02:31:20,551 --> 02:31:25,371
He who is truthful testifies honestly, but
a false witness lies.

2281
02:31:26,131 --> 02:31:31,771
There is one who speaks rashly like the piercing
of a sword, but the tongue of the wise

2282
02:31:31,811 --> 02:31:32,711
heals.

2283
02:31:33,511 --> 02:31:39,511
Truth’s lips will be established forever,
but a lying tongue is only momentary.

2284
02:31:40,671 --> 02:31:46,611
Deceit is in the heart of those who plot
evil, but joy comes to the promoters of peace.

2285
02:31:47,411 --> 02:31:52,151
No mischief shall happen to the righteous,
but the wicked shall be filled with evil.

2286
02:31:53,271 --> 02:31:59,151
Lying lips are an abomination to the LORD,
but those who do the truth are his delight.

2287
02:32:00,351 --> 02:32:05,531
A prudent man keeps his knowledge, but the
hearts of fools proclaim foolishness.

2288
02:32:06,211 --> 02:32:12,471
The hands of the diligent ones shall rule,
but laziness ends in slave labour.

2289
02:32:12,511 --> 02:32:17,831
Anxiety in a man’s heart weighs it down,
but a kind word makes it glad.

2290
02:32:19,031 --> 02:32:24,931
A righteous person is cautious in friendship, but
the way of the wicked leads them astray.

2291
02:32:24,971 --> 02:32:30,931
The slothful man doesn’t roast his game,
but the possessions of diligent men are prized.

2292
02:32:32,091 --> 02:32:36,631
In the way of righteousness is life; in
its path there is no death.

2293
02:32:37,671 --> 02:32:39,284
Proverbs, chapter thirteen.

2294
02:32:39,324 --> 02:32:45,331
A wise son listens to his father’s
instruction, but a scoffer doesn’t listen to rebuke.

2295
02:32:45,371 --> 02:32:52,051
By the fruit of his lips, a man enjoys
good things, but the unfaithful crave

2296
02:32:52,091 --> 02:32:52,991
violence.

2297
02:32:53,391 --> 02:32:56,471
He who guards his mouth guards his soul.

2298
02:32:57,551 --> 02:33:00,451
One who opens wide his lips comes to ruin.

2299
02:33:00,851 --> 02:33:06,871
The soul of the sluggard desires, and has
nothing, but the desire of the diligent shall

2300
02:33:06,911 --> 02:33:07,851
be fully satisfied.

2301
02:33:08,871 --> 02:33:13,851
A righteous man hates lies, but a wicked
man brings shame and disgrace.

2302
02:33:15,151 --> 02:33:20,311
Righteousness guards the way of integrity,
but wickedness overthrows the sinner.

2303
02:33:21,131 --> 02:33:24,591
There are some who pretend to be rich, yet
have nothing.

2304
02:33:25,231 --> 02:33:28,731
There are some who pretend to be poor, yet
have great wealth.

2305
02:33:29,104 --> 02:33:34,524
The ransom of a man’s life is his riches,
but the poor hear no threats.

2306
02:33:35,844 --> 02:33:41,244
The light of the righteous shines brightly, but
the lamp of the wicked is snuffed out.

2307
02:33:42,224 --> 02:33:47,304
Pride only breeds quarrels, but wisdom is
with people who take advice.

2308
02:33:48,324 --> 02:33:54,744
Wealth gained dishonestly dwindles away,
but he who gathers by hand makes it grow.

2309
02:33:56,404 --> 02:34:02,164
Hope deferred makes the heart sick, but when
longing is fulfilled, it is a tree of life.

2310
02:34:02,204 --> 02:34:08,804
Whoever despises instruction will pay for
it, but he who respects a command will

2311
02:34:08,844 --> 02:34:09,744
be rewarded.

2312
02:34:10,184 --> 02:34:15,364
The teaching of the wise is a spring of
life, to turn from the snares of death.

2313
02:34:16,344 --> 02:34:21,364
Good understanding wins favour, but the
way of the unfaithful is hard.

2314
02:34:21,784 --> 02:34:26,484
Every prudent man acts from knowledge, but
a fool exposes folly.

2315
02:34:27,784 --> 02:34:32,984
A wicked messenger falls into trouble, but
a trustworthy envoy gains healing.

2316
02:34:33,744 --> 02:34:40,484
Poverty and shame come to him who
refuses discipline, but he who heeds correction shall

2317
02:34:40,524 --> 02:34:42,044
be honoured.

2318
02:34:42,084 --> 02:34:48,084
Longing fulfilled is sweet to the soul,
but fools detest turning from evil.

2319
02:34:48,524 --> 02:34:54,644
One who walks with wise men grows wise,
but a companion of fools suffers harm.

2320
02:34:55,364 --> 02:34:59,964
Misfortune pursues sinners, but prosperity
rewards the righteous.

2321
02:35:01,164 --> 02:35:06,824
A good man leaves an inheritance to his
children’s children, but the wealth of the sinner

2322
02:35:06,864 --> 02:35:08,464
is stored for the righteous.

2323
02:35:09,004 --> 02:35:14,904
An abundance of food is in poor people’s
fields, but injustice sweeps it away.

2324
02:35:15,544 --> 02:35:21,904
One who spares the rod hates his son, but
one who loves him is careful to discipline

2325
02:35:21,944 --> 02:35:22,844
him.

2326
02:35:23,464 --> 02:35:29,304
The righteous one eats to the satisfying of
his soul, but the belly of the wicked goes

2327
02:35:29,344 --> 02:35:30,244
hungry.

2328
02:35:31,244 --> 02:35:34,084
Proverbs, chapter fourteen.

2329
02:35:34,124 --> 02:35:39,864
Every wise woman builds her house, but the
foolish one tears it down with her own hands.

2330
02:35:41,044 --> 02:35:47,544
He who walks in his uprightness fears the
LORD, but he who is perverse in his ways

2331
02:35:47,584 --> 02:35:48,864
despises him.

2332
02:35:49,264 --> 02:35:54,824
The fool’s talk brings a rod to his back,
but the lips of the wise protect them.

2333
02:35:54,864 --> 02:36:01,344
Where no oxen are, the crib is clean, but
much increase is by the strength of the

2334
02:36:01,384 --> 02:36:02,029
ox.

2335
02:36:02,069 --> 02:36:07,229
A truthful witness will not lie, but a
false witness pours out lies.

2336
02:36:08,389 --> 02:36:14,749
A scoffer seeks wisdom, and doesn’t find
it, but knowledge comes easily to a discerning

2337
02:36:14,789 --> 02:36:15,689
person.

2338
02:36:15,729 --> 02:36:20,429
Stay away from a foolish man, for you
won’t find knowledge on his lips.

2339
02:36:21,229 --> 02:36:27,169
The wisdom of the prudent is to think about
his way, but the folly of fools is deceit.

2340
02:36:28,249 --> 02:36:34,489
Fools mock at making atonement for sins,
but amongst the upright there is good will.

2341
02:36:34,909 --> 02:36:40,009
The heart knows its own bitterness and joy;
he will not share these with a stranger.

2342
02:36:40,969 --> 02:36:46,129
The house of the wicked will be overthrown,
but the tent of the upright will flourish.

2343
02:36:47,289 --> 02:36:52,529
There is a way which seems right to a man,
but in the end it leads to death.

2344
02:36:53,449 --> 02:36:58,869
Even in laughter the heart may be
sorrowful, and mirth may end in heaviness.

2345
02:36:59,269 --> 02:37:04,969
The unfaithful will be repaid for his own
ways; likewise a good man will be rewarded

2346
02:37:05,009 --> 02:37:05,909
for his ways.

2347
02:37:07,169 --> 02:37:12,929
A simple man believes everything, but the
prudent man carefully considers his ways.

2348
02:37:14,129 --> 02:37:19,449
A wise man fears and shuns evil, but the
fool is hot headed and reckless.

2349
02:37:20,149 --> 02:37:25,429
He who is quick to become angry will
commit folly, and a crafty man is hated.

2350
02:37:26,069 --> 02:37:30,469
The simple inherit folly, but the prudent
are crowned with knowledge.

2351
02:37:31,569 --> 02:37:36,089
The evil bow down before the good, and the
wicked at the gates of the righteous.

2352
02:37:37,329 --> 02:37:42,949
The poor person is shunned even by his
own neighbour, but the rich person has many friends.

2353
02:37:43,809 --> 02:37:49,329
He who despises his neighbour sins, but he
who has pity on the poor is blessed.

2354
02:37:50,529 --> 02:37:52,869
Don’t they go astray who plot evil?

2355
02:37:53,909 --> 02:37:57,329
But love and faithfulness belong to those
who plan good.

2356
02:37:57,789 --> 02:38:03,309
In all hard work there is profit, but the
talk of the lips leads only to poverty.

2357
02:38:04,069 --> 02:38:09,309
The crown of the wise is their riches, but
the folly of fools crowns them with folly.

2358
02:38:10,649 --> 02:38:15,309
A truthful witness saves souls, but a
false witness is deceitful.

2359
02:38:15,589 --> 02:38:21,149
In the fear of the LORD is a secure
fortress, and he will be a refuge for his children.

2360
02:38:21,889 --> 02:38:27,349
The fear of the LORD is a fountain
of life, turning people from the snares of death.

2361
02:38:27,868 --> 02:38:33,868
In the multitude of people is the king’s glory,
but in the lack of people is the destruction

2362
02:38:33,908 --> 02:38:34,808
of the prince.

2363
02:38:35,988 --> 02:38:42,628
He who is slow to anger has great
understanding, but he who has a quick temper displays

2364
02:38:42,668 --> 02:38:43,568
folly.

2365
02:38:43,668 --> 02:38:48,508
The life of the body is a heart at peace,
but envy rots the bones.

2366
02:38:49,348 --> 02:38:56,008
He who oppresses the poor shows contempt for his
Maker, but he who is kind to the needy

2367
02:38:56,048 --> 02:38:56,948
honours him.

2368
02:38:58,148 --> 02:39:03,888
The wicked is brought down in his calamity,
but in death, the righteous has a refuge.

2369
02:39:04,488 --> 02:39:10,608
Wisdom rests in the heart of one who
has understanding, and is even made known in the

2370
02:39:10,648 --> 02:39:11,868
inward part of fools.

2371
02:39:12,688 --> 02:39:18,108
Righteousness exalts a nation, but sin is
a disgrace to any people.

2372
02:39:19,108 --> 02:39:25,708
The king’s favour is towards a servant who
deals wisely, but his wrath is towards one

2373
02:39:25,748 --> 02:39:26,828
who causes shame.

2374
02:39:27,408 --> 02:39:30,448
Proverbs, chapter fifteen.

2375
02:39:30,488 --> 02:39:35,388
A gentle answer turns away wrath, but a
harsh word stirs up anger.

2376
02:39:35,818 --> 02:39:41,668
The tongue of the wise commends knowledge,
but the mouths of fools gush out folly.

2377
02:39:43,088 --> 02:39:47,668
The LORD’s eyes are everywhere, keeping
watch on the evil and the good.

2378
02:39:48,828 --> 02:39:53,888
A gentle tongue is a tree of life, but
deceit in it crushes the spirit.

2379
02:39:54,568 --> 02:40:00,788
A fool despises his father’s correction,
but he who heeds reproof shows prudence.

2380
02:40:01,508 --> 02:40:07,488
In the house of the righteous is much
treasure, but the income of the wicked brings trouble.

2381
02:40:08,568 --> 02:40:13,248
The lips of the wise spread knowledge; not
so with the heart of fools.

2382
02:40:14,088 --> 02:40:20,088
The sacrifice made by the wicked is an
abomination to the LORD, but the prayer of the

2383
02:40:20,128 --> 02:40:21,428
upright is his delight.

2384
02:40:22,568 --> 02:40:28,688
The way of the wicked is an abomination to
the LORD, but he loves him who follows after

2385
02:40:28,728 --> 02:40:29,628
righteousness.

2386
02:40:30,408 --> 02:40:33,708
There is stern discipline for one who
forsakes the way.

2387
02:40:34,228 --> 02:40:36,428
Whoever hates reproof shall die.

2388
02:40:36,468 --> 02:40:43,128
Sheol and Abaddon are before the LORD— how
much more then the hearts of

2389
02:40:43,168 --> 02:40:44,168
the children of men!

2390
02:40:45,468 --> 02:40:50,028
A scoffer doesn’t love to be reproved; he
will not go to the wise.

2391
02:40:50,668 --> 02:40:55,708
A glad heart makes a cheerful face, but an
aching heart breaks the spirit.

2392
02:40:56,103 --> 02:41:02,423
The heart of one who has understanding
seeks knowledge, but the mouths of fools feed

2393
02:41:02,463 --> 02:41:03,363
on folly.

2394
02:41:04,143 --> 02:41:10,963
All the days of the afflicted are wretched,
but one who has a cheerful heart enjoys a

2395
02:41:11,003 --> 02:41:11,983
continual feast.

2396
02:41:12,023 --> 02:41:17,463
Better is little, with the fear of the
LORD, than great treasure with trouble.

2397
02:41:18,123 --> 02:41:23,843
Better is a dinner of herbs, where love
is, than a fattened calf with hatred.

2398
02:41:25,223 --> 02:41:31,723
A wrathful man stirs up contention, but
one who is slow to anger appeases strife.

2399
02:41:32,383 --> 02:41:37,663
The way of the sluggard is like a thorn
patch, but the path of the upright is a highway.

2400
02:41:38,443 --> 02:41:43,863
A wise son makes a father glad, but a
foolish man despises his mother.

2401
02:41:44,883 --> 02:41:51,483
Folly is joy to one who is void of
wisdom, but a man of understanding keeps his way straight.

2402
02:41:51,863 --> 02:41:57,923
Where there is no counsel, plans fail; but
in a multitude of counsellors they are established.

2403
02:41:59,083 --> 02:42:02,223
Joy comes to a man with the reply of his
mouth.

2404
02:42:03,223 --> 02:42:05,563
How good is a word at the right time!

2405
02:42:06,263 --> 02:42:12,663
The path of life leads upward for the
wise, to keep him from going downward to Sheol.

2406
02:42:12,703 --> 02:42:18,583
The LORD will uproot the house of the
proud, but he will keep the widow’s borders intact.

2407
02:42:19,383 --> 02:42:24,403
The LORD detests the thoughts of the wicked,
but the thoughts of the pure are pleasing.

2408
02:42:25,783 --> 02:42:31,763
He who is greedy for gain troubles his own
house, but he who hates bribes will live.

2409
02:42:31,803 --> 02:42:37,343
The heart of the righteous weighs answers, but
the mouth of the wicked gushes out evil.

2410
02:42:37,383 --> 02:42:42,283
The LORD is far from the wicked, but he
hears the prayer of the righteous.

2411
02:42:43,563 --> 02:42:45,923
The light of the eyes rejoices the heart.

2412
02:42:46,943 --> 02:42:49,203
Good news gives health to the bones.

2413
02:42:50,303 --> 02:42:55,363
The ear that listens to reproof lives, and
will be at home amongst the wise.

2414
02:42:56,183 --> 02:43:02,803
He who refuses correction despises his own
soul, but he who listens to reproof gets

2415
02:43:02,843 --> 02:43:03,743
understanding.

2416
02:43:04,403 --> 02:43:06,923
The fear of the LORD teaches wisdom.

2417
02:43:06,963 --> 02:43:09,243
Before honour is humility.

2418
02:43:09,863 --> 02:43:12,763
Proverbs, chapter sixteen.

2419
02:43:12,803 --> 02:43:18,203
The plans of the heart belong to man, but
the answer of the tongue is from the LORD.

2420
02:43:18,943 --> 02:43:24,243
All the ways of a man are clean in his own
eyes, but the LORD weighs the motives.

2421
02:43:24,723 --> 02:43:28,863
Commit your deeds to the LORD, and your
plans shall succeed.

2422
02:43:30,343 --> 02:43:36,823
The LORD has made everything for its own end—
yes, even the wicked for the day of evil.

2423
02:43:37,743 --> 02:43:43,963
Everyone who is proud in heart is an
abomination to the LORD; they shall certainly not

2424
02:43:44,003 --> 02:43:44,943
be unpunished.

2425
02:43:44,983 --> 02:43:48,383
By mercy and truth iniquity is atoned for.

2426
02:43:48,423 --> 02:43:51,643
By the fear of the LORD men depart from
evil.

2427
02:43:52,303 --> 02:43:58,323
When a man’s ways please the LORD, he makes
even his enemies to be at peace with him.

2428
02:43:59,303 --> 02:44:04,723
Better is a little with righteousness,
than great revenues with injustice.

2429
02:44:04,763 --> 02:44:08,903
A man’s heart plans his course, but the
LORD directs his steps.

2430
02:44:10,223 --> 02:44:12,423
Inspired judgements are on the lips of the
king.

2431
02:44:13,323 --> 02:44:14,963
He shall not betray his mouth.

2432
02:44:16,583 --> 02:44:21,863
Honest balances and scales are the LORD’s;
all the weights in the bag are his work.

2433
02:44:22,383 --> 02:44:28,043
It is an abomination for kings to do
wrong, for the throne is established by righteousness.

2434
02:44:29,203 --> 02:44:31,443
Righteous lips are the delight of kings.

2435
02:44:32,303 --> 02:44:34,523
They value one who speaks the truth.

2436
02:44:35,683 --> 02:44:41,003
The king’s wrath is a messenger of death,
but a wise man will pacify it.

2437
02:44:42,083 --> 02:44:44,163
In the light of the king’s face is life.

2438
02:44:45,283 --> 02:44:47,903
His favour is like a cloud of the spring
rain.

2439
02:44:48,663 --> 02:44:51,823
How much better it is to get wisdom than
gold!

2440
02:44:52,523 --> 02:44:56,523
Yes, to get understanding is to be chosen
rather than silver.

2441
02:44:57,763 --> 02:45:00,563
The highway of the upright is to depart
from evil.

2442
02:45:01,663 --> 02:45:04,263
He who keeps his way preserves his soul.

2443
02:45:05,223 --> 02:45:09,883
Pride goes before destruction, and an
arrogant spirit before a fall.

2444
02:45:10,603 --> 02:45:15,963
It is better to be of a lowly spirit
with the poor, than to divide the plunder with the

2445
02:45:16,003 --> 02:45:16,903
proud.

2446
02:45:17,143 --> 02:45:20,083
He who heeds the Word finds prosperity.

2447
02:45:21,103 --> 02:45:23,203
Whoever trusts in the LORD is blessed.

2448
02:45:24,363 --> 02:45:26,463
The wise in heart shall be called prudent.

2449
02:45:27,543 --> 02:45:29,623
Pleasantness of the lips promotes
instruction.

2450
02:45:30,723 --> 02:45:36,603
Understanding is a fountain of life to one
who has it, but the punishment of fools is

2451
02:45:36,643 --> 02:45:37,543
their folly.

2452
02:45:38,203 --> 02:45:42,743
The heart of the wise instructs his mouth,
and adds learning to his lips.

2453
02:45:43,623 --> 02:45:48,743
Pleasant words are a honeycomb, sweet to
the soul, and health to the bones.

2454
02:45:49,213 --> 02:45:54,873
There is a way which seems right to a man,
but in the end it leads to death.

2455
02:45:56,133 --> 02:46:02,453
The appetite of the labouring man labours
for him, for his mouth urges him on.

2456
02:46:02,993 --> 02:46:04,853
A worthless man devises mischief.

2457
02:46:06,013 --> 02:46:08,113
His speech is like a scorching fire.

2458
02:46:09,213 --> 02:46:11,173
A perverse man stirs up strife.

2459
02:46:12,293 --> 02:46:14,333
A whisperer separates close friends.

2460
02:46:15,113 --> 02:46:20,373
A man of violence entices his neighbour,
and leads him in a way that is not good.

2461
02:46:21,493 --> 02:46:28,093
One who winks his eyes to plot perversities,
one who compresses his lips, is bent on

2462
02:46:28,133 --> 02:46:28,433
evil.

2463
02:46:28,473 --> 02:46:30,693
Grey hair is a crown of glory.

2464
02:46:31,573 --> 02:46:33,513
It is attained by a life of righteousness.

2465
02:46:34,733 --> 02:46:41,313
One who is slow to anger is better than
the mighty; one who rules his spirit, than

2466
02:46:41,353 --> 02:46:42,633
he who takes a city.

2467
02:46:43,653 --> 02:46:48,593
The lot is cast into the lap, but its
every decision is from the LORD.

2468
02:46:49,653 --> 02:46:52,073
Proverbs, chapter seventeen.

2469
02:46:52,113 --> 02:46:57,273
Better is a dry morsel with quietness,
than a house full of feasting with strife.

2470
02:46:58,153 --> 02:47:04,653
A servant who deals wisely will rule over
a son who causes shame, and shall have

2471
02:47:04,693 --> 02:47:07,033
a part in the inheritance amongst the
brothers.

2472
02:47:07,893 --> 02:47:14,433
The refining pot is for silver, and the
furnace for gold, but the LORD tests the

2473
02:47:14,473 --> 02:47:15,213
hearts.

2474
02:47:15,253 --> 02:47:17,213
An evildoer heeds wicked lips.

2475
02:47:18,133 --> 02:47:20,673
A liar gives ear to a mischievous tongue.

2476
02:47:21,293 --> 02:47:23,973
Whoever mocks the poor reproaches his
Maker.

2477
02:47:25,173 --> 02:47:28,973
He who is glad at calamity shall not be
unpunished.

2478
02:47:29,933 --> 02:47:35,473
Children’s children are the crown of old
men; the glory of children is their parents.

2479
02:47:36,373 --> 02:47:41,873
Excellent speech isn’t fitting for a fool,
much less do lying lips fit a prince.

2480
02:47:42,653 --> 02:47:49,093
A bribe is a precious stone in the eyes
of him who gives it; wherever he turns, he prospers.

2481
02:47:50,093 --> 02:47:56,453
He who covers an offence promotes love; but
he who repeats a matter separates best friends.

2482
02:47:57,033 --> 02:48:03,113
A rebuke enters deeper into one who has
understanding than a hundred lashes into a fool.

2483
02:48:03,853 --> 02:48:10,133
An evil man seeks only rebellion; therefore
a cruel messenger shall be sent against him.

2484
02:48:11,173 --> 02:48:16,253
Let a bear robbed of her cubs meet a man,
rather than a fool in his folly.

2485
02:48:17,333 --> 02:48:21,893
Whoever rewards evil for good, evil shall
not depart from his house.

2486
02:48:22,302 --> 02:48:29,442
The beginning of strife is like breaching
a dam, therefore stop contention before quarrelling

2487
02:48:29,482 --> 02:48:30,382
breaks out.

2488
02:48:31,502 --> 02:48:38,322
He who justifies the wicked, and he who
condemns the righteous, both of them alike are

2489
02:48:38,362 --> 02:48:39,902
an abomination to the LORD.

2490
02:48:40,602 --> 02:48:46,222
Why is there money in the hand of a
fool to buy wisdom, since he has no understanding?

2491
02:48:47,162 --> 02:48:51,822
A friend loves at all times; and a brother
is born for adversity.

2492
02:48:52,302 --> 02:48:58,362
A man void of understanding strikes hands,
and becomes collateral in the presence of

2493
02:48:58,402 --> 02:49:00,202
his neighbour.

2494
02:49:00,242 --> 02:49:02,902
He who loves disobedience loves strife.

2495
02:49:03,822 --> 02:49:06,562
One who builds a high gate seeks
destruction.

2496
02:49:07,622 --> 02:49:14,102
One who has a perverse heart doesn’t find
prosperity, and one who has a deceitful

2497
02:49:14,142 --> 02:49:15,722
tongue falls into trouble.

2498
02:49:16,602 --> 02:49:19,822
He who becomes the father of a fool
grieves.

2499
02:49:20,422 --> 02:49:22,582
The father of a fool has no joy.

2500
02:49:23,282 --> 02:49:28,642
A cheerful heart makes good medicine, but
a crushed spirit dries up the bones.

2501
02:49:29,822 --> 02:49:34,822
A wicked man receives a bribe in secret,
to pervert the ways of justice.

2502
02:49:36,122 --> 02:49:42,262
Wisdom is before the face of one who
has understanding, but the eyes of a fool wander

2503
02:49:42,302 --> 02:49:43,722
to the ends of the earth.

2504
02:49:44,422 --> 02:49:49,682
A foolish son brings grief to his father,
and bitterness to her who bore him.

2505
02:49:50,482 --> 02:49:56,702
Also to punish the righteous is not good,
nor to flog officials for their integrity.

2506
02:49:57,942 --> 02:50:00,202
He who spares his words has knowledge.

2507
02:50:01,282 --> 02:50:03,842
He who is even tempered is a man of
understanding.

2508
02:50:04,842 --> 02:50:08,762
Even a fool, when he keeps silent, is
counted wise.

2509
02:50:09,902 --> 02:50:13,182
When he shuts his lips, he is thought to
be discerning.

2510
02:50:14,242 --> 02:50:16,602
Proverbs, chapter eighteen.

2511
02:50:16,642 --> 02:50:23,582
A man who isolates himself pursues
selfishness, and defies all sound judgement.

2512
02:50:23,622 --> 02:50:29,042
A fool has no delight in understanding,
but only in revealing his own opinion.

2513
02:50:29,902 --> 02:50:35,062
When wickedness comes, contempt also
comes, and with shame comes disgrace.

2514
02:50:35,102 --> 02:50:39,322
The words of a man’s mouth are like deep
waters.

2515
02:50:40,262 --> 02:50:43,222
The fountain of wisdom is like a flowing
brook.

2516
02:50:43,922 --> 02:50:49,762
To be partial to the faces of the wicked
is not good, nor to deprive the innocent of

2517
02:50:49,802 --> 02:50:50,702
justice.

2518
02:50:51,042 --> 02:50:55,662
A fool’s lips come into strife, and his
mouth invites beatings.

2519
02:50:55,957 --> 02:51:01,917
A fool’s mouth is his destruction, and his
lips are a snare to his soul.

2520
02:51:03,157 --> 02:51:09,597
The words of a gossip are like dainty
morsels: they go down into a person’s innermost

2521
02:51:09,637 --> 02:51:10,517
parts.

2522
02:51:10,557 --> 02:51:16,177
One who is slack in his work is brother to
him who is a master of destruction.

2523
02:51:17,097 --> 02:51:22,457
The LORD’s name is a strong tower: the
righteous run to him, and are safe.

2524
02:51:23,097 --> 02:51:29,737
The rich man’s wealth is his strong city,
like an unscalable wall in his own imagination.

2525
02:51:31,117 --> 02:51:36,357
Before destruction the heart of man is
proud, but before honour is humility.

2526
02:51:37,317 --> 02:51:42,037
He who answers before he hears, that is
folly and shame to him.

2527
02:51:42,937 --> 02:51:48,737
A man’s spirit will sustain him in
sickness, but a crushed spirit, who can bear?

2528
02:51:48,777 --> 02:51:51,237
The heart of the discerning gets
knowledge.

2529
02:51:52,137 --> 02:51:54,457
The ear of the wise seeks knowledge.

2530
02:51:55,417 --> 02:52:00,137
A man’s gift makes room for him, and
brings him before great men.

2531
02:52:00,737 --> 02:52:07,037
He who pleads his cause first seems right—
until another comes and questions him.

2532
02:52:07,457 --> 02:52:11,417
The lot settles disputes, and keeps strong
ones apart.

2533
02:52:11,917 --> 02:52:15,837
A brother offended is more difficult than
a fortified city.

2534
02:52:17,037 --> 02:52:19,157
Disputes are like the bars of a fortress.

2535
02:52:20,597 --> 02:52:23,737
A man’s stomach is filled with the fruit
of his mouth.

2536
02:52:24,277 --> 02:52:26,777
With the harvest of his lips he is
satisfied.

2537
02:52:28,097 --> 02:52:34,037
Death and life are in the power of the
tongue; those who love it will eat its fruit.

2538
02:52:35,157 --> 02:52:40,317
Whoever finds a wife finds a good thing,
and obtains favour of the LORD.

2539
02:52:40,777 --> 02:52:44,737
The poor plead for mercy, but the rich
answer harshly.

2540
02:52:45,537 --> 02:52:51,677
A man of many companions may be ruined,
but there is a friend who sticks closer than

2541
02:52:51,717 --> 02:52:52,617
a brother.

2542
02:52:53,297 --> 02:52:55,977
Proverbs, chapter nineteen.

2543
02:52:56,017 --> 02:53:02,577
Better is the poor who walks in his integrity
than he who is perverse in his lips and

2544
02:53:02,617 --> 02:53:03,517
is a fool.

2545
02:53:03,677 --> 02:53:10,077
It isn’t good to have zeal without knowledge,
nor being hasty with one’s feet and missing

2546
02:53:10,117 --> 02:53:11,017
the way.

2547
02:53:11,717 --> 02:53:17,257
The foolishness of man subverts his way;
his heart rages against the LORD.

2548
02:53:17,757 --> 02:53:22,317
Wealth adds many friends, but the poor is
separated from his friend.

2549
02:53:23,437 --> 02:53:26,037
A false witness shall not be unpunished.

2550
02:53:26,077 --> 02:53:29,697
He who pours out lies shall not go free.

2551
02:53:30,145 --> 02:53:36,285
Many will entreat the favour of a ruler, and
everyone is a friend to a man who gives

2552
02:53:36,325 --> 02:53:37,225
gifts.

2553
02:53:37,865 --> 02:53:43,625
All the relatives of the poor shun him;
how much more do his friends avoid him!

2554
02:53:43,985 --> 02:53:46,965
He pursues them with pleas, but they are
gone.

2555
02:53:48,165 --> 02:53:50,785
He who gets wisdom loves his own soul.

2556
02:53:51,505 --> 02:53:54,025
He who keeps understanding shall find
good.

2557
02:53:55,105 --> 02:53:57,745
A false witness shall not be unpunished.

2558
02:53:58,645 --> 02:54:00,945
He who utters lies shall perish.

2559
02:54:01,965 --> 02:54:08,305
Delicate living is not appropriate for a fool,
much less for a servant to have rule over

2560
02:54:08,345 --> 02:54:09,245
princes.

2561
02:54:09,425 --> 02:54:12,265
The discretion of a man makes him slow to
anger.

2562
02:54:13,065 --> 02:54:16,405
It is his glory to overlook an offence.

2563
02:54:16,445 --> 02:54:22,365
The king’s wrath is like the roaring of a
lion, but his favour is like dew on the grass.

2564
02:54:23,465 --> 02:54:25,965
A foolish son is the calamity of his
father.

2565
02:54:26,775 --> 02:54:29,465
A wife’s quarrels are a continual
dripping.

2566
02:54:30,245 --> 02:54:36,045
House and riches are an inheritance from fathers,
but a prudent wife is from the LORD.

2567
02:54:37,585 --> 02:54:40,065
Slothfulness casts into a deep sleep.

2568
02:54:41,145 --> 02:54:43,085
The idle soul shall suffer hunger.

2569
02:54:43,665 --> 02:54:49,825
He who keeps the commandment keeps his soul,
but he who is contemptuous in his ways shall

2570
02:54:49,865 --> 02:54:50,765
die.

2571
02:54:50,945 --> 02:54:55,705
He who has pity on the poor lends to the
LORD; he will reward him.

2572
02:54:56,485 --> 02:55:01,925
Discipline your son, for there is hope;
don’t be a willing party to his death.

2573
02:55:02,945 --> 02:55:08,785
A hot-tempered man must pay the penalty, for
if you rescue him, you must do it again.

2574
02:55:09,465 --> 02:55:15,085
Listen to counsel and receive instruction,
that you may be wise in your latter end.

2575
02:55:15,985 --> 02:55:20,985
There are many plans in a man’s heart, but
the LORD’s counsel will prevail.

2576
02:55:21,805 --> 02:55:25,325
That which makes a man to be desired is
his kindness.

2577
02:55:26,505 --> 02:55:28,365
A poor man is better than a liar.

2578
02:55:29,085 --> 02:55:35,425
The fear of the LORD leads to life,
then contentment; he rests and will not be touched

2579
02:55:35,465 --> 02:55:36,365
by trouble.

2580
02:55:37,265 --> 02:55:42,625
The sluggard buries his hand in the dish; he
will not so much as bring it to his mouth

2581
02:55:42,665 --> 02:55:43,565
again.

2582
02:55:43,985 --> 02:55:49,585
Flog a scoffer, and the simple will
learn prudence; rebuke one who has understanding,

2583
02:55:49,625 --> 02:55:52,125
and he will gain knowledge.

2584
02:55:53,145 --> 02:55:59,645
He who robs his father and drives away his
mother is a son who causes shame and brings

2585
02:55:59,685 --> 02:56:00,585
reproach.

2586
02:56:00,722 --> 02:56:06,202
If you stop listening to instruction, my son,
you will stray from the words of knowledge.

2587
02:56:07,282 --> 02:56:13,162
A corrupt witness mocks justice, and the
mouth of the wicked gulps down iniquity.

2588
02:56:14,242 --> 02:56:18,902
Penalties are prepared for scoffers, and
beatings for the backs of fools.

2589
02:56:20,402 --> 02:56:22,842
Proverbs, chapter twenty.

2590
02:56:22,882 --> 02:56:25,202
Wine is a mocker and beer is a brawler.

2591
02:56:25,962 --> 02:56:28,962
Whoever is led astray by them is not wise.

2592
02:56:29,962 --> 02:56:33,182
The terror of a king is like the roaring
of a lion.

2593
02:56:34,282 --> 02:56:37,642
He who provokes him to anger forfeits his
own life.

2594
02:56:38,102 --> 02:56:43,982
It is an honour for a man to keep
aloof from strife, but every fool will be quarrelling.

2595
02:56:44,562 --> 02:56:49,762
The sluggard will not plough by reason of
the winter; therefore he shall beg in harvest,

2596
02:56:49,802 --> 02:56:51,162
and have nothing.

2597
02:56:51,862 --> 02:56:57,722
Counsel in the heart of man is like
deep water, but a man of understanding will draw

2598
02:56:57,762 --> 02:56:58,662
it out.

2599
02:56:59,202 --> 02:57:04,542
Many men claim to be men of unfailing
love, but who can find a faithful man?

2600
02:57:05,202 --> 02:57:07,262
A righteous man walks in integrity.

2601
02:57:08,362 --> 02:57:10,402
Blessed are his children after him.

2602
02:57:11,342 --> 02:57:17,102
A king who sits on the throne of judgement
scatters away all evil with his eyes.

2603
02:57:17,742 --> 02:57:21,182
Who can say, “I have made my heart pure.

2604
02:57:21,802 --> 02:57:23,542
I am clean and without sin?”

2605
02:57:24,202 --> 02:57:29,542
Differing weights and differing measures, both of
them alike are an abomination to the

2606
02:57:29,582 --> 02:57:30,482
LORD.

2607
02:57:30,842 --> 02:57:36,982
Even a child makes himself known by his
doings, whether his work is pure, and whether

2608
02:57:37,022 --> 02:57:37,922
it is right.

2609
02:57:38,842 --> 02:57:43,742
The hearing ear, and the seeing eye, The
LORD has made even both of them.

2610
02:57:43,782 --> 02:57:47,142
Don’t love sleep, lest you come to
poverty.

2611
02:57:48,242 --> 02:57:51,722
Open your eyes, and you shall be satisfied
with bread.

2612
02:57:52,702 --> 02:57:59,162
“It’s no good, it’s no good,” says the
buyer; but when he is gone his way, then

2613
02:57:59,202 --> 02:58:00,102
he boasts.

2614
02:58:00,362 --> 02:58:05,462
There is gold and abundance of rubies, but
the lips of knowledge are a rare jewel.

2615
02:58:06,282 --> 02:58:11,782
Take the garment of one who puts up
collateral for a stranger; and hold him in pledge

2616
02:58:11,822 --> 02:58:13,182
for a wayward woman.

2617
02:58:13,222 --> 02:58:19,802
Fraudulent food is sweet to a man,
but afterwards his mouth is filled with gravel.

2618
02:58:20,402 --> 02:58:25,222
Plans are established by advice; by wise
guidance you wage war!

2619
02:58:25,615 --> 02:58:32,255
He who goes about as a tale-bearer reveals
secrets; therefore don’t keep company with

2620
02:58:32,295 --> 02:58:34,295
him who opens wide his lips.

2621
02:58:35,535 --> 02:58:41,675
Whoever curses his father or his mother, his
lamp shall be put out in blackness of darkness.

2622
02:58:42,295 --> 02:58:46,835
An inheritance quickly gained at the
beginning won’t be blessed in the end.

2623
02:58:47,675 --> 02:58:49,855
Don’t say, “I will pay back evil.”

2624
02:58:50,815 --> 02:58:53,375
Wait for the LORD, and he will save you.

2625
02:58:54,175 --> 02:58:59,495
The LORD detests differing weights, and
dishonest scales are not pleasing.

2626
02:59:00,795 --> 02:59:05,955
A man’s steps are from the LORD; how then
can man understand his way?

2627
02:59:06,615 --> 02:59:12,395
It is a snare to a man to make
a rash dedication, then later to consider his vows.

2628
02:59:13,555 --> 02:59:18,535
A wise king winnows out the wicked, and
drives the threshing wheel over them.

2629
02:59:19,245 --> 02:59:24,555
The spirit of man is the LORD’s lamp,
searching all his innermost parts.

2630
02:59:25,115 --> 02:59:27,715
Love and faithfulness keep the king safe.

2631
02:59:28,455 --> 02:59:30,375
His throne is sustained by love.

2632
02:59:31,615 --> 02:59:33,595
The glory of young men is their strength.

2633
02:59:34,875 --> 02:59:37,395
The splendour of old men is their grey
hair.

2634
02:59:38,495 --> 02:59:43,795
Wounding blows cleanse away evil, and
beatings purge the innermost parts.

2635
02:59:44,335 --> 02:59:46,915
Proverbs, chapter twenty-one.

2636
02:59:46,955 --> 02:59:50,875
The king’s heart is in the LORD’s hand
like the watercourses.

2637
02:59:51,535 --> 02:59:53,275
He turns it wherever he desires.

2638
02:59:54,495 --> 02:59:59,635
Every way of a man is right in his own
eyes, but the LORD weighs the hearts.

2639
03:00:00,595 --> 03:00:04,935
To do righteousness and justice is more
acceptable to the LORD than sacrifice.

2640
03:00:05,635 --> 03:00:10,275
A high look and a proud heart, the lamp of
the wicked, is sin.

2641
03:00:10,855 --> 03:00:17,015
The plans of the diligent surely lead to
profit; and everyone who is hasty surely rushes

2642
03:00:17,055 --> 03:00:17,955
to poverty.

2643
03:00:18,915 --> 03:00:23,875
Getting treasures by a lying tongue is a
fleeting vapour for those who seek death.

2644
03:00:24,375 --> 03:00:29,775
The violence of the wicked will drive them
away, because they refuse to do what is right.

2645
03:00:30,475 --> 03:00:35,115
The way of the guilty is devious, but the
conduct of the innocent is upright.

2646
03:00:36,135 --> 03:00:41,255
It is better to dwell in the corner of
the housetop than to share a house with a contentious

2647
03:00:41,295 --> 03:00:41,915
woman.

2648
03:00:41,955 --> 03:00:47,575
The soul of the wicked desires evil; his
neighbour finds no mercy in his eyes.

2649
03:00:48,021 --> 03:00:51,421
When the mocker is punished, the simple
gains wisdom.

2650
03:00:52,541 --> 03:00:55,941
When the wise is instructed, he receives
knowledge.

2651
03:00:56,981 --> 03:01:02,101
The Righteous One considers the house of
the wicked, and brings the wicked to ruin.

2652
03:01:02,401 --> 03:01:08,761
Whoever stops his ears at the cry of the
poor, he will also cry out, but shall not be

2653
03:01:08,801 --> 03:01:09,641
heard.

2654
03:01:09,681 --> 03:01:15,421
A gift in secret pacifies anger, and a
bribe in the cloak, strong wrath.

2655
03:01:16,201 --> 03:01:22,741
It is joy to the righteous to do justice;
but it is a destruction to the workers of iniquity.

2656
03:01:23,001 --> 03:01:28,381
The man who wanders out of the way
of understanding shall rest in the assembly of the

2657
03:01:28,421 --> 03:01:29,321
departed spirits.

2658
03:01:30,221 --> 03:01:32,861
He who loves pleasure will be a poor man.

2659
03:01:33,641 --> 03:01:36,981
He who loves wine and oil won’t be rich.

2660
03:01:37,881 --> 03:01:42,201
The wicked is a ransom for the righteous,
the treacherous for the upright.

2661
03:01:42,941 --> 03:01:48,381
It is better to dwell in a desert land,
than with a contentious and fretful woman.

2662
03:01:49,061 --> 03:01:55,281
There is precious treasure and oil in the
dwelling of the wise, but a foolish man swallows

2663
03:01:55,321 --> 03:01:56,221
it up.

2664
03:01:56,561 --> 03:02:03,641
He who follows after righteousness and
kindness finds life, righteousness, and honour.

2665
03:02:03,681 --> 03:02:09,421
A wise man scales the city of the
mighty, and brings down the strength of its confidence.

2666
03:02:10,081 --> 03:02:14,621
Whoever guards his mouth and his tongue
keeps his soul from troubles.

2667
03:02:15,681 --> 03:02:21,861
The proud and arrogant man—“Scoffer” is his
name— he works in the arrogance of pride.

2668
03:02:23,001 --> 03:02:28,421
The desire of the sluggard kills him, for
his hands refuse to labour.

2669
03:02:28,461 --> 03:02:34,001
There are those who covet greedily all day
long; but the righteous give and don’t withhold.

2670
03:02:35,041 --> 03:02:41,161
The sacrifice of the wicked is an abomination—
how much more, when he brings it with

2671
03:02:41,201 --> 03:02:42,101
a wicked mind!

2672
03:02:42,651 --> 03:02:44,861
A false witness will perish.

2673
03:02:45,361 --> 03:02:47,901
A man who listens speaks to eternity.

2674
03:02:49,001 --> 03:02:54,901
A wicked man hardens his face; but as for
the upright, he establishes his ways.

2675
03:02:55,801 --> 03:02:59,821
There is no wisdom nor understanding nor
counsel against the LORD.

2676
03:03:00,881 --> 03:03:05,421
The horse is prepared for the day of
battle; but victory is with the LORD.

2677
03:03:06,621 --> 03:03:07,761
Proverbs, chapter twenty-two.

2678
03:03:08,981 --> 03:03:15,201
A good name is more desirable than great
riches, and loving favour is better than silver

2679
03:03:15,241 --> 03:03:16,141
and gold.

2680
03:03:17,161 --> 03:03:22,741
The rich and the poor have this in common:
The LORD is the maker of them all.

2681
03:03:23,881 --> 03:03:30,681
A prudent man sees danger and hides himself;
but the simple pass on, and suffer for

2682
03:03:30,721 --> 03:03:31,261
it.

2683
03:03:31,301 --> 03:03:37,041
The result of humility and the fear of the
LORD is wealth, honour, and life.

2684
03:03:38,241 --> 03:03:44,201
Thorns and snares are in the path of
the wicked; whoever guards his soul stays from them.

2685
03:03:44,621 --> 03:03:50,121
Train up a child in the way he should go,
and when he is old he will not depart from

2686
03:03:50,161 --> 03:03:51,061
it.

2687
03:03:51,261 --> 03:03:52,981
The rich rule over the poor.

2688
03:03:53,621 --> 03:03:55,561
The borrower is servant to the lender.

2689
03:03:56,701 --> 03:04:01,941
He who sows wickedness reaps trouble, and
the rod of his fury will be destroyed.

2690
03:04:02,581 --> 03:04:08,321
He who has a generous eye will be blessed,
for he shares his food with the poor.

2691
03:04:08,741 --> 03:04:15,401
Drive out the mocker, and strife will go
out; yes, quarrels and insults will stop.

2692
03:04:16,101 --> 03:04:21,261
He who loves purity of heart and speaks
gracefully is the king’s friend.

2693
03:04:22,441 --> 03:04:28,121
The LORD’s eyes watch over knowledge, but
he frustrates the words of the unfaithful.

2694
03:04:29,041 --> 03:04:31,801
The sluggard says, “There is a lion
outside!

2695
03:04:32,821 --> 03:04:34,321
I will be killed in the streets!”

2696
03:04:34,921 --> 03:04:37,381
The mouth of an adulteress is a deep pit.

2697
03:04:38,001 --> 03:04:41,321
He who is under the LORD’s wrath will fall
into it.

2698
03:04:42,161 --> 03:04:48,201
Folly is bound up in the heart of a
child; the rod of discipline drives it far from him.

2699
03:04:48,581 --> 03:04:54,841
Whoever oppresses the poor for his own increase
and whoever gives to the rich, both come

2700
03:04:54,881 --> 03:04:55,781
to poverty.

2701
03:04:56,681 --> 03:04:59,961
Turn your ear, and listen to the words of
the wise.

2702
03:05:00,721 --> 03:05:02,361
Apply your heart to my teaching.

2703
03:05:03,481 --> 03:05:08,921
For it is a pleasant thing if you keep them
within you, if all of them are ready on your

2704
03:05:08,961 --> 03:05:09,861
lips.

2705
03:05:10,341 --> 03:05:15,441
I teach you today, even you, so that your
trust may be in the LORD.

2706
03:05:16,121 --> 03:05:23,401
Haven’t I written to

2707
03:05:23,441 --> 03:05:23,741
you thirty excellent things of counsel and
knowledge, To teach you truth, reliable words,

2708
03:05:23,781 --> 03:05:27,001
to give sound answers to the ones who sent
you?

2709
03:05:27,284 --> 03:05:33,964
Don’t exploit the poor because he is poor;
and don’t crush the needy in court; for

2710
03:05:34,004 --> 03:05:38,864
the LORD will plead their case, and
plunder the life of those who plunder them.

2711
03:05:39,704 --> 03:05:42,084
Don’t befriend a hot-tempered man.

2712
03:05:42,404 --> 03:05:48,424
Don’t associate with one who harbours anger,
lest you learn his ways and ensnare your

2713
03:05:48,464 --> 03:05:49,364
soul.

2714
03:05:49,484 --> 03:05:54,804
Don’t you be one of those who strike
hands, of those who are collateral for debts.

2715
03:05:56,124 --> 03:06:01,264
If you don’t have means to pay, why should
he take away your bed from under you?

2716
03:06:02,204 --> 03:06:06,424
Don’t move the ancient boundary stone
which your fathers have set up.

2717
03:06:07,204 --> 03:06:09,564
Do you see a man skilled in his work?

2718
03:06:10,404 --> 03:06:11,344
He will serve kings.

2719
03:06:12,224 --> 03:06:21,924
He won’t

2720
03:06:21,964 --> 03:06:22,264
serve obscure men.

2721
03:06:22,304 --> 03:06:22,604
Proverbs, chapter twenty-three.

2722
03:06:22,644 --> 03:06:24,844
When you sit to eat with a ruler, consider
diligently what is before you; put a knife

2723
03:06:24,884 --> 03:06:27,804
to your throat if you are a man given to
appetite.

2724
03:06:28,524 --> 03:06:32,564
Don’t be desirous of his dainties, since
they are deceitful food.

2725
03:06:33,284 --> 03:06:35,144
Don’t weary yourself to be rich.

2726
03:06:36,164 --> 03:06:37,784
In your wisdom, show restraint.

2727
03:06:39,044 --> 03:06:41,864
Why do you set your eyes on that which is
not?

2728
03:06:42,824 --> 03:06:47,184
For it certainly sprouts wings like an
eagle and flies in the sky.

2729
03:06:47,944 --> 03:06:54,124
Don’t eat the food of him who has a
stingy eye, and don’t crave his delicacies, for as

2730
03:06:54,164 --> 03:06:56,784
he thinks about the cost, so he is.

2731
03:06:57,824 --> 03:06:58,724
“Eat and drink!”

2732
03:06:59,204 --> 03:07:02,444
he says to you, but his heart is not with
you.

2733
03:07:03,184 --> 03:07:07,824
You will vomit up the morsel which you
have eaten and waste your pleasant words.

2734
03:07:08,584 --> 03:07:13,904
Don’t speak in the ears of a fool, for he
will despise the wisdom of your words.

2735
03:07:15,004 --> 03:07:17,284
Don’t move the ancient boundary stone.

2736
03:07:18,064 --> 03:07:22,944
Don’t encroach on the fields of the
fatherless, for their Defender is strong.

2737
03:07:23,944 --> 03:07:25,944
He will plead their case against you.

2738
03:07:26,584 --> 03:07:31,104
Apply your heart to instruction, and your
ears to the words of knowledge.

2739
03:07:32,224 --> 03:07:34,404
Don’t withhold correction from a child.

2740
03:07:35,384 --> 03:07:38,464
If you punish him with the rod, he will
not die.

2741
03:07:39,424 --> 03:07:43,444
Punish him with the rod, and save his soul
from Sheol.

2742
03:07:43,484 --> 03:07:48,864
My son, if your heart is wise, then my
heart will be glad, even mine.

2743
03:07:49,564 --> 03:07:54,484
Yes, my heart will rejoice when your lips
speak what is right.

2744
03:07:54,847 --> 03:08:00,287
Don’t let your heart envy sinners, but
rather fear the LORD all day long.

2745
03:08:01,367 --> 03:08:06,327
Indeed surely there is a future hope, and
your hope will not be cut off.

2746
03:08:07,367 --> 03:08:12,387
Listen, my son, and be wise, and keep your
heart on the right path!

2747
03:08:13,067 --> 03:08:18,707
Don’t be amongst ones drinking too much
wine, or those who gorge themselves on meat;

2748
03:08:19,447 --> 03:08:25,347
for the drunkard and the glutton shall
become poor; and drowsiness clothes them in rags.

2749
03:08:25,687 --> 03:08:31,147
Listen to your father who gave you life,
and don’t despise your mother when she is old.

2750
03:08:31,707 --> 03:08:34,007
Buy the truth, and don’t sell it.

2751
03:08:34,807 --> 03:08:37,247
Get wisdom, discipline, and understanding.

2752
03:08:38,287 --> 03:08:40,807
The father of the righteous has great joy.

2753
03:08:41,487 --> 03:08:44,707
Whoever fathers a wise child delights in
him.

2754
03:08:45,617 --> 03:08:48,187
Let your father and your mother be glad!

2755
03:08:48,727 --> 03:08:50,327
Let her who bore you rejoice!

2756
03:08:51,527 --> 03:08:56,527
My son, give me your heart; and let your
eyes keep in my ways.

2757
03:08:57,687 --> 03:09:02,587
For a prostitute is a deep pit; and a
wayward wife is a narrow well.

2758
03:09:03,367 --> 03:09:09,787
Yes, she lies in wait like a robber, and
increases the unfaithful amongst men.

2759
03:09:09,827 --> 03:09:11,027
Who has woe?

2760
03:09:11,567 --> 03:09:12,467
Who has sorrow?

2761
03:09:13,287 --> 03:09:14,187
Who has strife?

2762
03:09:14,647 --> 03:09:15,547
Who has complaints?

2763
03:09:16,227 --> 03:09:17,447
Who has needless bruises?

2764
03:09:18,267 --> 03:09:19,607
Who has bloodshot eyes?

2765
03:09:20,267 --> 03:09:24,907
Those who stay long at the wine; those who
go to seek out mixed wine.

2766
03:09:25,847 --> 03:09:31,327
Don’t look at the wine when it is red,
when it sparkles in the cup, when it goes down

2767
03:09:31,367 --> 03:09:32,267
smoothly.

2768
03:09:32,787 --> 03:09:37,067
In the end, it bites like a snake, and
poisons like a viper.

2769
03:09:37,587 --> 03:09:42,647
Your eyes will see strange things, and
your mind will imagine confusing things.

2770
03:09:43,547 --> 03:09:50,267
Yes, you will be as he who lies down in the
middle of the sea, or as he who lies on top

2771
03:09:50,307 --> 03:09:54,087
of the rigging: “They hit me, and I was
not hurt!

2772
03:09:54,867 --> 03:09:57,027
They beat me, and I don’t feel it!

2773
03:09:57,747 --> 03:09:58,847
When will I wake up?

2774
03:09:59,507 --> 03:10:00,447
I can do it again.

2775
03:10:01,107 --> 03:10:02,167
I will look for more.”

2776
03:10:03,387 --> 03:10:06,147
Proverbs, chapter twenty-four.

2777
03:10:06,187 --> 03:10:12,747
Don’t be envious of evil men, neither desire
to be with them; for their hearts plot

2778
03:10:12,787 --> 03:10:15,587
violence and their lips talk about
mischief.

2779
03:10:16,907 --> 03:10:26,527
Through wisdom a house is built; by
understanding it

2780
03:10:26,567 --> 03:10:26,867
is established; by knowledge the rooms are
filled with all rare and beautiful treasure.

2781
03:10:26,907 --> 03:10:28,621
A wise man has great power.

2782
03:10:29,681 --> 03:10:36,321
A knowledgeable man increases strength, for by
wise guidance you wage your war, and

2783
03:10:36,361 --> 03:10:38,061
victory is in many advisors.

2784
03:10:39,301 --> 03:10:41,241
Wisdom is too high for a fool.

2785
03:10:42,201 --> 03:10:44,241
He doesn’t open his mouth in the gate.

2786
03:10:45,241 --> 03:10:48,561
One who plots to do evil will be called a
schemer.

2787
03:10:49,341 --> 03:10:51,181
The schemes of folly are sin.

2788
03:10:51,681 --> 03:10:53,821
The mocker is detested by men.

2789
03:10:54,621 --> 03:10:58,501
If you falter in the time of trouble, your
strength is small.

2790
03:10:59,441 --> 03:11:02,121
Rescue those who are being led away to
death!

2791
03:11:02,921 --> 03:11:06,221
Indeed, hold back those who are staggering
to the slaughter!

2792
03:11:06,721 --> 03:11:12,701
If you say, “Behold, we didn’t know this,”
doesn’t he who weighs the hearts consider

2793
03:11:12,741 --> 03:11:13,601
it?

2794
03:11:13,641 --> 03:11:16,541
He who keeps your soul, doesn’t he know
it?

2795
03:11:17,061 --> 03:11:20,601
Shall he not render to every man according
to his work?

2796
03:11:21,221 --> 03:11:27,921
My son, eat honey, for it is good,
the droppings of the honeycomb, which are sweet

2797
03:11:27,961 --> 03:11:32,181
to your taste; so you shall know wisdom to
be to your soul.

2798
03:11:32,821 --> 03:11:38,601
If you have found it, then there will be a
reward: Your hope will not be cut off.

2799
03:11:39,381 --> 03:11:43,681
Don’t lay in wait, wicked man, against the
habitation of the righteous.

2800
03:11:44,541 --> 03:11:51,021
Don’t destroy his resting place; for a
righteous man falls seven times and rises up

2801
03:11:51,061 --> 03:11:54,501
again, but the wicked are overthrown by
calamity.

2802
03:11:55,021 --> 03:11:57,041
Don’t rejoice when your enemy falls.

2803
03:11:57,961 --> 03:12:04,241
Don’t let your heart be glad when he is
overthrown, lest the LORD see it, and it displease

2804
03:12:04,281 --> 03:12:06,941
him, and he turn away his wrath from him.

2805
03:12:07,741 --> 03:12:13,801
Don’t fret yourself because of evildoers, neither
be envious of the wicked; for there

2806
03:12:13,841 --> 03:12:16,001
will be no reward to the evil man.

2807
03:12:16,701 --> 03:12:18,901
The lamp of the wicked will be snuffed
out.

2808
03:12:19,781 --> 03:12:22,761
My son, fear the LORD and the king.

2809
03:12:23,581 --> 03:12:28,261
Don’t join those who are rebellious, for
their calamity will rise suddenly.

2810
03:12:29,241 --> 03:12:32,141
Who knows what destruction may come from
them both?

2811
03:12:32,601 --> 03:12:38,161
These also are sayings of the wise: To
show partiality in judgement is not good.

2812
03:12:38,781 --> 03:12:44,861
He who says to the wicked, “You are
righteous,” peoples will curse him, and nations will

2813
03:12:44,901 --> 03:12:50,961
abhor him— but it will go well with
those who convict the guilty, and a rich blessing

2814
03:12:51,001 --> 03:12:52,081
will come on them.

2815
03:12:52,360 --> 03:12:55,500
An honest answer is like a kiss on the
lips.

2816
03:12:56,880 --> 03:13:00,540
Prepare your work outside, and get your
fields ready.

2817
03:13:01,480 --> 03:13:03,620
Afterwards, build your house.

2818
03:13:04,580 --> 03:13:07,440
Don’t be a witness against your neighbour
without cause.

2819
03:13:08,500 --> 03:13:10,020
Don’t deceive with your lips.

2820
03:13:10,980 --> 03:13:17,120
Don’t say, “I will do to him as he has
done to me; I will repay the man according to

2821
03:13:17,160 --> 03:13:18,060
his work.”

2822
03:13:18,380 --> 03:13:24,320
I went by the field of the sluggard,
by the vineyard of the man void of understanding.

2823
03:13:25,240 --> 03:13:28,460
Behold, it was all grown over with thorns.

2824
03:13:29,320 --> 03:13:34,160
Its surface was covered with nettles, and
its stone wall was broken down.

2825
03:13:34,660 --> 03:13:36,740
Then I saw, and considered well.

2826
03:13:36,780 --> 03:13:43,740
I saw, and received instruction: a little
sleep, a little slumber, a

2827
03:13:43,780 --> 03:13:49,660
little folding of the hands to sleep, so
your poverty will come as a robber and your

2828
03:13:49,700 --> 03:13:51,220
want as an armed man.

2829
03:13:52,380 --> 03:13:54,800
Proverbs, chapter twenty-five.

2830
03:13:54,840 --> 03:14:00,860
These also are proverbs of Solomon, which the
men of Hezekiah king of Judah copied out.

2831
03:14:01,540 --> 03:14:07,260
It is the glory of God to conceal a thing,
but the glory of kings is to search out a

2832
03:14:07,300 --> 03:14:08,200
matter.

2833
03:14:08,640 --> 03:14:14,960
As the heavens for height, and the earth
for depth, so the hearts of kings are unsearchable.

2834
03:14:15,320 --> 03:14:20,140
Take away the dross from the silver, and
material comes out for the refiner.

2835
03:14:20,840 --> 03:14:25,860
Take away the wicked from the king’s
presence, and his throne will be established in

2836
03:14:25,900 --> 03:14:26,800
righteousness.

2837
03:14:27,580 --> 03:14:33,340
Don’t exalt yourself in the presence of the
king, or claim a place amongst great men;

2838
03:14:33,960 --> 03:14:39,340
for it is better that it be said to
you, “Come up here,” than that you should be put

2839
03:14:39,380 --> 03:14:43,100
lower in the presence of the prince, whom
your eyes have seen.

2840
03:14:44,160 --> 03:14:47,020
Don’t be hasty in bringing charges to
court.

2841
03:14:47,960 --> 03:14:51,040
What will you do in the end when your
neighbour shames you?

2842
03:14:51,640 --> 03:14:57,500
Debate your case with your neighbour, and
don’t betray the confidence of another, lest

2843
03:14:57,540 --> 03:15:02,660
one who hears it put you to shame, and
your bad reputation never depart.

2844
03:15:03,720 --> 03:15:08,220
A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold
in settings of silver.

2845
03:15:08,720 --> 03:15:15,200
As an earring of gold, and an ornament of
fine gold, so is a wise reprover

2846
03:15:15,240 --> 03:15:16,400
to an obedient ear.

2847
03:15:16,824 --> 03:15:22,984
As the cold of snow in the time of
harvest, so is a faithful messenger to those who send

2848
03:15:23,024 --> 03:15:26,524
him; for he refreshes the soul of his
masters.

2849
03:15:27,664 --> 03:15:34,243
As clouds and wind without rain, so is he
who boasts of gifts deceptively.

2850
03:15:34,284 --> 03:15:36,544
By patience a ruler is persuaded.

2851
03:15:37,704 --> 03:15:39,584
A soft tongue breaks the bone.

2852
03:15:40,584 --> 03:15:41,784
Have you found honey?

2853
03:15:42,524 --> 03:15:47,964
Eat as much as is sufficient for you, lest
you eat too much, and vomit it.

2854
03:15:48,984 --> 03:15:54,524
Let your foot be seldom in your neighbour’s
house, lest he be weary of you, and hate

2855
03:15:54,564 --> 03:15:55,184
you.

2856
03:15:55,224 --> 03:16:01,663
A man who gives false testimony against his neighbour
is like a club, a sword, or a sharp

2857
03:16:01,704 --> 03:16:02,604
arrow.

2858
03:16:02,684 --> 03:16:08,784
Confidence in someone unfaithful in time of trouble
is like a bad tooth or a lame foot.

2859
03:16:09,984 --> 03:16:16,484
As one who takes away a garment in cold
weather, or vinegar on soda, so is one who

2860
03:16:16,524 --> 03:16:18,364
sings songs to a heavy heart.

2861
03:16:18,404 --> 03:16:21,864
If your enemy is hungry, give him food to
eat.

2862
03:16:22,904 --> 03:16:29,044
If he is thirsty, give him water to drink;
for you will heap coals of fire on his head,

2863
03:16:29,824 --> 03:16:31,404
and the LORD will reward you.

2864
03:16:32,424 --> 03:16:38,064
The north wind produces rain; so a
backbiting tongue brings an angry face.

2865
03:16:39,144 --> 03:16:44,104
It is better to dwell in the corner of
the housetop than to share a house with a contentious

2866
03:16:44,144 --> 03:16:44,764
woman.

2867
03:16:44,804 --> 03:16:50,684
Like cold water to a thirsty soul, so is
good news from a far country.

2868
03:16:51,584 --> 03:16:57,484
Like a muddied spring and a polluted well,
so is a righteous man who gives way before

2869
03:16:57,524 --> 03:16:58,424
the wicked.

2870
03:16:58,964 --> 03:17:04,644
It is not good to eat much honey, nor is
it honourable to seek one’s own honour.

2871
03:17:04,684 --> 03:17:11,404
Like a city that is broken down and without
walls is a man whose spirit is without restraint.

2872
03:17:12,724 --> 03:17:15,224
Proverbs, chapter twenty-six.

2873
03:17:15,264 --> 03:17:21,423
Like snow in summer, and as rain in
harvest, so honour is not fitting for a fool.

2874
03:17:21,464 --> 03:17:27,944
Like a fluttering sparrow, like a darting
swallow, so the undeserved curse doesn’t

2875
03:17:27,984 --> 03:17:28,884
come to rest.

2876
03:17:29,564 --> 03:17:35,564
A whip is for the horse, a bridle for the
donkey, and a rod for the back of fools!

2877
03:17:36,724 --> 03:17:41,684
Don’t answer a fool according to his
folly, lest you also be like him.

2878
03:17:42,204 --> 03:17:47,144
Answer a fool according to his folly, lest
he be wise in his own eyes.

2879
03:17:47,524 --> 03:17:53,304
One who sends a message by the hand of
a fool is cutting off feet and drinking violence.

2880
03:17:54,084 --> 03:17:59,744
Like the legs of the lame that hang loose,
so is a parable in the mouth of fools.

2881
03:18:00,884 --> 03:18:06,824
As one who binds a stone in a sling, so is
he who gives honour to a fool.

2882
03:18:07,344 --> 03:18:13,064
Like a thorn bush that goes into the hand
of a drunkard, so is a parable in the mouth

2883
03:18:13,104 --> 03:18:14,004
of fools.

2884
03:18:14,644 --> 03:18:21,144
As an archer who wounds all, so is he who
hires a fool or he who hires

2885
03:18:21,184 --> 03:18:22,544
those who pass by.

2886
03:18:22,944 --> 03:18:27,904
As a dog that returns to his vomit, so is
a fool who repeats his folly.

2887
03:18:29,344 --> 03:18:31,784
Do you see a man wise in his own eyes?

2888
03:18:32,364 --> 03:18:34,824
There is more hope for a fool than for
him.

2889
03:18:35,864 --> 03:18:38,984
The sluggard says, “There is a lion in the
road!

2890
03:18:39,784 --> 03:18:41,804
A fierce lion roams the streets!”

2891
03:18:42,564 --> 03:18:47,324
As the door turns on its hinges, so does
the sluggard on his bed.

2892
03:18:47,784 --> 03:18:49,844
The sluggard buries his hand in the dish.

2893
03:18:50,664 --> 03:18:53,144
He is too lazy to bring it back to his
mouth.

2894
03:18:53,864 --> 03:18:59,024
The sluggard is wiser in his own eyes than
seven men who answer with discretion.

2895
03:19:00,264 --> 03:19:06,764
Like one who grabs a dog’s ears is one who
passes by and meddles in a quarrel not his

2896
03:19:06,804 --> 03:19:07,364
own.

2897
03:19:07,404 --> 03:19:13,804
Like a madman who shoots torches, arrows, and
death, is the man who deceives his neighbour

2898
03:19:13,844 --> 03:19:16,344
and says, “Am I not joking?”

2899
03:19:17,024 --> 03:19:19,164
For lack of wood a fire goes out.

2900
03:19:20,004 --> 03:19:22,304
Without gossip, a quarrel dies down.

2901
03:19:23,404 --> 03:19:30,204
As coals are to hot embers, and wood to
fire, so is a contentious man to kindling strife.

2902
03:19:31,384 --> 03:19:37,224
The words of a whisperer are as dainty
morsels, they go down into the innermost parts.

2903
03:19:37,884 --> 03:19:44,284
Like silver dross on an earthen vessel are the
lips of a fervent one with an evil heart.

2904
03:19:45,504 --> 03:19:51,324
A malicious man disguises himself with his
lips, but he harbours evil in his heart.

2905
03:19:51,364 --> 03:19:57,404
When his speech is charming, don’t believe
him, for there are seven abominations in his

2906
03:19:57,444 --> 03:19:58,344
heart.

2907
03:19:58,464 --> 03:20:04,644
His malice may be concealed by deception, but
his wickedness will be exposed in the assembly.

2908
03:20:05,584 --> 03:20:08,384
Whoever digs a pit shall fall into it.

2909
03:20:09,024 --> 03:20:12,224
Whoever rolls a stone, it will come back
on him.

2910
03:20:13,464 --> 03:20:18,424
A lying tongue hates those it hurts; and a
flattering mouth works ruin.

2911
03:20:18,852 --> 03:20:22,412
Proverbs, chapter twenty-seven.

2912
03:20:22,452 --> 03:20:27,352
Don’t boast about tomorrow; for you don’t
know what a day may bring.

2913
03:20:28,352 --> 03:20:34,952
Let another man praise you, and not your
own mouth; a stranger, and not your own

2914
03:20:34,992 --> 03:20:35,772
lips.

2915
03:20:35,812 --> 03:20:42,692
A stone is heavy, and sand is a burden;
but a fool’s provocation is heavier than

2916
03:20:42,732 --> 03:20:43,632
both.

2917
03:20:43,892 --> 03:20:50,152
Wrath is cruel, and anger is overwhelming;
but who is able to stand before jealousy?

2918
03:20:51,232 --> 03:20:54,092
Better is open rebuke than hidden love.

2919
03:20:54,572 --> 03:20:59,852
The wounds of a friend are faithful,
although the kisses of an enemy are profuse.

2920
03:21:01,092 --> 03:21:07,612
A full soul loathes a honeycomb; but to a
hungry soul, every bitter thing is sweet.

2921
03:21:08,152 --> 03:21:13,332
As a bird that wanders from her nest, so
is a man who wanders from his home.

2922
03:21:14,372 --> 03:21:21,052
Perfume and incense bring joy to the heart;
so does earnest counsel from a man’s friend.

2923
03:21:22,092 --> 03:21:25,132
Don’t forsake your friend and your
father’s friend.

2924
03:21:25,612 --> 03:21:28,852
Don’t go to your brother’s house in the
day of your disaster.

2925
03:21:29,732 --> 03:21:33,352
A neighbour who is near is better than a
distant brother.

2926
03:21:34,452 --> 03:21:40,572
Be wise, my son, and bring joy to my
heart, then I can answer my tormentor.

2927
03:21:41,372 --> 03:21:47,932
A prudent man sees danger and takes
refuge; but the simple pass on, and suffer

2928
03:21:47,972 --> 03:21:48,812
for it.

2929
03:21:48,852 --> 03:21:52,152
Take his garment when he puts up
collateral for a stranger.

2930
03:21:53,132 --> 03:21:54,632
Hold it for a wayward woman!

2931
03:21:55,512 --> 03:22:01,112
He who blesses his neighbour with a loud
voice early in the morning, it will be taken

2932
03:22:01,152 --> 03:22:02,412
as a curse by him.

2933
03:22:03,152 --> 03:22:09,672
A continual dropping on a rainy day and a
contentious wife are alike: restraining

2934
03:22:09,712 --> 03:22:14,892
her is like restraining the wind, or like
grasping oil in his right hand.

2935
03:22:15,592 --> 03:22:20,372
Iron sharpens iron; so a man sharpens his
friend’s countenance.

2936
03:22:21,312 --> 03:22:24,472
Whoever tends the fig tree shall eat its
fruit.

2937
03:22:25,552 --> 03:22:28,932
He who looks after his master shall be
honoured.

2938
03:22:28,972 --> 03:22:33,832
Like water reflects a face, so a man’s
heart reflects the man.

2939
03:22:34,692 --> 03:22:40,732
Sheol and Abaddon are never satisfied; and
a man’s eyes are never satisfied.

2940
03:22:41,992 --> 03:22:48,612
The crucible is for silver, and the furnace
for gold; but man is refined by his praise.

2941
03:22:49,173 --> 03:22:55,653
Though you grind a fool in a mortar
with a pestle along with grain, yet his foolishness

2942
03:22:55,693 --> 03:22:57,593
will not be removed from him.

2943
03:22:58,333 --> 03:23:04,733
Know well the state of your flocks, and
pay attention to your herds, for riches are not

2944
03:23:04,773 --> 03:23:08,613
forever, nor does the crown endure to all
generations.

2945
03:23:09,793 --> 03:23:15,553
The hay is removed, and the new growth
appears, the grasses of the hills are gathered

2946
03:23:15,593 --> 03:23:16,493
in.

2947
03:23:16,693 --> 03:23:21,213
The lambs are for your clothing, and the
goats are the price of a field.

2948
03:23:21,693 --> 03:23:27,033
There will be plenty of goats’ milk for
your food, for your family’s food, and for the

2949
03:23:27,073 --> 03:23:28,733
nourishment of your servant girls.

2950
03:23:29,513 --> 03:23:32,693
Proverbs, chapter twenty-eight.

2951
03:23:32,733 --> 03:23:37,973
The wicked flee when no one pursues; but
the righteous are as bold as a lion.

2952
03:23:39,073 --> 03:23:45,133
In rebellion, a land has many rulers, but
order is maintained by a man of understanding

2953
03:23:45,173 --> 03:23:46,013
and knowledge.

2954
03:23:46,053 --> 03:23:51,833
A needy man who oppresses the poor is like
a driving rain which leaves no crops.

2955
03:23:52,633 --> 03:23:58,133
Those who forsake the law praise the wicked;
but those who keep the law contend with

2956
03:23:58,173 --> 03:23:59,073
them.

2957
03:23:59,353 --> 03:24:05,113
Evil men don’t understand justice; but those
who seek the LORD understand it fully.

2958
03:24:05,613 --> 03:24:11,713
Better is the poor who walks in his integrity
than he who is perverse in his ways, and

2959
03:24:11,753 --> 03:24:12,653
he is rich.

2960
03:24:12,873 --> 03:24:19,333
Whoever keeps the law is a wise son; but
he who is a companion of gluttons shames his

2961
03:24:19,373 --> 03:24:20,273
father.

2962
03:24:20,873 --> 03:24:26,453
He who increases his wealth by excessive interest
gathers it for one who has pity on

2963
03:24:26,493 --> 03:24:27,393
the poor.

2964
03:24:27,933 --> 03:24:33,353
He who turns away his ear from hearing the
law, even his prayer is an abomination.

2965
03:24:34,253 --> 03:24:40,273
Whoever causes the upright to go astray in an
evil way, he will fall into his own trap;

2966
03:24:40,913 --> 03:24:43,113
but the blameless will inherit good.

2967
03:24:44,213 --> 03:24:50,053
The rich man is wise in his own
eyes; but the poor who has understanding sees through

2968
03:24:50,093 --> 03:24:50,993
him.

2969
03:24:51,333 --> 03:24:57,393
When the righteous triumph, there is great
glory; but when the wicked rise, men hide

2970
03:24:57,433 --> 03:24:58,333
themselves.

2971
03:24:58,873 --> 03:25:10,073
He who conceals his sins doesn’t prosper,
but whoever confesses

2972
03:25:10,113 --> 03:25:10,413
and renounces them finds mercy.

2973
03:25:10,453 --> 03:25:12,773
Blessed is the man who always fears; but
one who hardens his heart falls into trouble.

2974
03:25:13,138 --> 03:25:19,478
As a roaring lion or a charging bear, so
is a wicked ruler over helpless people.

2975
03:25:20,738 --> 03:25:23,778
A tyrannical ruler lacks judgement.

2976
03:25:23,818 --> 03:25:27,238
One who hates ill-gotten gain will have
long days.

2977
03:25:28,178 --> 03:25:33,458
A man who is tormented by blood guilt will
be a fugitive until death.

2978
03:25:34,478 --> 03:25:35,598
No one will support him.

2979
03:25:36,358 --> 03:25:42,458
Whoever walks blamelessly is kept safe; but
one with perverse ways will fall suddenly.

2980
03:25:43,538 --> 03:25:50,158
One who works his land will have an
abundance of food; but one who chases fantasies will

2981
03:25:50,198 --> 03:25:51,598
have his fill of poverty.

2982
03:25:52,078 --> 03:25:58,958
A faithful man is rich with blessings; but one
who is eager to be rich will not go unpunished.

2983
03:25:59,558 --> 03:26:05,138
To show partiality is not good, yet a man
will do wrong for a piece of bread.

2984
03:26:06,158 --> 03:26:11,378
A stingy man hurries after riches, and
doesn’t know that poverty waits for him.

2985
03:26:12,058 --> 03:26:17,818
One who rebukes a man will afterward find
more favour than one who flatters with the

2986
03:26:17,858 --> 03:26:18,758
tongue.

2987
03:26:18,878 --> 03:26:25,338
Whoever robs his father or his mother and
says, “It’s not wrong,” is a partner with a

2988
03:26:25,378 --> 03:26:26,278
destroyer.

2989
03:26:27,138 --> 03:26:32,718
One who is greedy stirs up strife; but one
who trusts in the LORD will prosper.

2990
03:26:33,378 --> 03:26:39,438
One who trusts in himself is a fool; but
one who walks in wisdom is kept safe.

2991
03:26:39,918 --> 03:26:46,718
One who gives to the poor has no lack;
but one who closes his eyes will have many curses.

2992
03:26:47,918 --> 03:26:53,838
When the wicked rise, men hide themselves;
but when they perish, the righteous thrive.

2993
03:26:54,418 --> 03:26:57,158
Proverbs, chapter twenty-nine.

2994
03:26:57,198 --> 03:27:03,958
He who is often rebuked and stiffens his
neck will be destroyed suddenly, with no remedy.

2995
03:27:04,388 --> 03:27:10,918
When the righteous thrive, the people rejoice;
but when the wicked rule, the people groan.

2996
03:27:11,658 --> 03:27:17,978
Whoever loves wisdom brings joy to his
father; but a companion of prostitutes squanders

2997
03:27:18,018 --> 03:27:18,918
his wealth.

2998
03:27:19,118 --> 03:27:25,018
The king by justice makes the land stable,
but he who takes bribes tears it down.

2999
03:27:25,758 --> 03:27:29,258
A man who flatters his neighbour spreads a
net for his feet.

3000
03:27:30,458 --> 03:27:35,618
An evil man is snared by his sin, but the
righteous can sing and be glad.

3001
03:27:36,898 --> 03:27:39,278
The righteous care about justice for the
poor.

3002
03:27:40,358 --> 03:27:42,378
The wicked aren’t concerned about
knowledge.

3003
03:27:43,455 --> 03:27:47,175
Mockers stir up a city, but wise men turn
away anger.

3004
03:27:48,355 --> 03:27:54,835
If a wise man goes to court with a foolish
man, the fool rages or scoffs, and

3005
03:27:54,875 --> 03:27:55,775
there is no peace.

3006
03:27:56,775 --> 03:28:01,915
The bloodthirsty hate a man of integrity;
and they seek the life of the upright.

3007
03:28:02,755 --> 03:28:08,155
A fool vents all of his anger, but a wise
man brings himself under control.

3008
03:28:08,895 --> 03:28:13,455
If a ruler listens to lies, all of his
officials are wicked.

3009
03:28:14,695 --> 03:28:20,375
The poor man and the oppressor have this
in common: The LORD gives sight to the eyes

3010
03:28:20,415 --> 03:28:21,315
of both.

3011
03:28:21,695 --> 03:28:26,855
The king who fairly judges the poor, his
throne shall be established forever.

3012
03:28:28,075 --> 03:28:34,775
The rod of correction gives wisdom, but a
child left to himself causes shame to his mother.

3013
03:28:35,635 --> 03:28:41,175
When the wicked increase, sin increases;
but the righteous will see their downfall.

3014
03:28:41,635 --> 03:28:47,895
Correct your son, and he will give you
peace; yes, he will bring delight to your soul.

3015
03:28:48,835 --> 03:28:55,255
Where there is no revelation, the people cast
off restraint; but one who keeps the law

3016
03:28:55,295 --> 03:28:56,195
is blessed.

3017
03:28:57,115 --> 03:28:59,575
A servant can’t be corrected by words.

3018
03:29:00,335 --> 03:29:03,435
Though he understands, yet he will not
respond.

3019
03:29:04,735 --> 03:29:07,235
Do you see a man who is hasty in his
words?

3020
03:29:07,935 --> 03:29:10,415
There is more hope for a fool than for
him.

3021
03:29:11,515 --> 03:29:16,535
He who pampers his servant from youth will
have him become a son in the end.

3022
03:29:17,515 --> 03:29:22,255
An angry man stirs up strife, and a
wrathful man abounds in sin.

3023
03:29:23,075 --> 03:29:28,975
A man’s pride brings him low, but one of
lowly spirit gains honour.

3024
03:29:29,015 --> 03:29:32,855
Whoever is an accomplice of a thief is an
enemy of his own soul.

3025
03:29:33,855 --> 03:29:36,475
He takes an oath, but dares not testify.

3026
03:29:38,015 --> 03:29:43,915
The fear of man proves to be a snare, but
whoever puts his trust in the LORD is kept

3027
03:29:43,955 --> 03:29:44,855
safe.

3028
03:29:45,475 --> 03:29:50,375
Many seek the ruler’s favour, but a man’s
justice comes from the LORD.

3029
03:29:51,135 --> 03:29:57,055
A dishonest man detests the righteous, and
the upright in their ways detest the wicked.

3030
03:29:58,235 --> 03:30:01,395
Proverbs, chapter thirty.

3031
03:30:01,435 --> 03:30:08,175
The words of Agur the son of Jakeh,
the revelation: the man says to Ithiel, to Ithiel

3032
03:30:08,215 --> 03:30:13,815
and Ucal: “Surely I am the most ignorant
man, and don’t have a man’s understanding.

3033
03:30:14,473 --> 03:30:19,453
I have not learnt wisdom, neither do I
have the knowledge of the Holy One.

3034
03:30:19,753 --> 03:30:23,333
Who has ascended up into heaven, and
descended?

3035
03:30:24,073 --> 03:30:26,593
Who has gathered the wind in his fists?

3036
03:30:27,753 --> 03:30:29,853
Who has bound the waters in his garment?

3037
03:30:30,833 --> 03:30:33,233
Who has established all the ends of the
earth?

3038
03:30:33,893 --> 03:30:37,753
What is his name, and what is his son’s
name, if you know?

3039
03:30:38,813 --> 03:30:40,673
“Every word of God is flawless.

3040
03:30:41,413 --> 03:30:44,653
He is a shield to those who take refuge in
him.

3041
03:30:45,653 --> 03:30:51,033
Don’t you add to his words, lest he
reprove you, and you be found a liar.

3042
03:30:52,153 --> 03:30:54,033
“Two things I have asked of you.

3043
03:30:54,853 --> 03:30:56,513
Don’t deny me before I die.

3044
03:30:57,413 --> 03:30:59,613
Remove far from me falsehood and lies.

3045
03:31:00,793 --> 03:31:02,513
Give me neither poverty nor riches.

3046
03:31:03,613 --> 03:31:10,693
Feed me with the food that is needful for
me, lest I be full, deny you, and say, ‘Who

3047
03:31:10,733 --> 03:31:11,633
is the LORD?’

3048
03:31:12,273 --> 03:31:17,393
or lest I be poor, and steal, and so
dishonour the name of my God.

3049
03:31:18,093 --> 03:31:23,773
“Don’t slander a servant to his master,
lest he curse you, and you be held guilty.

3050
03:31:24,993 --> 03:31:29,673
There is a generation that curses their
father, and doesn’t bless their mother.

3051
03:31:30,273 --> 03:31:36,313
There is a generation that is pure in their
own eyes, yet are not washed from their filthiness.

3052
03:31:36,933 --> 03:31:40,673
There is a generation, oh how lofty are
their eyes!

3053
03:31:41,473 --> 03:31:42,993
Their eyelids are lifted up.

3054
03:31:43,773 --> 03:31:50,033
There is a generation whose teeth are like
swords, and their jaws like knives, to devour

3055
03:31:50,073 --> 03:31:53,653
the poor from the earth, and the needy
from amongst men.

3056
03:31:54,553 --> 03:31:57,933
“The leech has two daughters: ‘Give,
give.’

3057
03:31:58,633 --> 03:32:05,513
“There are three things that are never
satisfied; four that don’t say, ‘Enough!’: Sheol,

3058
03:32:06,233 --> 03:32:12,353
the barren womb, the earth that is not
satisfied with water, and the fire that doesn’t

3059
03:32:12,393 --> 03:32:13,373
say, ‘Enough!’

3060
03:32:14,073 --> 03:32:20,553
“The eye that mocks at his father, and
scorns obedience to his mother, the ravens of

3061
03:32:20,593 --> 03:32:24,453
the valley shall pick it out, the young
eagles shall eat it.

3062
03:32:24,493 --> 03:32:30,313
“There are three things which are too
amazing for me, four which I don’t understand:

3063
03:32:31,733 --> 03:32:37,793
The way of an eagle in the air, the way of
a serpent on a rock, the way of a ship in

3064
03:32:37,833 --> 03:32:41,293
the middle of the sea, and the way of a
man with a maiden.

3065
03:32:41,815 --> 03:32:49,175
“So is the way of an adulterous woman: She
eats and wipes her mouth, and says, ‘I

3066
03:32:49,215 --> 03:32:50,275
have done nothing wrong.’

3067
03:32:50,315 --> 03:32:57,315
“For three things the earth trembles, and
under four, it can’t bear up: For

3068
03:32:57,355 --> 03:33:03,955
a servant when he is king, a fool when he
is filled with food, for an unloved woman

3069
03:33:03,995 --> 03:33:08,255
when she is married, and a servant who is
heir to her mistress.

3070
03:33:09,135 --> 03:33:14,075
“There are four things which are little on
the earth, but they are exceedingly wise:

3071
03:33:15,115 --> 03:33:19,955
The ants are not a strong people, yet they
provide their food in the summer.

3072
03:33:21,015 --> 03:33:26,175
The hyraxes are but a feeble folk, yet
make they their houses in the rocks.

3073
03:33:27,315 --> 03:33:30,855
The locusts have no king, yet they advance
in ranks.

3074
03:33:31,735 --> 03:33:35,915
You can catch a lizard with your hands,
yet it is in kings’ palaces.

3075
03:33:36,835 --> 03:33:42,675
“There are three things which are stately in
their march, four which are stately in going:

3076
03:33:43,675 --> 03:33:50,215
The lion, which is mightiest amongst animals,
and doesn’t turn away for any; the greyhound;

3077
03:33:50,895 --> 03:33:54,815
the male goat; and the king against whom
there is no rising up.

3078
03:33:55,855 --> 03:34:01,415
“If you have done foolishly in lifting up
yourself, or if you have thought evil, put

3079
03:34:01,455 --> 03:34:03,075
your hand over your mouth.

3080
03:34:04,035 --> 03:34:09,375
For as the churning of milk produces butter,
and the wringing of the nose produces blood,

3081
03:34:09,875 --> 03:34:12,495
so the forcing of wrath produces strife.”

3082
03:34:13,295 --> 03:34:16,635
Proverbs, chapter thirty-one.

3083
03:34:16,675 --> 03:34:23,015
The words of King Lemuel—the revelation
which his mother taught him: “Oh, my son!

3084
03:34:23,055 --> 03:34:25,035
Oh, son of my womb!

3085
03:34:25,075 --> 03:34:26,935
Oh, son of my vows!

3086
03:34:27,775 --> 03:34:32,655
Don’t give your strength to women, nor
your ways to that which destroys kings.

3087
03:34:33,475 --> 03:34:39,935
It is not for kings, Lemuel, it is not for
kings to drink wine, nor for princes to

3088
03:34:39,975 --> 03:34:41,915
say, ‘Where is strong drink?’

3089
03:34:42,575 --> 03:34:48,795
lest they drink, and forget the law, and
pervert the justice due to anyone who is afflicted.

3090
03:34:49,355 --> 03:34:54,595
Give strong drink to him who is ready to
perish, and wine to the bitter in soul.

3091
03:34:55,355 --> 03:35:00,855
Let him drink, and forget his poverty, and
remember his misery no more.

3092
03:35:01,855 --> 03:35:07,015
Open your mouth for the mute, in the cause
of all who are left desolate.

3093
03:35:07,463 --> 03:35:13,183
Open your mouth, judge righteously, and
serve justice to the poor and needy.”

3094
03:35:14,443 --> 03:35:16,383
Who can find a worthy woman?

3095
03:35:17,283 --> 03:35:19,443
For her value is far above rubies.

3096
03:35:20,323 --> 03:35:22,543
The heart of her husband trusts in her.

3097
03:35:23,503 --> 03:35:25,183
He shall have no lack of gain.

3098
03:35:26,183 --> 03:35:30,363
She does him good, and not harm, all the
days of her life.

3099
03:35:30,403 --> 03:35:35,063
She seeks wool and flax, and works eagerly
with her hands.

3100
03:35:35,863 --> 03:35:37,723
She is like the merchant ships.

3101
03:35:38,523 --> 03:35:40,103
She brings her bread from afar.

3102
03:35:41,163 --> 03:35:47,603
She rises also while it is yet night,
gives food to her household, and portions for her

3103
03:35:47,643 --> 03:35:48,543
servant girls.

3104
03:35:49,283 --> 03:35:51,803
She considers a field, and buys it.

3105
03:35:52,443 --> 03:35:55,283
With the fruit of her hands, she plants a
vineyard.

3106
03:35:56,023 --> 03:35:59,723
She arms her waist with strength, and
makes her arms strong.

3107
03:36:00,683 --> 03:36:03,203
She perceives that her merchandise is
profitable.

3108
03:36:04,323 --> 03:36:06,143
Her lamp doesn’t go out by night.

3109
03:36:06,963 --> 03:36:10,943
She lays her hands to the distaff, and her
hands hold the spindle.

3110
03:36:11,803 --> 03:36:17,123
She opens her arms to the poor; yes, she
extends her hands to the needy.

3111
03:36:18,143 --> 03:36:23,943
She is not afraid of the snow for
her household, for all her household are clothed with

3112
03:36:23,983 --> 03:36:24,883
scarlet.

3113
03:36:25,443 --> 03:36:28,283
She makes for herself carpets of tapestry.

3114
03:36:29,023 --> 03:36:31,243
Her clothing is fine linen and purple.

3115
03:36:31,943 --> 03:36:37,063
Her husband is respected in the gates, when
he sits amongst the elders of the land.

3116
03:36:38,083 --> 03:36:43,323
She makes linen garments and sells them,
and delivers sashes to the merchant.

3117
03:36:44,303 --> 03:36:46,503
Strength and dignity are her clothing.

3118
03:36:47,483 --> 03:36:49,163
She laughs at the time to come.

3119
03:36:49,923 --> 03:36:51,743
She opens her mouth with wisdom.

3120
03:36:52,423 --> 03:36:54,323
Kind instruction is on her tongue.

3121
03:36:55,303 --> 03:37:00,383
She looks well to the ways of her
household, and doesn’t eat the bread of idleness.

3122
03:37:01,343 --> 03:37:04,163
Her children rise up and call her blessed.

3123
03:37:04,203 --> 03:37:10,943
Her husband also praises her: “Many women
do noble things, but

3124
03:37:10,983 --> 03:37:12,143
you excel them all.”

3125
03:37:12,583 --> 03:37:18,983
Charm is deceitful, and beauty is vain; but
a woman who fears the Lord, she shall be

3126
03:37:19,023 --> 03:37:19,923
praised.

3127
03:37:20,463 --> 03:37:22,143
Give her of the fruit of her hands!

3128
03:37:23,123 --> 03:37:24,883
Let her works praise her in the gates!

